E["npc:apothecary-johaan"] = {t="npc",n="Apothecary Johaan",z="tirisfal",s="Apothecary Johaan is an alchemist and researcher of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Brill. Tasked by his order and Lady Sylvanas, he conducts lethal experiments on local flora and fauna to develop the Forsaken's new plague.",h="Apothecary Johaan is an alchemist and researcher of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Brill.",sec={{t="A Servant of the Society",b="Working openly out of the Forsaken settlement of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, Apothecary Johaan represents the scientific ambitions of the newly formed Royal Apothecary Society. Like his colleagues across Lordaeron, Johaan operates under direct orders to craft biological and alchemical weapons capable of securing the Forsaken's fragile future against the living and the Scourge alike.",sp=0},{t="Brewing the New Plague",b="Johaan coordinates early field trials for what the Society calls the 'New Plague'. Using raw materials harvested from Tirisfal's corrupted wildlife and agricultural blights—such as gloom weed and the tainted soil of nearby farmsteads—he tests toxin mixtures and evaluates their potency on living subjects before dispatching results down south to Silverpine Forest.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Apothecary Johaan is an alchemical researcher stationed in Brill. He belongs to the Royal Apothecary Society and directs young Forsaken champions to gather vile reagents across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"apothecary johaan","who is johaan","johaan brill"}},{q="Where can I find Apothecary Johaan?",a="He can be found standing outside near the gallows and alchemical apparatus in the town of Brill, just north of the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"johaan location","where is johaan","find johaan"}},{q="What is Johaan working on?",a="Johaan is formulating and refining early strains of the New Plague, testing biological agents and venomous extracts from Tirisfal's blighted fields and beasts.",al={"johaan experiments","what does johaan do","johaan plague"}},{q="What does he do with the plague samples?",a="Once test mixtures are concocted and their lethality assessed, Johaan packages the samples and sends couriers to deliver them to allied apothecaries stationed in Silverpine Forest.",al={"delivery to silverpine","where do plague samples go"}},{q="What organization does Johaan belong to?",a="He is an active member of the Royal Apothecary Society, the alchemical guild serving Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken in the Undercity.",al={"johaan faction","who does johaan work for"}},{q="Why is he interested in the local farms?",a="Human farms like the Solliden Farmstead and the nearby pumpkin patches contain fungal growths and blighted crops that provide key chemical precursors for his experimental toxins.",al={"fields of grief johaan","why send me to farms"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Johaan's research is central to the Forsaken cause, developing the very weapons needed to carve out a permanent homeland free of Scourge and living threats.",["faction:Horde"]="While orcs and tauren might balk at alchemical blights, Johaan's deadly concoctions serve the strategic security of the Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"apothecary","brill","gloom weed","johaan","plague","royal apothecary society","silverpine","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:brill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","quest:367","quest:365","quest:445","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","zone:silverpine"},src={"Apothecary Johaan"}}
E["npc:aramis-hammerhand"] = {t="npc",n="Aramis Hammerhand",z="tirisfal",s="Aramis Hammerhand is an undead holy warrior situated within the desecrated chapel of Deathknell. As a Forsaken paladin trainer, he instructs newly risen dead who seek to reclaim their bond with the Holy Light. Walking this path in undeath requires immense discipline, as wielding such radiant energy inflicts agonizing pain upon their decayed flesh.",h="Aramis Hammerhand is an undead holy warrior situated within the desecrated chapel of Deathknell.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Deathknell",b="Standing within the somber walls of Deathknell's chapel, Aramis Hammerhand represents an anomaly among the recently awakened Forsaken. In life, many citizens of Lordaeron answered the call of the Silver Hand, only to perish when the Scourge swept across the north. Aramis survived the fall only to be raised into undeath, yet he chose not to abandon the martial and spiritual teachings of his former existence. Now, he offers guidance to others who refuse to surrender their devotion.",sp=0},{t="The Agony of the Holy Light",b="For an undead being, channeling the Holy Light is an ordeal of supreme willpower. The power burns necrotic flesh and reawakens long-dead nerves to excruciating pain. Aramis instructs his initiates that holding to this faith requires enduring continual torment. Through tasks like 'A Difficult Path' and 'Rediscovering the Light', he demands that young paladins confront the physical and spiritual costs of wielding a force inherently opposed to their present nature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Aramis Hammerhand?",a="Aramis Hammerhand is a Forsaken paladin trainer located inside the chapel at Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. He assists newly risen undead who wish to pursue the path of holy combat.",al={"aramis lore","who is hammerhand","deathknell paladin trainer"}},{q="Can the Forsaken actually wield the Holy Light?",a="Yes, through sheer willpower and conviction, Forsaken can call upon the Holy Light. However, doing so causes immense physical agony, as the radiant energy burns and scours their rotting flesh while healing or bolstering them.",al={"can undead be paladins","how do undead use light","forsaken light"}},{q="Where can I find Aramis Hammerhand?",a="He can be found standing inside the chapel of Deathknell, the introductory settlement for the Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is aramis","hammerhand location","paladin trainer deathknell"}},{q="What quests does Aramis Hammerhand offer?",a="Aramis offers several class-specific quests for newly risen paladins, including 'A Difficult Path', 'Rediscovering the Light', 'A Light in the Darkness', 'Coming to Terms', and 'Continue Your Training'.",al={"aramis quests","deathknell paladin quests"}},{q="Why is a paladin trainer working for the Forsaken?",a="Before the plague, Lordaeron was the cradle of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Many of the newly liberated Forsaken remember their oaths and refuse to abandon their sacred calling, regardless of their undead state.",al={"why are there forsaken paladins","forsaken silver hand"}},{q="Does using the Light heal the undead in the normal way?",a="While the Light can mend their bodies and grant them martial strength, the process is excruciating. It reignites their sensory nervous systems, forcing them to feel the rot of their own bodies.",al={"does light hurt undead","light healing undead lore"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For Forsaken paladins, Aramis is the first mentor they meet, guiding them through the agony and spiritual discipline required to wield the Holy Light in an undead vessel.",["race:Undead"]="Aramis demonstrates that rising into undeath does not require abandoning Lordaeron's proud heritage of holy warfare, even if it comes with immense personal suffering."},kw={"aramis","chapel","deathknell","forsaken","hammerhand","light","paladin","tirisfal","trainer"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:light","quest:98601","quest:90902","quest:98389","quest:91208"},src={"Aramis Hammerhand"}}
E["npc:captured-mountaineer"] = {t="npc",n="Captured Mountaineer",z="tirisfal",s="The Captured Mountaineer is an Ironforge dwarf held prisoner in the basement of the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. Bound and guarded by the Forsaken, he serves as an unwilling subject for the Royal Apothecary Society's grim experiments.",h="The Captured Mountaineer is an Ironforge dwarf held prisoner in the basement of the Gallows' End Tavern in...",sec={{t="A Prisoner in the Cellar",b="Tucked away beneath the floorboards of the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, this Ironforge Mountaineer sits captive far from the safety of Khaz Modan. While patrons drink above, the Royal Apothecary Society puts him to work as an unwitting test subject for their concoctions. Apothecary Johaan and his peers test the lethal potency of their developing plague against living Alliance physiology, using the prisoner to gauge how well their toxins bring a swift and agonizing end to the living.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is the Captured Mountaineer?",a="He is an Alliance scout from Ironforge who fell into Forsaken hands. He is currently imprisoned in the basement of the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill.",al={"who is this dwarf","dwarf in brill tavern","captive dwarf"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken keeping him alive in the basement?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society uses him as a live test subject. Rather than executing him outright, apothecaries like Johaan administer experimental mixtures to study their effectiveness against living dwarven biology.",al={"why keep him alive","why is he in the tavern","what are they doing to the dwarf"}},{q="What happens to him during the tests?",a="As part of the research into developing a new plague, he is forced to ingest concoctions brewed by the apothecaries. The lethal mixture quickly proves effective, terminating the prisoner as proof of the toxin's progress.",al={"does the dwarf die","what happens in a new plague"},sp=1},{q="Who else interacts with him down here?",a="Aside from the apothecaries conducting experiments, locals like Renee Lauer have spent time down in the cellar, sharing stories with the captive dwarf while he remains bound.",al={"who talks to the dwarf","renee lauer"}}},ang={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a proud brother of Ironforge caged beneath a Forsaken tavern and subjected to horrific alchemical trials is a bitter reminder of the Forsaken's ruthless hostility toward the living.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, live Alliance captives are vital resources for the Royal Apothecary Society's goal of perfecting a plague capable of wiping out Scourge and living foes alike."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill basement","captured mountaineer","dwarf prisoner","gallows end tavern","ironforge scout"},rel={"quest:367","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Captured Mountaineer"}}
E["npc:captured-scarlet-zealot"] = {t="npc",n="Captured Scarlet Zealot",z="tirisfal",s="The Captured Scarlet Zealot is a crusader prisoner held captive in the basement of Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. Watched over by Forsaken apothecaries and townsfolk, he serves as a living test subject for the Royal Apothecary Society's developing concoctions.",h="The Captured Scarlet Zealot is a crusader prisoner held captive in the basement of Gallows' End Tavern in...",sec={{t="A Bitter Captive in Brill",b="Confined beneath Gallows' End Tavern, this member of the Scarlet Crusade embodies the unyielding fanaticism of his order. Even in chains, surrounded by the undead he views as an abomination, he offers no remorse and venomously denounces anyone who speaks to him—such as Renee Lauer, whom he reviles as a traitor. For the Forsaken, capturing a living zealot is not an act of mercy; it provides valuable human test material to evaluate the lethality of experimental plagues and toxins under development by Apothecary Johaan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a Scarlet Zealot kept alive in Brill?",a="The Forsaken keep him captive in the tavern basement as a living subject for testing new poisons and chemical agents developed by the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"why is scarlet zealot captured","why keep zealot alive","who is the zealot in brill cellar"}},{q="Where can I find this captive?",a="He is imprisoned in the damp cellar beneath Gallows' End Tavern, situated in the center of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is captured scarlet zealot","scarlet zealot location","zealot in brill"}},{q="How does he react to the Forsaken around him?",a="He remains fanatically defiant despite his confinement, lashing out with insults and labeling locals like Renee Lauer traitors to humanity and the Light.",al={"what does the zealot say","zealot dialogue","renee lauer and zealot"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken of Brill, this fanatic in chains represents the relentless crusaders seeking their extermination, serving a far more useful role as an apothecary's guinea pig.",["class:Priest"]="Scarlet zealots claim exclusive dominion over the Holy Light, yet this prisoner's unwavering zeal offers no defense against the grim reality of Forsaken captivity."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","captured scarlet zealot","gallows' end tavern","prisoner","renee lauer","scarlet crusade","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","quest:365"},src={"Captured Scarlet Zealot"}}
E["npc:coleman-farthing"] = {t="npc",n="Coleman Farthing",z="tirisfal",s="Coleman Farthing is a bitter Forsaken survivor residing in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. In life, he worked for the wealthy Agamand dynasty at their extensive flour mills in northern Tirisfal. Convinced to stay and defend the estate against the Scourge, he died alongside his fellow laborers, and now dedicates his undeath to exacting vengeance on his former masters.",h="Coleman Farthing is a bitter Forsaken survivor residing in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill.",sec={{t="A Bitter Servant",b="Before the Third War, Coleman Farthing earned an honest living as a laborer at the Agamand Mills, the largest milling and agricultural operation in Tirisfal Glades. When the Scourge poured across Lordaeron, the aristocratic Agamand family refused to flee their valuable lands. Instead, they urged their household and laborers to take up arms alongside them, promising they could hold the farmsteads against the undead horde. Coleman and his fellow workers stayed, believing their masters—a decision that cost every last one of them their lives.",sp=0},{t="Vengeance from the Grave",b="Raised into undeath only to break free under the banner of the Forsaken, Coleman harbors a burning hatred for the Agamands. Rather than blaming only the Scourge, he blames the sheer hubris and greed of his employers for tricking their staff into an impossible last stand. Now loitering in Brill's tavern, Coleman enlists Horde champions to march into the blighted mills, cut down the risen Agamand kin, and shatter the heirloom relics housed within their family crypt so that their legacy is utterly erased.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Coleman Farthing be found?",a="Coleman Farthing spends his days inside the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, located in central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"coleman farthing location","where is coleman farthing","coleman farthing brill"}},{q="Why does Coleman hate the Agamand family so much?",a="When the Scourge invaded Lordaeron, the Agamand patriarchs convinced their workers—including Coleman—to stay and fight to protect the mills rather than flee to safety. The entire workforce was slaughtered as a result. Coleman views their rallying cry as arrogant manipulation that led him directly to his death.",al={"why does coleman hate agamands","coleman farthing motivation","agamand mills grudge"}},{q="What happened to the Agamand Mills?",a="The sprawling estate was completely overrun by the Scourge. Its wind-driven mills stand ruined and haunted, while the Agamand family members and their slaughtered workers wander the blighted fields as mindlessly hostile undead under the Lich King's sway.",al={"what happened to agamand mills","agamand mills lore","who owns agamand mills"}},{q="What tasks does Coleman give to adventurers?",a="Coleman directs adventurers to journey north to the Agamand Mills to cull the roaming undead, slay the risen members of the Agamand lineage to recover their remains for desecration, and raid the Agamand Family Crypt for ancestral weaponry.",al={"coleman farthing quests","agamand quests brill"}},{q="Why does Coleman want the Agamand heirloom weapons?",a="Coleman sees the Agamands' ancestral weaponry as symbols of the hollow pride that led his fellow workers to their deaths. He sends skilled warriors to plunder these relics from the family crypt, both to strip the dynasty of its honor and put the weapons to practical use against their enemies.",al={"agamand heirlooms quest lore","why steal agamand weapons"}},{q="Is Coleman Farthing related to Bishop Farthing?",a="They share a surname and origins in the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, but there is no confirmed record of their specific familial ties.",al={"bishop farthing relation","coleman farthing family"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Coleman represents the shared resentment many commoners hold toward Lordaeron's old nobility, whose arrogance and pride often hastened their subjects' demise during the plague.",["class:Warrior"]="Coleman points aspiring warriors directly toward the Agamand Family Crypt, urging them to plunder the martial heirlooms of a fallen aristocratic house to arm themselves for the wars ahead."},kw={"agamand heirlooms","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","gallows' end tavern","lordaeron","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:gallows-end-tavern","subzone:agamand-mills","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","quest:354","quest:362","quest:1821","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Coleman Farthing"}}
E["npc:dark-cleric-beryl"] = {t="npc",n="Dark Cleric Beryl",z="tirisfal",s="Dark Cleric Beryl is a Forsaken priest trainer stationed in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. He guides newly awakened undead priests as they learn to wield shadow magic and adapt to their new, unholy existence under the Dark Lady.",h="Dark Cleric Beryl is a Forsaken priest trainer stationed in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Shadows",b="Residing on the upper floor of the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, Dark Cleric Beryl serves the Forsaken by mentoring nascent priests. Once dedicated to the Holy Light in life, many Forsaken priests found their connection to holy magic agonizing or severed upon being raised into undeath. Beryl assists these newly risen practitioners as they turn their focus toward shadow and the dark arts, guiding them through early trials like crafting their Garments of Darkness and proving their dedication to the new path.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dark Cleric Beryl?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl is a Forsaken priest trainer located upstairs in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. He instructs newly risen undead priests in expanding their spellcraft and embracing the shadows.",al={"beryl role","who is beryl","cleric beryl lore"}},{q="Where can I find Dark Cleric Beryl?",a="He is located in Tirisfal Glades inside the town of Brill. You can find him upstairs within the Gallows' End Tavern.",al={"beryl location","where is beryl","find dark cleric beryl"}},{q="Why do Forsaken priests use the title Dark Cleric?",a="Forsaken priests who abandon the traditional dogmas of the Holy Light or balance it with darker disciplines take up the title of Dark Cleric. Because channeling the Light is excruciating for their undead flesh, many lean heavily into shadow magic and the Cult of Forgotten Shadows.",al={"what is a dark cleric","forsaken dark clerics","why dark cleric"}},{q="What quests does Beryl offer?",a="Beryl is involved in early Forsaken priest training quests, including 'In Favor of Darkness' and 'Garments of Darkness', which teach young acolytes how to aid their allies and attire themselves in vestments suitable for the shadow.",al={"beryl quests","dark cleric beryl quests"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For Forsaken priests venturing into Tirisfal Glades, Beryl serves as an essential mentor in Brill, providing guidance on how to manipulate shadow magic and survive the harsh transition into unholy power.",["race:Undead"]="Beryl represents the Forsaken's adaptation to their cursed condition, trading the blind devotion of Lordaeron's former faiths for practical, shadowy resilience."},kw={"beryl","brill","dark cleric beryl","forsaken priest","gallows' end tavern","priest trainer","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","quest:5650","quest:5651","topic:forsaken"},src={"Dark Cleric Beryl"}}
E["npc:deathguard-bartholomew"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Bartholomew",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Bartholomew is a vigilant Forsaken soldier stationed in the town of Brill. Tasked with maintaining security across Tirisfal Glades, he helps travelers navigate the blighted settlement and assists in enforcing discipline among local defenders.",h="Deathguard Bartholomew is a vigilant Forsaken soldier stationed in the town of Brill.",sec={{t="Sentinel of Brill",b="Standing watch in the settlement of Brill, Deathguard Bartholomew represents the stalwart military backbone of the Forsaken. Like his fellow Deathguards throughout Tirisfal Glades, he defends reclaimed territory from lingering Scourge, fanatical Scarlet Crusaders, and any other threats to Lady Sylvanas's domain. In addition to keeping watch, he provides directions to travelers attempting to navigate the town's facilities and participates in maintaining orderly conduct among the newly risen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Bartholomew?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew is a Forsaken guard stationed in Brill within Tirisfal Glades. He stands as a sentry safeguarding the town and guides wayfarers to points of interest.",al={"bartholomew","who is bartholomew","deathguard bartholomew lore"}},{q="What is the role of the Deathguard?",a="The Deathguard serves as the primary infantry and defense force of the Forsaken. They patrol the territories of Lordaeron, defend settlements like Brill from the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade, and enforce order on behalf of the Dark Lady.",al={"what are deathguards","deathguard faction","forsaken guards"}},{q="Can Deathguard Bartholomew give directions?",a="Yes. Like many town sentries across Azeroth, Bartholomew can direct travelers to essential facilities throughout Brill, including trainers, the inn, and profession vendors.",al={"where is the inn","brill directions","guard directions brill"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For newly liberated Forsaken emerging from Deathknell, guards like Bartholomew in Brill are the first organized face of Lady Sylvanas's standing army.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies arriving from Kalimdor can rely on Bartholomew to find their bearings in the mist-shrouded streets of Brill."},kw={"bartholomew","brill","deathguard","forsaken","guard","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:86784","quest:99134"},src={"Deathguard Bartholomew"}}
E["npc:deathguard-burgess"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Burgess",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Burgess is a Forsaken sentry stationed in the town of Brill within Tirisfal Glades. Standing watch over the settlement, he keeps order and directs travelers to vital services across the hamlet.",h="Deathguard Burgess is a Forsaken sentry stationed in the town of Brill within Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Watchman in Brill",b="Positioned in the settlement of Brill just north of the Undercity, Deathguard Burgess serves as one of the town guards maintaining security against the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade. Like other Deathguards throughout Tirisfal Glades, Burgess aids arriving Forsaken by providing directions to local tradesfolk, class trainers, and civic services, keeping the vulnerable outpost running smoothly.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Burgess?",a="Deathguard Burgess is an undead sentry serving the Forsaken in the town of Brill. He helps keep order in the hamlet and assists visitors with directions to local trainers and points of interest.",al={"burgess brill","who is burgess","deathguard burgess lore"}},{q="What role do the Deathguards serve in Brill?",a="The Deathguard are the standard military and police force of the Forsaken. In places like Brill, they protect the local populace from outside threats like the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade while maintaining civil order.",al={"what are deathguards","deathguards role"}},{q="Can Deathguard Burgess provide directions?",a="Yes. Like many town guards across Azeroth, talking to Burgess allows travelers to ask for the location of class trainers, the local inn, profession masters, and other essential facilities in Brill.",al={"burgess directions","where to go in brill"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For newly awoken Forsaken leaving Deathknell, guards like Burgess in Brill provide your first orientation to the wider infrastructure of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Visiting allies from Kalimdor can speak to Burgess to navigate the unfamiliar, blighted layout of Brill when seeking out supply vendors or resting at the inn."},kw={"brill","burgess","deathguard burgess","forsaken","guard","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:374","quest:99134","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Deathguard Burgess"}}
E["npc:deathguard-dillinger"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Dillinger",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Dillinger is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Brill within Tirisfal Glades. Standing watch over the town's perimeter, he directs newly arrived undead toward necessary services and tasks recruits with keeping the local Scourge remnants at bay.",h="Deathguard Dillinger is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Brill within Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Sentinel of Brill",b="As a member of the Forsaken Deathguard, Dillinger stands at the entrance of Brill, serving as both a frontline protector and an orienting guide for travelers emerging from Deathknell. He provides directions to town amenities such as the inn, the town hall, and local trainers, helping newly awakened undead navigate their new reality under the Dark Lady's rule.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borderlands",b="Dillinger actively enlists capable adventurers to purge lingering mindless Scourge from the nearby farms and mills. Through assignments like cullling rotting ghouls and reclaiming infested facilities, he seeks to establish a buffer zone of security around Brill, ensuring the fledgling Forsaken settlements can endure against unending undead predation.",sp=0},{t="Containing Mindless Horrors",b="Beyond routine patrols, Dillinger coordinates responses against persistent Scourge threats lurking in the ruins around Brill. When summoned horrors such as Ulag the Cleaver emerge from nearby tombs or neglected homesteads, Dillinger ensures able fighters are dispatched to put the rampaging monstrosities down before they breach the settlement's borders.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can I find Deathguard Dillinger?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is posted on the outskirts of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades, watching the path leading into town.",al={"dillinger location","where is dillinger","deathguard dillinger coordinates"}},{q="What is the role of the Deathguard?",a="The Deathguard serves as the military standing army and constabulary of the Forsaken, guarding settlements like Brill and the Undercity against the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and other regional threats.",al={"what is deathguard","who are the deathguards","deathguard purpose"}},{q="What tasks does Deathguard Dillinger offer?",a="Dillinger tasks adventurers with slaying mindless Scourge wandering the surrounding fields and mills, reclaiming vital local infrastructure, and dealing with dangerous entities like Ulag the Cleaver.",al={"dillinger quests","what quests does dillinger have"}},{q="Can Deathguard Dillinger provide directions?",a="Yes, speaking with Dillinger allows players to request directions to essential services, profession trainers, and class mentors located throughout Brill.",al={"dillinger directions","ask dillinger for help"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken fighting other undead near Brill?",a="The mindless undead wandering Tirisfal remain under the thrall of the Scourge and the Lich King. Having broken free of that mental control, the Forsaken must eliminate these feral remnants to protect their own territory.",al={"why fight scourge","undead fighting undead","brill ghouls"}},{q="Who is Ulag the Cleaver?",a="Ulag the Cleaver is a dangerous Scourge horror tied to nearby tombs outside Brill. Dillinger coordinates with Forsaken recruits to summon and destroy Ulag to keep the surrounding area safe.",al={"ulag quest","who is ulag","ulag the cleaver"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For newly freed Forsaken arriving from Deathknell, Dillinger is often the first face of military authority they meet, directing them toward training and their first duties in service of Sylvanas.",["faction:Horde"]="Dillinger represents the Forsaken's struggle to carve out a secure foothold in northern Lordaeron, showing Horde allies the relentless menace posed by mindless Scourge at their doorsteps.",["class:Warrior"]="Aspiring Forsaken warriors frequently work directly with Dillinger to test their martial mettle against the ferocious ghouls and skeletal horrors prowling the outskirts of Brill."},kw={"a putrid task","brill","deathguard","deathguard dillinger","dillinger","the mills overrun","tirisfal glades","ulag the cleaver"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:404","quest:426","quest:1819","quest:1818","subzone:cold-hearth-manor"},src={"Deathguard Dillinger"}}
E["npc:deathguard-linnea"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Linnea",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Linnea is a Forsaken soldier stationed at Death's Watch Waystation in southeastern Tirisfal Glades. She helps secure the roads between Brill and the eastern borders, watching for threats posed by the Scarlet Crusade and lingering Scourge. Adventurers passing along the main thoroughfares often assist her unit with patrol duties.",h="Deathguard Linnea is a Forsaken soldier stationed at Death's Watch Waystation in southeastern Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Vigil on the Roadside",b="Deathguard Linnea stands sentinel at Death's Watch Waystation, a small fortified post southeast of Brill. Life—or unlife—on patrol in Tirisfal Glades is treacherous, as the Forsaken must vigilantly defend their fledgling realm against Scarlet Crusade infiltrators and mindless Scourge prowling the wilderness. Stationed alongside her fellow guards, Linnea oversees patrol efforts along the roadway, coordinating reports with local authorities such as Magistrate Sevren in Brill to keep the realm's southern approach secure.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Linnea?",a="Linnea is an undead soldier serving in the Deathguard, the military force charged with defending Forsaken territory. She is posted at Death's Watch Waystation along the road southeast of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"linnea","deathguard linnea lore","who is linnea"}},{q="What is Death's Watch Waystation?",a="It is an outpost established by the Forsaken to monitor and secure the eastern and southern thoroughfares of Tirisfal Glades. The station provides a forward staging ground against Scarlet Crusade scouts and roaming undead.",al={"deaths watch","deaths watch waystation","waystation tirisfal"}},{q="Why does she need help patrolling?",a="Forsaken military resources are stretched thin across Tirisfal Glades. Linnea relies on passing travelers and rising champions to help clear out surrounding threats, ensuring messengers and supply runners can travel safely back and forth to Brill.",al={"rear guard patrol lore","why help linnea"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken newly risen from Deathknell, aiding Deathguard Linnea at the waystation is one of the earliest duties undertaken to secure the borders of their new kingdom.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Forsaken traversing Tirisfal Glades can earn goodwill by assisting Linnea in stabilizing the outlying roadways against hostile forces."},kw={"brill","death's watch waystation","deathguard linnea","forsaken","magistrate sevren","rear guard patrol","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:death-s-watch-waystation","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:356","quest:360"},src={"Deathguard Linnea"}}
E["npc:deathguard-simmer"] = {t="npc",n="Deathguard Simmer",z="tirisfal",s="Deathguard Simmer is a Forsaken soldier stationed at the Calston Estate just east of Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. Tasked with securing the perimeter against human zealots, he directs newly risen Forsaken to combat the relentless incursions of the Scarlet Crusade.",h="Deathguard Simmer is a Forsaken soldier stationed at the Calston Estate just east of Deathknell in Tirisfal...",sec={{t="Guardian of the Estate",b="Positioned at the ruins of Calston Estate, Deathguard Simmer represents the Forsaken military line holding the border between the safe haven of Deathknell and the wider perils of Tirisfal Glades. The region crawls with living humans—most notably the fanatical Scarlet Crusade—who view all undead as abominations to be purged with fire and blade. Simmer coordinates local counter-offensives, dispatching adventurers to strike at Scarlet encampments like the nearby Scarlet Palisade and disrupt their operations before they can march on newly awakened Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deathguard Simmer?",a="Deathguard Simmer is a Forsaken sentry stationed at the Calston Estate in Tirisfal Glades. He assists in defending the local territory by tasking adventurers with neutralizing nearby hostile forces, particularly the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"deathguard simmer","who is simmer","simmer npc"}},{q="Where is Deathguard Simmer located?",a="He is located at Calston Estate, an abandoned farmstead found just east of the exit road leading out of Deathknell in southwestern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"deathguard simmer location","where is simmer","find deathguard simmer"}},{q="What threats does Deathguard Simmer fight?",a="Simmer focuses on the Scarlet Crusade, a faction of zealous humans occupying fortifications like the Scarlet Palisade. He enlists scouts and soldiers to recover intelligence and eliminate the crusaders threatening the Forsaken hold on the area.",al={"simmer enemies","what does simmer fight","scarlet palisade quests"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Simmer offers some of the first missions directly targeting the Scarlet Crusade, marking an undead adventurer's graduation from the crypts of Deathknell into the broader defense of Lordaeron."},kw={"calston estate","deathguard","deathguard simmer","deathknell","scarlet palisade","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:calston-estate","subzone:deathknell","subzone:scarlet-palisade","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:365"},src={"Deathguard Simmer"}}
E["npc:elder-graveborn"] = {t="npc",n="Elder Graveborn",z="tirisfal",s="Elder Graveborn is an ancestral spirit who manifests just southeast of Brill during the Lunar Festival. Appearing as a spectral earthen elder, he honors travelers and guides pilgrims searching for other ancient spirits scattered throughout northern Lordaeron.",h="Elder Graveborn is an ancestral spirit who manifests just southeast of Brill during the Lunar Festival.",sec={{t="A Spirit in Tirisfal",b="Appearing just beyond the Forsaken town of Brill, Elder Graveborn stands among the haunted woods of Tirisfal Glades as part of the worldwide Lunar Festival. Despite the blighted surroundings and the troubled state of the kingdom, the spectral elder offers peaceful greetings to travelers seeking the festival's traditional blessings. In addition to bestowing his own ancestral wisdom, Graveborn shares news of other elders lingering nearby—pointing pilgrims toward spirits abiding in the Undercity, the Sepulcher, and across the Plaguelands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Elder Graveborn?",a="Elder Graveborn is a revered ancestral ghost who appears during the Lunar Festival. He materializes in Tirisfal Glades just southeast of Brill to grant festival blessings to passing adventurers.",al={"elder graveborn lore","who is graveborn","brill ghost elder"}},{q="Why is he in Tirisfal Glades?",a="During the Lunar Festival, ancestral spirits appear across Azeroth to celebrate past heroes and communal heritage. Elder Graveborn watches over the lands outside Brill, maintaining an ancient presence amidst the fallen kingdom of Lordaeron.",al={"why brill","where is elder graveborn"}},{q="Can Alliance adventurers speak to him?",a="Yes. Festival elders welcome travelers of both factions regardless of territory. However, Alliance characters must exercise caution when approaching his resting ground, as he stands in close proximity to the Forsaken hub of Brill.",al={"can alliance talk to graveborn","alliance elder brill"}},{q="What information does he offer travelers?",a="Elder Graveborn guides pilgrims toward other local ancestors, sharing rumors of spirits residing in the Undercity, Silverpine's Sepulcher, Light's Hope Chapel, the Weeping Cave, and Scholomance.",al={"elder graveborn directions","graveborn quotes"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken walking the road between Brill and the Undercity, Graveborn serves as a tranquil reminder of Azeroth's ancient past, resting untroubled by the Scourge or the blight.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance pilgrims must skirt the outskirts of Brill carefully to pay their respects to Graveborn without drawing the wrath of Forsaken town guards and patrols."},kw={"ancestor","brill","earthen","elder graveborn","graveborn","lunar festival","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:8652","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","zone:undercity","npc:elder-darkcore","npc:elder-obsidian","subzone:sepulcher","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel"},src={"Elder Graveborn"}}
E["npc:eleanor-shackleton"] = {t="npc",n="Eleanor Shackleton",z="tirisfal",s="Eleanor Shackleton is a Forsaken outdoorswoman found camping southwest of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Rather than lingering within town or the Undercity, she assists wandering travelers in learning wilderness survival and field crafts. She shares her surname with other Forsaken surviving in the region, suggesting lingering ties from life before the plague.",h="Eleanor Shackleton is a Forsaken outdoorswoman found camping southwest of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Guide to the Glades",b="While many newly awakened Forsaken head straight to Brill or delve into the Undercity, Eleanor Shackleton makes her camp in the haunted woods to the southwest. Surviving out in Tirisfal requires pragmatic self-reliance, and Eleanor serves as an instructor for fledgling adventurers seeking to live off the blighted land. Through her various field lessons, she guides travelers in establishing campsites, gathering firewood, and maintaining trade crafts while roaming far from civilization's forge fires and kitchens.",sp=0},{t="Ties from a Past Life",b="In the shattered remnants of Lordaeron, family names often serve as the sole surviving tether to an undead's mortal past. Eleanor carries the surname Shackleton, shared by Pierce Shackleton in Brill and Samantha Shackleton elsewhere in Tirisfal. Whether the three maintain close bonds or merely carry common ancestry from their mortal days, each has carved out a distinct role in serving the Forsaken cause across the blighted kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Eleanor Shackleton?",a="Eleanor Shackleton makes her camp southwest of Brill, tucked into the woods of Tirisfal Glades away from the main paved road.",al={"eleanor shackleton location","where is eleanor","shackleton spot"}},{q="What does Eleanor Shackleton teach adventurers?",a="Eleanor guides travelers through the basics of wilderness survival, offering instruction on camping, foraging, and practicing professions out in the wild.",al={"eleanor quests","what does eleanor do","camping quests tirisfal"}},{q="Is Eleanor related to other Shackletons in Lordaeron?",a="She shares her family name with Pierce Shackleton in Brill and Samantha Shackleton, indicating potential kinship from their lives before the kingdom fell to the Scourge.",al={"pierce shackleton relative","samantha shackleton","shackleton family lore"}},{q="Why is she camping outside Brill instead of staying in town?",a="Eleanor focuses on fieldcraft and wilderness survival. Setting up her camp in the woods allows her to meet wayfarers and train them directly where those skills are needed.",al={"why camp outside brill","eleanor shackleton camp"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, learning to survive in the wilderness without living comforts is vital, and Eleanor ensures that newly risen brethren adapt quickly to roughing it in Tirisfal.",["profession:Cooking"]="Eleanor's instruction covers setting up a field campfire and preparing meals away from civilized hearths, making her camp a key stop for traveling cooks."},kw={"brill","camping 101","eleanor shackleton","shackleton","sticks and bones","the adventurer","the great outdoors","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:96658","quest:96607","quest:86784","quest:96627"},src={"Eleanor Shackleton"}}
E["npc:executor-arren"] = {t="npc",n="Executor Arren",z="tirisfal",s="Executor Arren is a high-ranking Forsaken officer stationed in Deathknell. He oversees the immediate defense and consolidation of the settlement as newly awakened undead emerge from their graves. Arren coordinates the local campaign against mindless Scourge zombies, feral beasts, and the encroaching zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.",h="Executor Arren is a high-ranking Forsaken officer stationed in Deathknell.",sec={{t="Commander of Deathknell",b="Standing resolute just outside the chapel in Deathknell, Executor Arren serves as the primary military voice for the nascent Forsaken within their awakening grounds. While the caretakers in the crypts guide newly raised undead through their disorientation, Arren directs their focus outward toward survival. Under Queen Sylvanas Windrunner's banner, he organizes local operations to sweep away mindless zombies that threaten the village borders, establishing secure territory in the shadow of Lordaeron's fall.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Borderlands",b="Deathknell is surrounded by perils far deadlier than confused fledglings. Under Arren's orders, scouts and initiates strike at the vicious arachnids inhabiting Night Web's Hollow and eliminate dangerous predators haunting the woodland fringes. By demanding decisive action from every capable hand, Arren tests the fortitude of new arrivals, ensuring only those capable of defending their second chance at existence remain in the service of the Dark Lady.",sp=0},{t="The Crimson Threat",b="Arren's greatest strategic concern lies with the Scarlet Crusade. The zealots consider all undead to be monstrosities requiring total eradication, failing or refusing to distinguish between the Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken. Arren organizes targeted strikes against Scarlet patrols encamped in the Tirisfal wilderness, intercepting couriers and analyzing stolen dispatches to safeguard Deathknell from being purged in holy fire.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Executor Arren?",a="Executor Arren is the commanding military officer overseeing Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. He organizes newly risen Forsaken into an effective fighting force to defend the village and secure the surrounding countryside.",al={"arren role","who is arren","deathknell executor"}},{q="What rank is an Executor among the Forsaken?",a="Executors are trusted military and administrative commanders within the Forsaken hierarchy. They govern local garrisons, direct operations in the field, and enforce the will and law of Queen Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"executor title","what is an executor","forsaken executor rank"}},{q="Why does Arren send recruits against the zombies?",a="The zombies prowling near Deathknell are mindless Scourge remnants left behind after the plague devastated Lordaeron. Arren orders them cleared so that newly awakened undead are not torn apart upon leaving the crypts.",al={"why kill zombies","the damned quest","mindless scourge"}},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a radical human faction dedicated to exterminating all undead. They hold outposts across the ruins of Lordaeron and actively seek to purge the Forsaken, considering them identical to the Scourge.",al={"scarlet crusade tirisfal","why crusade here","crusaders in deathknell"}},{q="What is Night Web's Hollow?",a="Night Web's Hollow is a spider-infested cave north of Deathknell. Arren directs recruits to clear out the aggressive arachnids to eliminate a major local hazard and demonstrate martial competence.",al={"spider cave deathknell","night webs hollow","arren spider quest"}},{q="Where does Arren send recruits once they finish his tasks?",a="Once Deathknell's immediate threats are neutralized, Arren directs capable recruits outward to Brill to report to Executor Zygand and aid the broader Forsaken effort across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"next after deathknell","where to go after arren","the executor in the field"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Executor Arren is one of the first commanders every Forsaken meets upon emerging into Tirisfal, giving them their earliest taste of duty under the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="Arren's frontline commands in Deathknell represent the Horde's initial foothold in northern Lordaeron, securing survival amidst hostile surroundings."},kw={"deathknell","executor arren","forsaken","night web's hollow","scarlet crusade","sylvanas","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:night-web-s-hollow","quest:96627"},src={"Executor Arren"}}
E["npc:executor-zygand"] = {t="npc",n="Executor Zygand",z="tirisfal",s="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken commander stationed at the town hall in Brill, overseeing defensive and military operations across central Tirisfal Glades. Reporting directly to the Undercity's high command, he coordinates the purge of Scarlet Crusade forces pressing into Forsaken territory.",h="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken commander stationed at the town hall in Brill, overseeing defensive and...",sec={{t="Command in Brill",b="Positioned at the administrative heart of Brill, Executor Zygand coordinates regional defense for the Forsaken after their initial awakening in Deathknell. Serving as the direct superior to regional officers like Executor Arren and field sentries such as Deathguard Linnea, Zygand synthesizes scout intelligence and dispatches able recruits to safeguard Lordaeron's borders from encroachment.",sp=0},{t="The War on the Crusade",b="Zygand's primary military concern is the fanatic presence of the Scarlet Crusade, which infests outposts across Tirisfal Glades. Under his direction, agents are sent systematically to strike at Crusader scouts, encampments, and forward bases, ensuring the zealots never muster sufficient strength to threaten the approaches to the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken officer operating out of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He commands local Deathguard garrisons, receives tactical reports from lower-ranking officers, and directs military campaigns against local threats.",al={"zygand","who is executor zygand","zygand role"}},{q="Where can I find Executor Zygand?",a="He is located inside or near the main town hall of Brill, the central Forsaken settlement in Tirisfal Glades situated just north of the Undercity.",al={"zygand location","where is zygand","executor zygand map"}},{q="What is Zygand's main goal in Tirisfal Glades?",a="His primary focus is orchestrating the regional war against the Scarlet Crusade. He monitors the zealots' movements throughout Tirisfal and issues orders to dismantle their encampments and leadership before they can march on the Undercity.",al={"zygand quest goal","why fight crusade","zygand purpose"}},{q="Who reports to Executor Zygand?",a="Zygand acts as the superior officer to Executor Arren, who directs initial recruits in Deathknell, as well as field sentries like Deathguard Linnea patrolling the main crossroads of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"zygand subordinates","who serves zygand","arren superior"}},{q="Does Executor Zygand handle rogue undead threats?",a="Yes. In addition to fighting the Scarlet Crusade, Zygand issues regional bounties to eliminate feral undead and dangerous rogue scavengers, such as the mindless ghoul Maggot Eye, that endanger travel through the glades.",al={"maggot eye","zygand bounties","wanted quests"}},{q="What rank does an 'Executor' hold among the Forsaken?",a="An Executor serves as a regional governor and military commander within the Forsaken hierarchy. They manage settlements, command local units of the Deathguard, and enforce Queen Sylvanas's rule across Lordaeron's contested regions.",al={"what is an executor","executor rank","forsaken executor"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken venturing out of Deathknell, Executor Zygand represents the wider military authority of the Undercity, welcoming new citizens into active service against their bitterest enemies.",["faction:Horde"]="Travelers from Kalimdor visiting Tirisfal Glades see in Zygand the structured, disciplined military leadership driving the Forsaken's struggle to secure Lordaeron."},kw={"arren","brill","deathguard","executor","maggot eye","scarlet crusade","tirisfal","zygand"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","quest:370","npc:executor-arren","npc:deathguard-linnea","quest:398","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken"},src={"Executor Zygand"}}
E["npc:gunther-arcanus"] = {t="npc",n="Gunther Arcanus",z="tirisfal",s="Gunther Arcanus is an exceptionally powerful necromancer dwelling on an isolated island in Brightwater Lake. Slain during the Third War and raised into undeath, he managed to shatter the Lich King's mental grip entirely on his own. Long believing he was the sole undead possessing free will, he defended his retreat against all outsiders until discovered by the Forsaken.",h="Gunther Arcanus is an exceptionally powerful necromancer dwelling on an isolated island in Brightwater Lake.",sec={{t="A Student of Dalaran",b="Before the fall of Lordaeron, Gunther was a promising apprentice among the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. Alongside close friends Bethor Iceshard and Thule Ravenclaw, he studied the arcane arts, secretly delving into necromancy despite the Kirin Tor's strict prohibitions against dark magic. To commemorate their brotherhood, the trio once bound their apprentice wands together into a single heirloom.",sp=0},{t="Breaking the Shackles",b="When the Scourge swept across the north during the Third War, Gunther perished to the Plague of Undeath and was raised into servitude. Unlike most who required the Lich King's power to weaken or Lady Sylvanas to break their chains, Gunther's raw arcane mastery and sheer willpower allowed him to shake off the Lich King's mental domination entirely by himself. Convinced that every other walking corpse remained a mindless thrall of the Scourge, he retreated to an island in Tirisfal Glades, surrounding himself with shambling guardians and cutting off all contact with the living and dead alike.",sp=0},{t="The Prodigal Lich",b="Seeking powerful allies against the Scourge, the Forsaken sent emissaries to claim the mysterious necromancer's spellbook. Upon examining the arcane tome in the Undercity, Bethor Iceshard recognized the unique handwriting of his long-lost peer. By enchanting the returned grimoire and demanding the destruction of local Scourge commanders, Gunther finally realized he was not alone in his freedom. Convinced that Sylvanas's faction represents a true rebellion against the Scourge, he has forged a pact with his former schoolmate to aid the Forsaken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gunther Arcanus?",a="He is a former wizard of the Kirin Tor from Dalaran who perished during the Third War. Raised into undeath, he broke free of the Lich King's domination on his own and retreated to an island in Brightwater Lake in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who is gunther","gunther lore","gunther arcanus story"}},{q="Why does Gunther look like a regular Forsaken instead of a skeletal lich?",a="While traditional liches transfer their spirits into phylacteries and generate monstrous, floating skeletal forms, Gunther achieved his lich-like necromantic status without abandoning his original reanimated corpse, preserving his physical mortal appearance.",al={"why does gunther look human","gunther not a skeleton","why is gunther a lich"}},{q="Why was Gunther living alone on an island?",a="After breaking the Lich King's mental control, Gunther believed he was the only undead in existence with free will. Assuming all other walking dead were still mindless slaves of the Scourge, he secluded himself and ordered his minions to strike down anyone who approached.",al={"why is gunther alone","gunther island isolation","why does gunther hide"}},{q="How does Gunther know Bethor Iceshard?",a="They were classmates and close friends in Dalaran studying under the Kirin Tor, along with a third mage named Thule Ravenclaw. The three friends even wove their apprentice wands together as a symbol of their bond.",al={"bethor and gunther","how does gunther know bethor","bethor iceshard history"}},{q="Does Gunther join the Forsaken?",a="Yes. Once adventurers return his enchanted spellbook and execute the local Scourge agent Lillith Nefara to prove their independence from the Lich King, Gunther pledges his allegiance to Bethor and the Forsaken cause.",al={"does gunther join horde","gunther faction","is gunther forsaken"},sp=1},{q="Who is Lillith Nefara?",a="Lillith Nefara is an agent of the Scourge stationed in Tirisfal Glades. Gunther requires her death as proof that the adventurer truly serves an enemy of the Lich King rather than the Scourge itself.",al={"lillith nefara","nefara","gunther target"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Gunther's self-liberation makes him an anomaly among the Forsaken, proving that intense arcane training and iron will alone could sometimes shatter the Lich King's mental dominion.",["class:Mage"]="Trained in Dalaran, Gunther represents the Kirin Tor wizards who covertly dabbled in forbidden necromantic spells before the Scourge invaded Lordaeron.",["class:Warlock"]="Gunther's commanding grasp of dark arts and reanimation demonstrates how far forbidden scholarship could flourish outside the watchful eyes of Dalaran's leadership."},kw={"arcanus","bethor","brightwater","dalaran","gunther","iceshard","kirin tor","lich","necromancer","thule","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:gunther-s-retreat","npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:405","quest:366","quest:409","quest:411","npc:thor","quest:446"},src={"Gunther Arcanus"}}
E["npc:high-executor-derrington"] = {t="npc",n="High Executor Derrington",z="tirisfal",s="High Executor Derrington commands the Forsaken vanguard stationed at the Bulwark on the eastern border of Tirisfal Glades. A no-nonsense military officer, he oversees the Horde's front-line defense against the Scourge and Scarlet Crusade threats emanating from the Western Plaguelands. From this fortified barricade, he directs seasoned champions toward contested ruins like Andorhal and Scholomance.",h="High Executor Derrington commands the Forsaken vanguard stationed at the Bulwark on the eastern border of...",sec={{t="Commander at the Threshold",b="Standing directly before the fortified barricades of the Bulwark, High Executor Derrington serves as the gatekeeper between the haunted safety of Tirisfal Glades and the rotting horrors of the Western Plaguelands. Derrington holds little patience for political maneuvering in the Undercity, viewing the front lines as a crucible of sheer survival. For Horde soldiers and sellswords seeking to test their mettle, Derrington provides direct military orders, sending scouts and strike teams deep into plagueridden territory to blunt enemy incursions before they breach Tirisfal.",sp=0},{t="A War on Two Fronts",b="Derrington's defensive position is beleaguered on multiple axes. To the east lies the Scourge, entrenched in the shattered town of Andorhal and spilling through the countryside via corrupting cauldrons. Simultaneously, the zealous fanatics of the Scarlet Crusade contest northern fortifications and skirmish relentlessly with Forsaken patrols. Derrington coordinates surgical counterattacks, sabotage against the Scarlet lines, and the systematic disruption of Scourge cauldron fields to safeguard the eastern border.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is High Executor Derrington?",a="High Executor Derrington is the senior Forsaken commander at the Bulwark, the military outpost separating Tirisfal Glades from the Western Plaguelands. He coordinates the Horde's strategic push eastward against both the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"derrington","who is derrington","high executor derrington lore"}},{q="Where is Derrington located?",a="He is stationed at the Bulwark, the fortified choke point located at the far eastern edge of Tirisfal Glades along the road leading into the Western Plaguelands.",al={"where is derrington","derrington location","find high executor derrington"}},{q="What is Derrington's objective at the Bulwark?",a="Derrington's goal is to ensure the survival of the Forsaken by maintaining a strong defensive perimeter against the Scourge and striking eastward into the Western Plaguelands. He tasks adventurers with scouting Andorhal, disabling plague cauldrons, and neutralizing Scarlet Crusade operations.",al={"what does derrington want","bulwark purpose","derrington mission"}},{q="Does Derrington care about Undercity politics?",a="No. Derrington expresses open disdain for court schemers and politicians, noting that such luxuries do not exist on the front lines where survival must be fought for every day.",al={"derrington personality","is derrington political"}},{q="What major threats does Derrington send soldiers against?",a="Derrington primarily targets the Scourge holding the ruins of Andorhal, the dark necromancers inside Scholomance, and nearby Scarlet Crusade garrisons that threaten the Horde's eastern supply routes.",al={"derrington quests","what does derrington fight"}},{q="Why is the Bulwark so heavily fortified?",a="The Bulwark stands as the primary chokepoint between the relative security of Tirisfal Glades and the active combat zones of the Plaguelands. Derrington's forces hold the pass to prevent massive Scourge swarms or Scarlet Crusade crusades from sweeping directly toward the Undercity.",al={"why is the bulwark here","bulwark lore"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers arriving in Tirisfal, Derrington is the principal military commander directing forces into the dangerous conflicts of the Western Plaguelands.",["race:Undead"]="Derrington represents the martial backbone of the Forsaken military, focused squarely on preserving their reclaimed lands from Scourge reclamation and Scarlet fanaticism.",["class:Warrior"]="Derrington embodies the grim, practical grit of a front-line soldier who values martial competence and battlefield results over Court scheming."},kw={"andorhal","bulwark","derrington","forsaken","high executor derrington","scourge","tirisfal glades","western plaguelands"},rel={"subzone:bulwark","zone:tirisfal","subzone:andorhal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:scholomance","subzone:cauldron"},src={"High Executor Derrington"}}
E["npc:magistrate-sevren"] = {t="npc",n="Magistrate Sevren",z="tirisfal",s="Magistrate Sevren is the chief administrative official presiding over the settlement of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Standing inside the town hall, he organizes early Forsaken defense and directs arriving champions to stabilize the territory around the Undercity.",h="Magistrate Sevren is the chief administrative official presiding over the settlement of Brill in Tirisfal...",sec={{t="Town Magistrate of Brill",b="Operating from the town hall in Brill, Magistrate Sevren coordinates civil authority and strategic efforts in the lands just north of the Undercity. As new Forsaken step forth into Tirisfal Glades, Sevren assesses local crises and dispatches adventurers to restore order, secure ruined infrastructure, and suppress persistent threats lingering in the surrounding hills.",sp=0},{t="Securing the Graves",b="Sevren's primary concerns center on the preservation and recovery of the Tirisfal dead. Local graverobbers, rot hides, and rogue undead disrupt burial grounds, threatening the emerging dominion of Sylvanas Windrunner. Sevren ensures that ancestral tombs—such as the Agamand Family Crypt—are reclaimed and that deserters or uncooperative forces do not subvert Forsaken authority in the region.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Magistrate Sevren?",a="Magistrate Sevren is the administrative head of Brill, stationed within the town hall. He serves as an overseer for Forsaken territorial management, handing out tasks to adventurers who arrive from Deathknell to aid the fledgling realm.",al={"magistrate sevren","who is sevren","brill magistrate"}},{q="Where can Magistrate Sevren be found?",a="He is located inside the Town Hall in the center of Brill, in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"sevren location","where is magistrate sevren","find sevren"}},{q="What threats does Magistrate Sevren deal with?",a="Sevren contends with local threats to Tirisfal Glades, including human graverobbers, rogue rot hides, Scourge remnants desecrating local crypts, and rogue undead figures who refuse allegiance to Lady Sylvanas.",al={"sevren quests","what does sevren want","brill problems"}},{q="What is Magistrate Sevren's allegiance?",a="He is loyal to the Forsaken and governs Brill on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Undercity.",al={"sevren faction","who does sevren serve"}},{q="Why does Sevren send adventurers to the family crypt?",a="The crypts belonging to the old Agamand dynasty are overrun with undead and scavenging threats. Sevren demands that adventurers secure the ancestral resting places to prevent enemies from exploiting them.",al={"agamand crypt","sevren crypt quest"}},{q="Does Sevren have ties to the Undercity leadership?",a="Yes. As the local magistrate, he frequently liaises with agents and officials from the Undercity, dispatching messengers and directing adventurers deeper into the capital once their competence in Brill is proven.",al={"sevren undercity","sevren raleigh"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For newly liberated Forsaken leaving Deathknell, Magistrate Sevren represents the civic face of Sylvanas's realm, providing your first major assignments to safeguard your homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Horde arriving in Tirisfal will find Sevren coordinating the front-line pacification of Tirisfal Glades against bandits, Scourge remnants, and rebel factions."},kw={"agamand","brill","forsaken","magistrate","sevren","tirisfal","town hall","undercity"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:355","quest:360","quest:358","quest:408","zone:undercity"},src={"Magistrate Sevren"}}
E["npc:shadow-priest-sarvis"] = {t="npc",n="Shadow Priest Sarvis",z="tirisfal",s="Shadow Priest Sarvis stands inside the ruined chapel of Deathknell, serving as one of the primary guides for newly awakened Forsaken. He introduces fresh corpses to their grim reality, directing them to purge mindless undead and gather intelligence on local threats. Under Lady Sylvanas's banner, Sarvis works tirelessly to shape bewildered undead into disciplined servants of the Forsaken.",h="Shadow Priest Sarvis stands inside the ruined chapel of Deathknell, serving as one of the primary guides for...",sec={{t="Shepherd of the Newly Awakened",b="Within the shadowy chapel of Deathknell, Shadow Priest Sarvis waits for those who have just clawed their way out of the grave. The awakening of a Forsaken soul is jarring and horrific, with many immediately losing their minds to mindless frenzy or despondency. Sarvis acts as an anchor, giving purpose to the newly risen. He assigns new recruits to put down the shambling, mindless corpses roaming the cemetery and directs them to secure Deathknell's borders against the encroaching Scourge.",sp=0},{t="Securing Deathknell",b="Beyond acclimating new recruits, Sarvis oversees crucial local defenses against lingering threats in Tirisfal Glades. He monitors the rogue mindless undead gathering at the Rotbrain Encampment and coordinates the containment of Scourge forces probing Deathknell's perimeter. By directing novices toward vital intelligence and martial trials, Sarvis ensures that the town remains a fortified bastion for the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shadow Priest Sarvis?",a="Sarvis is a Forsaken shadow priest stationed in Deathknell. He guides freshly awakened undead, giving them their initial orders and helping secure the town against the Scourge.",al={"sarvis","who is sarvis","deathknell priest"}},{q="Where can I find Shadow Priest Sarvis?",a="He is located inside the ruined church at the center of Deathknell, the Forsaken starting area in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"sarvis location","where is sarvis","find sarvis"}},{q="Why is Sarvis having players kill mindless zombies?",a="Not every corpse raised from the grave retains their free will and sanity. Those who succumb to madness are deemed a hazard to the settlement and must be destroyed before they endanger the living dead.",al={"why kill mindless ones","rotbrains","the mindless ones"}},{q="What is the Rotbrain Encampment?",a="The Rotbrain Encampment is a nearby pocket where mindless, feral undead gather. Sarvis orders assaults against it to prevent these rogue ghouls and zombies from overrunning Deathknell.",al={"rotbrain camp","rotbrains deathknell"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Sarvis is one of the very first voices you hear after waking from the grave, setting you on your path to serve the Dark Lady.",["class:Priest"]="Sarvis exemplifies the Forsaken's embrace of shadow magic, serving as a dark mentor figure in a chapel stripped of Holy Light."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken","novice elreth","rotbrain","sarvis","shadow priest sarvis","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","subzone:rotbrain-encampment"},src={"Shadow Priest Sarvis"}}
E["npc:shari-stilwell"] = {t="npc",n="Shari Stilwell",z="tirisfal",s="Shari Stilwell is a Forsaken paladin trainer stationed in the settlement of Brill within Tirisfal Glades. Bearing a surname shared with notable figures in the Eastern Kingdoms, she instructs Forsaken who take up the mantle of holy warriors. Her presence marks a rare and unconventional discipline among the undead under the Banshee Queen.",h="Shari Stilwell is a Forsaken paladin trainer stationed in the settlement of Brill within Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Beacon in Brill",b="Found among the blight-touched buildings of Brill, Shari Stilwell stands out as a mentor to Forsaken holy warriors. While the holy Light is excruciating to the undead, Shari guides fledgling Forsaken who endure that agonizing path. She aids newcomers seeking their footing in Tirisfal Glades through their early training and adjustments, offering guidance to those looking to secure a place within the Forsaken kingdom.",sp=0},{t="Ties of the Stilwell Name",b="Shari shares her family name with several living figures scattered across the southern kingdoms, including Daphne, Merissa, and the renowned paladin Jordan Stilwell. Whether she was torn away from these kin during the fall of Lordaeron or shares only a distant lineage remains an unspoken tragedy of the Scourge's devastation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Shari Stilwell?",a="Shari Stilwell is an undead paladin trainer stationed in Brill in Tirisfal Glades. She assists Forsaken paladins with their early martial and holy instruction as they learn to survive in Lordaeron.",al={"who is shari stilwell","shari stilwell lore","brill paladin trainer"}},{q="Where can Shari Stilwell be found?",a="She is located in the town of Brill, just north of the Capital City ruins and the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"shari stilwell location","where is shari stilwell","find shari stilwell"}},{q="Is Shari related to Jordan Stilwell?",a="She shares her surname with Jordan Stilwell, the famous human paladin and smith, as well as Daphne and Merissa Stilwell. Their exact family connection is unconfirmed, but likely severed by the plague that destroyed Lordaeron.",al={"jordan stilwell relation","stilwell family ties","shari stilwell relatives"}},{q="Can Forsaken wield the Light as paladins?",a="Channeling the Holy Light is deeply painful for undead beings, causing intense agony and burning sensations. However, trainers like Shari Stilwell guide determined Forsaken through the mental fortitude and devotion required to wield both martial skill and holy power.",al={"forsaken paladins","how can undead be paladins","undead paladin lore"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For Forsaken paladins beginning their journey in Tirisfal Glades, Shari Stilwell serves as the primary trainer and mentor in Brill.",["race:Undead"]="Shari Stilwell reflects the tragic splintering of families wrought by the Third War, standing as an undead mentor while potential kin endure far to the south."},kw={"brill","forsaken","light","paladin","shari","stilwell","tirisfal","trainer"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","npc:jordan-stilwell","npc:daphne-stilwell","npc:merissa-stilwell","quest:91209"},src={"Shari Stilwell"}}
E["npc:yvette-farthing"] = {t="npc",n="Yvette Farthing",z="tirisfal",s="Yvette Farthing is a Forsaken resident of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, dwelling in the Gallows' End Tavern alongside her father, Coleman. Though she appears as hardened and detached as any of Sylvanas's people, she carries the lingering ghost of a mortal romance cut short by the Scourge.",h="Yvette Farthing is a Forsaken resident of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, dwelling in the Gallows' End Tavern...",sec={{t="Echoes of the Mills",b="Before the Third War swept Lordaeron into ruin, Yvette was in love with Thurman Agamand, one of the heirs of the prosperous Agamand Mills. When the Scourge plague approached, Yvette and her father, Coleman, begged Thurman to abandon the estate and flee with them. Thurman refused out of devotion to his family's legacy. Both would eventually perish and rise into undeath, but while Yvette found a place among the free-willed Forsaken in Brill, Thurman's tragic final fate remained unknown to her.",sp=0},{t="A Final Farewell",b="Before the mills were overrun, Thurman penned an urgent love letter to Yvette, detailing the treachery of his brother Devlin and lamenting his choice to stay. The Scourge intercepted the message, leaving it lost among the ruins of Agamand Mills until recovered by adventurers. Upon reading Thurman's dying confession, Yvette briefly displays genuine mortal despair before forcing herself back into cold detachment, bitter that such past attachments have no place in the grim reality of the Forsaken.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Yvette Farthing?",a="Yvette Farthing is a Forsaken woman living in Brill's Gallows' End Tavern. She is the daughter of Coleman Farthing and formerly lived in the farmlands of Tirisfal Glades before the Third War destroyed the kingdom.",al={"yvette farthing lore","who is yvette","brill yvette"}},{q="What is Yvette's connection to Agamand Mills?",a="In life, Yvette was romantically involved with Thurman Agamand. When the plague threatened the region, she tried to convince him to flee with her, but he chose to remain and defend his family's estate.",al={"yvette agamand","thurman agamand and yvette","yvette lover"}},{q="What happens when you deliver Thurman's letter to her?",a="When an adventurer delivers Thurman's long-lost letter, Yvette is momentarily crushed by sorrow upon reading his final words of love and betrayal. However, she quickly hardens her demeanor, declaring that she is Forsaken now and that mortal sentiment is useless.",al={"a letter undelivered turn in","thurmans letter reward","yvette reaction letter"},sp=1},{q="Who is Yvette's father?",a="Her father is Coleman Farthing, a Forsaken also residing in the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. They both managed to survive long enough to flee together initially, though both eventually succumbed to the plague and became Forsaken.",al={"yvette father","coleman and yvette","who is coleman farthing"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Yvette represents the deep emotional conflict many Forsaken endure, struggling between lingering human memories of love and the bitter, hardened reality of undeath."},kw={"a letter undelivered","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","gallows' end tavern","thurman agamand","tirisfal glades","yvette farthing"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","quest:361","subzone:agamand-mills","subzone:brill","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Yvette Farthing"}}
E["quest:1819"] = {t="quest",n="Ulag the Cleaver",z="tirisfal",s="Ulag the Cleaver is a rite of passage for young Forsaken warriors in Tirisfal Glades. Deathguard Dillinger tasks you with releasing and executing an enslaved Scourge warrior bound inside a northern mausoleum, testing your martial resolve and earning the respect of the Deathguard.",h="Ulag the Cleaver is a rite of passage for young Forsaken warriors in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Bound Scourge Thrall",b="When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, the Forsaken managed to capture a peculiar undead warrior who named himself Ulag the Cleaver. While Ulag possessed a conscious, lucid mind, his spirit remained inextricably dominated by the psychic thrall of the Lich King. Seeking to understand how the Scourge binds free will, the Forsaken kept him restrained under a magical seal beneath a mausoleum north of Brill, hoping to break the entity's spiritual chains.",sp=0},{t="The Executioner's Trial",b="All efforts to sever Ulag from the Lich King's mental grip ended in failure. Recognizing that true freedom could only come through destruction, Deathguard Dillinger repurposed the captive as a trial of combat for rising Forsaken warriors. By disturbing the skull stone trigger outside the crypt, a warrior breaks the protective wards, releases Ulag from his imprisonment, and grants him release at the edge of an axe.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ulag the Cleaver?",a="Ulag the Cleaver was an undead warrior captured by the Forsaken during the Scourge's invasion of Tirisfal Glades. Uniquely, he retained his free mind and identity, yet remained completely enthralled by the Lich King's mental command.",al={"ulag lore","who is ulag","ulag the cleaver identity"}},{q="Why was Ulag imprisoned under the mausoleum?",a="Forsaken scholars and soldiers imprisoned him beneath a magical seal to study how the Lich King's mind control functioned. They had hoped to discover a method to sever the psychic link that bound him, though their experiments proved unsuccessful.",al={"why is ulag locked up","mausoleum prisoner tirisfal"}},{q="Why do the Deathguards want Ulag killed now?",a="Having admitted defeat in breaking the Lich King's grip on Ulag, the Forsaken decided death was the only mercy remaining. Deathguard Dillinger chose to use the execution as a test of martial courage and discipline for aspiring warriors.",al={"why kill ulag","reason to slay ulag"}},{q="How is Ulag summoned?",a="He is imprisoned beneath a mausoleum just north of Brill. Interacting with the skull stone near the tomb releases the magical seal that binds him, causing him to rise and attack.",al={"how to summon ulag","where is ulag","ulag skull stone"}},{q="Who gives the quest to slay Ulag?",a="Deathguard Dillinger, who guards the western road leading out of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, assigns this mission specifically to Forsaken warriors seeking further instruction.",al={"quest giver ulag","who sends me to ulag"}},{q="What happens after Ulag is defeated?",a="Upon confirming Ulag's demise, Deathguard Dillinger acknowledges your valor and sends you to speak with Coleman Farthing in Brill to continue your training.",al={"after ulag","ulag quest follow up"}}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="This trial serves as an early proving ground for Forsaken warriors, testing your courage against a powerful, mind-controlled champion of the Scourge.",["race:Undead"]="Ulag's fate illustrates the horrifying reality of Scourge control, showing the tragic distinction between Forsaken who broke free and those whose minds remain enslaved to the Lich King."},kw={"brill","deathguard dillinger","dillinger","mausoleum","scourge","skull stone","ulag","ulag the cleaver"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","quest:1818","quest:1820","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1819},src={"Ulag the Cleaver (quest)"}}
E["quest:1820"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Coleman",z="tirisfal",s="Speak with Coleman is a transitional task in Tirisfal Glades offered to champions who have proven their worth against the Scourge. Deathguard Dillinger directs capable warriors from the town square to the local tavern to assist Coleman Farthing with personal and factional vendettas.",h="Speak with Coleman is a transitional task in Tirisfal Glades offered to champions who have proven their worth...",sec={{t="A Word from the Guard",b="After assisting in the containment of severe local threats—such as laying to rest dangerous Scourge remnants like Ulag the Cleaver—adventurers earn the personal trust of Deathguard Dillinger. As one of the sentinels watching the roads into Brill, Dillinger judges who is capable of handling more than routine perimeter patrols and points capable fighters toward citizens in need of specialized service.",sp=0},{t="A Private Vendetta",b="Not every conflict in Tirisfal Glades is fought on high command orders from the Undercity. Across the ruined kingdom of Lordaeron, surviving undead carry deep grudges tied to the lands, families, and fortunes they left behind. Coleman Farthing bides his time within the Gallow's End Tavern, seeking an instrument of vengeance to strike back at the threats lingering near former settlements like the Agamand Mills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Coleman Farthing?",a="Coleman Farthing waits inside the Gallow's End Tavern, located on the eastern side of the town of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"coleman farthing location","where is coleman farthing","find farthing brill"}},{q="Who sends you to talk to Coleman?",a="Deathguard Dillinger, who guards the entrance path into Brill, sends you to speak with Coleman after you prove your martial prowess.",al={"who gives speak with coleman","dillinger quest"}},{q="What kind of work does Coleman Farthing have?",a="Coleman seeks a capable combatant to serve as an instrument of revenge against the enemies of the Forsaken, specifically concerning matters around the old Agamand properties.",al={"what does coleman want","coleman farthing task"}},{q="What prerequisites are needed before receiving this task?",a="Deathguard Dillinger only refers you to Coleman once you have proven your loyalty and combat skill to the Forsaken by defeating Ulag the Cleaver.",al={"prereqs for speak with coleman","ulag requirement"}},{q="Does this mission grant substantial rewards directly?",a="This assignment simply connects you with Farthing in the tavern, opening up his personal line of requests rather than providing substantial gear or coin on its own.",al={"speak with coleman rewards","is it worth doing"}},{q="What is the Gallow's End Tavern?",a="The Gallow's End Tavern is the central inn of Brill, serving as a gathering spot, resting point, and informal center for private contracts among the local undead.",al={"brill tavern","gallows end tavern"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Many Forsaken hold personal grudges alongside their loyalty to the Dark Lady; Coleman Farthing's requests reflect how personal loss and national defense intertwine in Tirisfal.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers helping secure Lordaeron, connecting with local townsfolk in Brill provides vital footing for operations throughout Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"agamand","brill","coleman farthing","deathguard dillinger","forsaken","gallow's end tavern","horde","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","npc:coleman-farthing","quest:1821","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",["end"]="Coleman Farthing",level="10",faction="Horde",id=1820},src={"Speak with Coleman"}}
E["quest:1821"] = {t="quest",n="Agamand Heirlooms",z="tirisfal",s="Coleman Farthing tasks adventurers with plundering the Agamand Family Crypt at the northern end of Agamand Mills. Driven by bitter resentment over his mortal demise, he seeks to strip his former masters of their ancestral weapons and erase their final remnants of dignity.",h="Coleman Farthing tasks adventurers with plundering the Agamand Family Crypt at the northern end of Agamand...",sec={{t="A Servant's Bitter Grudge",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, Coleman Farthing served the wealthy and influential Agamand family at their expansive mills in Tirisfal Glades. Whatever occurred during the fall of their estate, Farthing blames his former lords entirely for his death. Now raised into undeath among the Forsaken, he views the Agamands' downfall with spiteful satisfaction, rejoicing that the once-proud dynasty has been reduced to mindless minions enslaved to the Lich King.",sp=0},{t="Desecrating the Crypt",b="To completely extinguish what remains of the family's prestige, Farthing sends adventurers into the Agamand Family Crypt nestled beneath the northern bluffs of the mills. Within its haunted stone halls, the restive dead wander alongside lingering Scourge. Farthing demands the extraction of four storied relics—the Agamand family sword, axe, dagger, and mace—ensuring their bloodline's legacy is stripped of every remaining shred of honor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Coleman Farthing in life?",a="Coleman Farthing was a retainer employed by the wealthy Agamand family at Agamand Mills prior to the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. He died during the calamity and blames his masters for his demise, harboring an intense resentment that carried over into his undeath.",al={"who is coleman farthing","coleman backstory","farthing history"}},{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want the heirlooms?",a="Farthing seeks complete vengeance against his former masters. By pillaging their ancestral sword, axe, dagger, and mace from the family tomb, he aims to strip the fallen lineage of its last vestiges of honor and memory.",al={"why steal heirlooms","coleman motive","why take weapons"}},{q="What happened to the Agamand family?",a="The Agamand family perished when the Scourge swept across Tirisfal Glades. Rather than finding peace in death, they were raised as mindless undead thralls bound to the will of the Lich King, wandering their ruined mills and crypt.",al={"agamand fate","are agamands alive","what are agamands now"}},{q="Where is the Agamand Family Crypt located?",a="The crypt lies at the northern edge of Agamand Mills, set into the rocky cliffs overlooking the blighted farmsteads in northern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"crypt location","where is crypt","agamand crypt map"}},{q="What weapons are kept within the crypt?",a="The crypt holds four distinct ancestral weapons belonging to the bloodline: the Agamand Family Sword, the Agamand Family Axe, the Agamand Family Dagger, and the Agamand Family Mace.",al={"which heirlooms","four heirlooms","agamand weapons"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken attacking the Agamands if both are undead?",a="The Forsaken possess free will and fight for their own survival, whereas the undead Agamands remain mindless slaves of the Scourge, serving the Lich King that the Forsaken despise.",al={"undead vs undead","why fight agamands","forsaken scourge conflict"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Coleman Farthing's bitter quest embodies the lingering grudges and unhealed wounds that many Forsaken carry from their mortal lives into undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing out the crypt undermines the Scourge's entrenched hold over northern Tirisfal Glades, making the realm safer for Horde travelers.",["class:Rogue"]="Slipping past lurking ghouls to pilfer ancient armaments from guarded burial vaults is second nature to stealthy operatives."},kw={"agamand family crypt","agamand heirlooms","agamand mills","coleman farthing","heirloom weapon","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","quest:1820"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",level="11",faction="Horde",id=1821},src={"Agamand Heirlooms"}}
E["quest:354"] = {t="quest",n="Deaths in the Family",z="tirisfal",s="Coleman Farthing, a former mill worker now dwelling in Brill, seeks personal vengeance against the aristocratic Agamand family. Convinced to stay and defend their estates against the Scourge during the Third War, Farthing and his fellow workers perished alongside their stubborn employers, only for the Agamands to rise as mindless thralls of the Lich King.",h="Coleman Farthing, a former mill worker now dwelling in Brill, seeks personal vengeance against the...",sec={{t="A Legacy of Pride",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, the Agamand family stood as the wealthiest and most influential agrarian dynasty in Tirisfal Glades. Their sprawling mills and fertile pastures produced bountiful grain, commanding the labor of dozens of tenant farmers and millers. When the Plague of Undeath crept across the kingdom, the Agamands refused to flee or abandon their ancestral holdings, convinced that stone walls and loyal workers could hold off the horrors advancing from the east.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Loyalty",b="Believing their lords' assurances, loyal employees like Coleman Farthing stood their ground to defend the estate. The defense proved futile against the Scourge's relentless onslaught. The Agamands and their workers were slaughtered, their bodies rotting where they fell before being raised into undeath. While Farthing eventually broke free through Sylvanas Windrunner's liberation, the Agamand patriarchs and heirs remained trapped under the Lich King's mental grip, wandering the ruined mills as mindless Scourge sentries.",sp=0},{t="Bitter Retribution",b="Now residing in Brill, Coleman Farthing harbors intense resentment toward the former masters whose arrogance cost him his mortal life. Seeking closure and retribution, he sends Forsaken champions to Agamand Mills to destroy Gregor, Nissa, and Thurman Agamand. Farthing openly hopes that behind their rotting visages, his former masters retained just enough consciousness to feel terror as their unlife was violently brought to an end.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was the Agamand family?",a="The Agamands were the wealthiest and most prosperous landowning family in Tirisfal Glades before the fall of Lordaeron. They owned and operated the vast Agamand Mills, employing numerous local farmers and millers.",al={"who are the agamands","agamand backstory","agamand mills history"}},{q="Why is Coleman Farthing so angry at them?",a="Farthing was employed at their mills in life. When the Scourge arrived, the Agamands convinced their workers to remain and fortify the estate rather than flee. Farthing views their aristocratic pride as the direct reason he and his peers died and became undead.",al={"coleman farthing grudge","why does farthing hate the agamands","farthing motive"}},{q="Did the Agamands join the Forsaken?",a="No. Unlike Coleman Farthing and the other free-willed Forsaken, the Agamands never broke free from the Lich King's control. They remain mindless Scourge minions haunting the ruined family mills.",al={"are agamands forsaken","why are the agamands scourge","who controls the agamands"}},{q="Which Agamand family members must be destroyed?",a="The quest tasks you with hunting down Gregor Agamand, Nissa Agamand, and Thurman Agamand, collecting their remains from the family estate to confirm their destruction.",al={"who do you kill","agamand targets","which agamands"}},{q="Where are Agamand Mills located?",a="Agamand Mills lies in the northern reaches of Tirisfal Glades, northwest of Brill. The once-fertile estate consists of several ruined windmills and farmhouses infested with Scourge.",al={"where is agamand mills","agamand location"}},{q="What does Coleman Farthing do with their remains?",a="Coleman asks for their remains purely to confirm their destruction. The trophy represents the closure of his mortal grudges and proof that the proud lords who doomed him have been permanently extinguished.",al={"why collect remains","farthing remains"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This task reflects the profound personal grudges many Forsaken still bear from their mortal lives, illustrating the lingering trauma of Lordaeron's fall and the bitterness toward those who led them to ruin.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing the Agamand leadership removes dangerous Scourge commanders lurking uncomfortably close to Brill and the Undercity's northern approaches."},kw={"agamand","agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","deaths in the family","gregor agamand","nissa agamand","scourge","thurman agamand","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",level="11",faction="Horde",id=354},src={"Deaths in the Family (Classic)"}}
E["quest:355"] = {t="quest",n="Speak with Sevren",z="tirisfal",s="Following the settling of Coleman Farthing's personal score at Agamand Mills, Magistrate Sevren summons the adventurer to Brill. The mills house far more than bitter family ghosts; they represent an active Scourge peril on the settlement's northern border.",h="Following the settling of Coleman Farthing's personal score at Agamand Mills, Magistrate Sevren summons the...",sec={{t="From Vengeance to Civic Duty",b="Coleman Farthing sought personal retribution against his former neighbors, the Agamands, sending travelers north to tear through the undead lurking about the flour mills. Once those remains were delivered, Coleman recognized that his private grudge intersected with a wider tactical problem: the entire Agamand estate remains swarming with mindlessly aggressive Scourge minions right on Brill's doorstep.",sp=0},{t="The Magistrate's Call",b="Magistrate Sevren oversees civic and military security in Brill for the Dark Lady. Impressed by reports of an adventurer capable of surviving deep incursions into the haunted farmlands, Sevren steps in to direct those capable hands toward the root of the infestation—the ancient Agamand family crypt itself.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Coleman Farthing send me to Magistrate Sevren?",a="Coleman satisfied his own vengeance against the resurrected Agamand family, but he knows the undead presence at the mills threatens all of Brill. He reported your combat prowess to Magistrate Sevren, who organizes local defense.",al={"why go to sevren","coleman farthing referral","who is magistrate sevren"}},{q="Where can Magistrate Sevren be found?",a="Magistrate Sevren is stationed in Brill, Tirisfal Glades, usually found standing outside the town hall directing local affairs for the Forsaken.",al={"sevren location","where is magistrate sevren","find sevren"}},{q="What threat do the Agamand Mills pose?",a="The mills lie just north of Brill and remain thoroughly infested by mindless Scourge. Left unchecked, the walking dead and restless spirits wandering the fields could easily overrun the town.",al={"agamand mills danger","why are mills a threat"}},{q="What happens after speaking with Magistrate Sevren?",a="Sevren enlists you for a direct strike into the Agamand Family Crypt to eliminate the deeper Scourge threat anchoring the undead to the mills.",al={"next quest after sevren","what does sevren want"}},{q="Does this quest require returning to the mills immediately?",a="This brief assignment is simply a bridge. You report to Sevren in Brill to conclude Coleman's lead before accepting your next mission into the crypt.",al={"do i go back to the mills","is this quest just talking"}},{q="Why does Brill care about the Agamand family?",a="In life, the Agamands were wealthy regional mill owners and prominent neighbors in Tirisfal. In death, their unhallowed estate serves as a fortified staging ground for mindless Scourge.",al={"agamand importance","who are the agamands to brill"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Proving capable against the mindless Scourge earns rapid recognition in Brill, moving you from freelance odd-jobs to direct civic defense under Magistrate Sevren.",["faction:Horde"]="Brill represents the first line of defense for the Undercity; securing the surrounding farmland from the Scourge is vital for the Horde's hold on northern Lordaeron."},kw={"agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","magistrate sevren","sevren","the family crypt","the haunted mills","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:coleman-farthing","quest:362","quest:408","subzone:brill","subzone:agamand-mills","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="10",faction="Horde",id=355},src={"Speak with Sevren (Classic)"}}
E["quest:356"] = {t="quest",n="Rear Guard Patrol",z="tirisfal",s="Rear Guard Patrol is a military scouting mission tasked by Deathguard Linnea to protect the Forsaken defenses along Tirisfal's eastern border. It directs operatives to purge stray Scourge horrors and lingering spirits haunting the Balnir Farmstead before they can compromise the supply lines supporting the Bulwark.",h="Rear Guard Patrol is a military scouting mission tasked by Deathguard Linnea to protect the Forsaken defenses...",sec={{t="Securing the Bulwark's Flank",b="The Bulwark stands as the primary bulwark holding back the pestilence and armies of the Western Plaguelands from spilling into Tirisfal Glades. Deathguard Linnea oversees rear-echelon security along this frontier. Because the line cannot afford to divide its forces against ambushes from behind, any undead that bypass the choke point must be destroyed before they can sever the supply lines feeding the front.",sp=0},{t="The Ruins of Balnir Farmstead",b="Once famous across Lordaeron for breeding prize royal steeds, the Balnir Farmstead fell to ruin during the Third War. Now thoroughly blighted, the overgrown fields and crumbling stables provide cover for interloping Bleeding Horrors and restless, Wandering Spirits. Clearing the site denies the Lich King a staging post inside Tirisfal itself and safeguards the road for Horde reinforcements.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this patrol important for the Bulwark?",a="The Bulwark holds the narrow border pass against the Western Plaguelands. If wandering Scourge flank the fortification or settle behind it, the defenders would be caught in a two-front battle and lose the supply lines connecting them to Brill and the Undercity.",al={"why do rear guard patrol","bulwark importance","why secure balnir"}},{q="Who orders this mission?",a="Deathguard Linnea, an officer stationed near the road leading east into the Plaguelands, assigns the patrol and forwards reports of success to Executor Zygand.",al={"who gives rear guard patrol","deathguard linnea"}},{q="What creatures haunt the Balnir Farmstead?",a="The blighted farmstead crawls with Bleeding Horrors—reanimated corpses stitched together by necromancy—and Wandering Spirits of former inhabitants who died during the Scourge's initial conquest.",al={"balnir farmstead mobs","what monsters are at balnir","bleeding horror"}},{q="What was the Balnir Farmstead before the plague?",a="Before the Third War, the Balnir family bred prized horses renowned throughout the Kingdom of Lordaeron, including the noble steeds favored by Lordaeron's royalty and chivalry.",al={"balnir lore","what was balnir farmstead","balnir history"}},{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is a senior Forsaken military commander responsible for operations along Tirisfal's eastern frontier and the defense of the Bulwark.",al={"executor zygand lore","who is zygand"}},{q="Why don't the Forsaken just abandon the eastern border?",a="Abandoning the Bulwark would open all of Tirisfal Glades and the gates of the Undercity directly to the endless hordes of the Scourge marching from the Plaguelands.",al={"why defend the bulwark","why fight at the border"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, safeguarding the Bulwark's rear is a matter of sheer survival; breaking the Scourge's presence at Balnir Farmstead keeps the homelands free from the Lich King's renewed grasp.",["faction:Horde"]="Holding Tirisfal's eastern perimeter ensures the Horde maintains its tenuous foothold in the northern Eastern Kingdoms against the undead legions."},kw={"balnir","bleeding horror","bulwark","linnea","scourge","tirisfal","wandering spirit","zygand"},rel={"npc:deathguard-linnea","subzone:balnir-farmstead","subzone:bulwark","npc:executor-zygand","quest:1882","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Linnea",level="11",faction="Horde",id=356},src={"Rear Guard Patrol"}}
E["quest:358"] = {t="quest",n="Graverobbers",z="tirisfal",s="Magistrate Sevren of Brill tasks adventurers with purging Rot Hide gnolls from the Mass Grave southwest of Garren's Haunt. These undead beasts were sent by the Scourge to dig up the corpses of early plague victims to swell their ranks. Slaying them and recovering their embalming ichor protects the fallen and aids the Royal Apothecary Society's research.",h="Magistrate Sevren of Brill tasks adventurers with purging Rot Hide gnolls from the Mass Grave southwest of...",sec={{t="Desecration of the Mass Graves",b="When the Plague of Undeath first tore through Tirisfal Glades, the dead piled up faster than formal burials could accommodate. Immense mass graves were dug across the north to contain the staggering loss. Until recently, those buried remains escaped resurrection. Now, however, the Scourge has unleashed Rot Hide gnolls upon the trenches southwest of Garren's Haunt, sending them to exhumate the decayed remains to reinforce the Lich King's armies.",sp=0},{t="Turning Scourge Alchemy Inward",b="The Rot Hides are sustained by embalming ichor, an alchemical concoction that preserves and animates their rotting frames. By commanding scouts to slay the graverobbers and extract this fluid, Magistrate Sevren strikes two blows at once: halting the Scourge's harvest of raw bodies and delivering valuable biological specimens directly to the apothecaries in Brill, who seek to turn the Lich King's own craft against him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scourge digging up the Mass Grave?",a="The Mass Grave holds countless victims from the initial arrival of the Plague in Tirisfal. The Scourge intends to unearth these preserved bodies to raise new soldiers and swell their armies against the Forsaken.",al={"why are gnolls digging corpses","what does the scourge want with bodies","mass grave purpose"}},{q="What are the Rot Hide gnolls?",a="They are undead gnolls enslaved by the Scourge. Animated and preserved using alchemical embalming ichor, they serve as scavengers and shock troops around Garren's Haunt and the neighboring graves.",al={"rot hide lore","undead gnolls tirisfal","what are rot hides"}},{q="Where is the Mass Grave located?",a="The Mass Grave lies southwest of Garren's Haunt, in the northern hills of Tirisfal Glades, just north of Brill.",al={"where are graverobbers","mass grave location","garren's haunt mass grave"}},{q="What do the Forsaken want with the Embalming Ichor?",a="Magistrate Sevren hands the collected ichor over to Forsaken apothecaries to study how the Scourge animates and maintains its lesser thralls, searching for weaknesses to exploit in the ongoing war.",al={"why collect embalming ichor","what is ichor for","ichor lore"}},{q="Who orders the death of the Graverobbers?",a="Magistrate Sevren, the Forsaken overseer of Brill, issues the bounty to defend Tirisfal's borders and secure useful reagents for the Apothecaries.",al={"who gives graverobbers","magistrate sevren role"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken care if dead plague victims are raised?",a="Every corpse claimed and raised by the Scourge becomes an enemy soldier marching under the Lich King's will, directly threatening the newly liberated Forsaken kingdom.",al={"why do forsaken protect graves","why care about dead bodies"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, preventing the Scourge from raising Tirisfal's former citizens spares their fallen countrymen the horrific fate of mindless servitude.",["faction:Horde"]="Halting the Scourge's resupply efforts secures northern Lordaeron, strengthening the Horde's foothold against the Lich King's remaining forces."},kw={"brill","embalming ichor","garren's haunt","graverobbers","magistrate sevren","mass grave","rot hide","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:garren-s-haunt","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",level="8",faction="Horde",id=358},src={"Graverobbers (Classic)"}}
E["quest:360"] = {t="quest",n="Return to the Magistrate",z="tirisfal",s="Return to the Magistrate concludes an urgent reconnaissance dispatch between the eastern border of Tirisfal Glades and the town of Brill. Having reported to Deathguard Linnea at the Bulwark, adventurers are sent back to deliver troubling news directly to Magistrate Sevren. The message confirms that the mindless minions of the Lich King continue to test the borders of the young Forsaken nation.",h="Return to the Magistrate concludes an urgent reconnaissance dispatch between the eastern border of Tirisfal...",sec={{t="Frontier Reports",b="The eastern road out of Tirisfal Glades leads directly into the blighted ruins of the Western Plaguelands, where the Scourge holds devastating sway. To keep the undead hordes from spilling over into their newly claimed homeland, the Forsaken established the Bulwark—a fortified checkpoint garrisoned by grim sentries like Deathguard Linnea. After reviewing the defenses and learning what presses against the eastern gate, Linnea sends messengers racing back west along the King's Road toward Brill before enemy infiltrators can capitalize on any gaps.",sp=0},{t="Sevren's Vow",b="When Magistrate Sevren receives the dispatch in Brill, it confirms his worst fears: Scourge scouts are finding pathways around or through the frontline perimeter. For the Forsaken, every creeping ghoul and mindless skeleton is not merely a military nuisance, but a reminder of the enslavement they broke free from during the fall of Lordaeron. Sevren remains adamant that no matter how ceaseless the Lich King's onslaught becomes, the free undead will never surrender their newfound autonomy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this report come from?",a="The report comes from Deathguard Linnea, stationed at the Bulwark along the eastern boundary of Tirisfal Glades. She guards the barricades separating Tirisfal from the Scourge-choked Western Plaguelands.",al={"quest origin","who sent this report","where is linnea"}},{q="Why is Magistrate Sevren concerned about this news?",a="The dispatch informs Sevren that Scourge forces have managed to slip past the Bulwark's fortifications. For the Forsaken in Brill, enemy incursions threaten their fledgling towns and serve as a constant reminder of the Lich King's efforts to reclaim them.",al={"why is sevren worried","what does the report say","scourge threat"}},{q="Who is Magistrate Sevren?",a="Magistrate Sevren is the civil administrator of Brill. Operating out of the town hall, he oversees local defenses, infrastructure, and the mobilization of newly raised Forsaken citizens across central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"sevren lore","who is the magistrate"}},{q="What is the Bulwark?",a="The Bulwark is a fortified outpost constructed along the main thoroughfare between Tirisfal Glades and the Western Plaguelands. It serves as the primary barrier preventing Scourge incursions into Forsaken lands.",al={"bulwark lore","eastern border tirisfal"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken hate the Scourge so much?",a="The Forsaken were once mindless thralls of the Scourge, slaughtered in life and raised in undeath to butcher their own kin. Having regained their free will, they despise the Lich King and fear losing their minds to his control once again.",al={"forsaken vs scourge","why hate lich king"}},{q="What path does this message travel?",a="Messengers travel west along the main road from the Bulwark, skirting the northern edge of the Balnir Farmstead and heading through central Tirisfal Glades until reaching the town center of Brill.",al={"route from bulwark to brill","road to brill"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Carrying intelligence from the Bulwark brings home the precarious reality of Forsaken freedom: the master you escaped still clawing at the doorstep of your new home.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms relies on the stability of Tirisfal Glades, making the Bulwark's defenses critical against the undead horrors of the Plaguelands."},kw={"brill","bulwark","forsaken duties","linnea","scourge","sevren","tirisfal"},rel={"subzone:brill","subzone:bulwark","npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:deathguard-linnea","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Linnea",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="9",faction="Horde",id=360},src={"Return to the Magistrate (Classic)"}}
E["quest:361"] = {t="quest",n="A Letter Undelivered",z="tirisfal",s="A faded, bloodstained missive found among the skeletal ruins of Agamand Mills, addressed to Yvette Farthing. It reveals a tragic parting between two lovers as the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, offering a glimpse into what the Forsaken left behind when they traded life for undeath.",h="A faded, bloodstained missive found among the skeletal ruins of Agamand Mills, addressed to Yvette Farthing.",sec={{t="A Message Lost in the Fall",b="Written by Thurman Agamand, the eldest son of patriarch Gregor Agamand, this unsent parchment never reached its intended recipient before the family estate collapsed into ruin. When the Plague of Undeath consumed Tirisfal Glades, Thurman refused to abandon his ancestral home and kin. Amid the horrors of the onslaught, he took up quill to write one last message to Yvette Farthing, whom he had loved before the kingdom turned to ash.",sp=0},{t="The Severed Bond",b="When the letter is finally placed into Yvette Farthing's hands at the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, it provokes a brief, agonizing flash of memory. She remembers begging Thurman to flee Agamand Mills alongside her and her father, and she laments that Thurman's brother, Brand, bore ill will toward him. Yet the warmth is fleeting. Like so many of the Forsaken, Yvette steels her heart, casting aside mortal remorse and declaring that love has no place in her new existence.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who wrote this letter?",a="The letter was penned by Thurman Agamand, the eldest son of Gregor Agamand. Thurman perished defending his family's mills against the Scourge alongside the rest of his cursed household.",al={"author","thurman agamand","who is thurman"}},{q="Who is Yvette Farthing?",a="Yvette Farthing is a Forsaken woman currently residing inside the tavern in Brill. In life, she and her father fled the countryside before the Scourge, leaving behind her lover, Thurman Agamand.",al={"yvette","who is yvette","recipient"}},{q="Where did the letter come from?",a="The letter is recovered from the walking skeletons prowling the devastated grounds and fields of Agamand Mills in western Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where to find letter","letter drop","letter location"}},{q="What happened between Thurman and Yvette?",a="They were lovers before the Third War. Yvette begged Thurman to abandon his family's mills and escape with her, but Thurman chose loyalty to his kin and remained behind to face the Plague.",al={"thurman and yvette","yvette backstory","what happened to them"}},{q="What does Yvette do when she reads the letter?",a="She grieves briefly for Thurman and curses both the Scourge and his brother Brand, but quickly suppresses her emotions. She insists that regrets are for the weak and that romance has no place in her Forsaken existence.",al={"yvette reaction","what does yvette say"},sp=1},{q="Who is Brand Agamand?",a="Brand was Thurman's brother. According to Yvette, Brand harbored deep resentment and ill intent toward Thurman even before the estate fell to the Plague.",al={"brand","brand agamand","who is brand"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The letter embodies the sharp, painful division between a Forsaken's mortal memories and their cold, purpose-driven existence under the Banshee Queen.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers visiting Brill, this recovered parchment offers a stark demonstration of the emotional detachment that defines the Forsaken people."},kw={"agamand","brill","farthing","letter","scourge","tavern","thurman","undelivered","yvette"},rel={"npc:yvette-farthing","subzone:agamand-mills","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","npc:farthing"},m={start="A Letter to Yvette",["end"]="Yvette Farthing",level="7",faction="Horde",id=361},src={"A Letter Undelivered"}}
E["quest:362"] = {t="quest",n="The Haunted Mills",z="tirisfal",s="Coleman Farthing of Brill seeks vengeance against his former landowners, the Agamands, by having their restless undead remains collected and destroyed. This task sends you north to Agamand Mills to put down Devlin Agamand, the sharp-tongued younger son of the estate. It begins a bitter vendetta against the family who failed to protect Tirisfal's common folk from the Plague.",h="Coleman Farthing of Brill seeks vengeance against his former landowners, the Agamands, by having their...",sec={{t="A Bitter Harvest",b="Before the Third War, Agamand Mills stood as the breadbasket of northern Tirisfal, owned by a wealthy landed family. When the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, the common folk looked to the noble landowners for safety, only to find neither sanctuary nor salvation. Coleman Farthing survived in undeath, but his heart remains consumed by hatred for the family he served. Rather than letting them roam in eternal torment, Farthing desires the morbid satisfaction of collecting their bones to desecrate them under his own heel.",sp=0},{t="The Younger Brother",b="Devlin Agamand was the younger brother of Thurman Agamand. In life, Devlin was widely remembered as a weak, spiteful, and sharp-tongued youth who stood in stark contrast to his gentle elder brother. When the Plague of Undeath crept into the mill estate, Devlin was among the quickest to fall prey to the corruption. Now, stripped of whatever fragile wit he possessed in life, his mindless corpse chatters incessantly along the northern road leading into the family mills.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Coleman Farthing want Devlin's remains?",a="Coleman Farthing blames the wealthy Agamand family for abandoning and failing him and his relatives when the Scourge overran Lordaeron. Seeking personal revenge in undeath, he wants to gather the Agamand bones so he can display them on his mantle and personally grind them into dust.",al={"why coleman want bones","coleman farthing motive","why kill devlin"}},{q="Where can Devlin Agamand be found?",a="Devlin wanders near the road just south of the Agamand Mills in northern Tirisfal Glades, gibbering madly among the undead that prowl the outskirts of the estate.",al={"devlin location","find devlin agamand","where is devlin"}},{q="What was Devlin like before the Plague?",a="According to Coleman Farthing, Devlin was the smaller, weaker, and distinctly sharp-tongued younger son of the Agamand household, very unlike his tall and mild-mannered older brother Thurman.",al={"who was devlin","devlin agamand lore","devlin agamand in life"}},{q="Is Devlin part of the Scourge or Forsaken?",a="Devlin is a mindless thrall of the Scourge. Unlike the Forsaken of the Undercity, he never broke free of the Lich King's grip and mindlessly stalks his family's ruined lands.",al={"is devlin scourge","devlin faction"}},{q="What other quests take place at Agamand Mills?",a="The quest 'Deaths in the Family' also directs Forsaken adventurers to Agamand Mills to eliminate the rest of the Agamand household, making it natural to pursue both tasks concurrently.",al={"agamand mills quests","quests near devlin"}},{q="What happens after turning in Devlin's remains?",a="After accepting the bones, Coleman Farthing directs you to speak with Sevren in Brill, which eventually leads deeper into the Agamand family crypt.",al={"quest continuation","next quest after haunted mills"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This task reflects the deep class resentments that survived Lordaeron's fall, showing how Forsaken retain mortal grudges against the landed nobility who failed to protect them from the Plague.",["faction:Horde"]="Assisting the Forsaken in Tirisfal means helping them purge dangerous pockets of the Scourge from the borders of Brill and Undercity."},kw={"agamand mills","brill","coleman farthing","devlin agamand","haunted mills","plague","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:coleman-farthing","subzone:agamand-mills","quest:354","quest:355","quest:408","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Coleman Farthing",level="10",faction="Horde",id=362},src={"The Haunted Mills (Classic)"}}
E["quest:365"] = {t="quest",n="Fields of Grief",z="tirisfal",s="Fields of Grief is an early Forsaken mission assigned by Deathguard Simmer along the road north of Deathknell. It tasks fledglings with raiding a living human farmstead to harvest Tirisfal pumpkins for the Royal Apothecary Society in Brill.",h="Fields of Grief is an early Forsaken mission assigned by Deathguard Simmer along the road north of Deathknell.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Survival",b="For new Forsaken adventurers freshly risen from the crypts of Deathknell, stepping onto the misty roads of Tirisfal Glades is an immediate lesson in hostility. Deathguard Simmer represents the pragmatic malice of Sylvanas Windrunner's forces: survival means seizing what the living possess and turning it toward the Undercity's darker endeavors.",sp=0},{t="Raiding the Living",b="The targets of the raid are the mortal human farmers attempting to work the blighted soil west of the road, north of Deathknell. Described by the Deathguard as infesting the realm like mold on a corpse, these peasants cling to their homesteads under the uneasy protection of nearby Scarlet Crusade towers. Snatching their crops deals a spiteful blow to their supplies while feeding the Royal Apothecary Society's endless demand for reagents.",sp=0},{t="Supplies for the Society",b="The stolen pumpkins are delivered directly to Apothecary Johaan, who conducts experimental research on the outskirts of Brill. The Royal Apothecary Society frequently uses local agricultural produce and flora as bases for alchemical brews, poisons, and plague research intended to secure the Forsaken's precarious foothold in northern Lordaeron.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Fields of Grief?",a="Deathguard Simmer gives the quest. He is stationed guarding the road in southern Tirisfal Glades, just north of the exit path leading from Deathknell.",al={"quest giver","fields of grief quest starter","who starts fields of grief"}},{q="Where do I take the Tirisfal Pumpkins?",a="You deliver the ten pumpkins to Apothecary Johaan, located outside the town of Brill further north in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where to turn in pumpkins","pumpkin turn in","fields of grief hand in"}},{q="Why are there living humans farming in Tirisfal Glades?",a="These human peasants are remnants of Lordaeron's original population who survived the Third War and the Scourge plague. They stubbornly cling to their homesteads in the shadow of nearby Scarlet Crusade guard posts, resisting Forsaken dominion.",al={"why humans here","living humans tirisfal","why are humans in undead zone"}},{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want pumpkins?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society utilizes various plants, blighted crops, and biological matter as testing agents and base components for their alchemical mixtures, poisons, and experimental plagues.",al={"why pumpkins","what are pumpkins for","apothecary johaan pumpkins"}},{q="Who patrols near the farmstead?",a="Zealots of the Scarlet Crusade patrol down from their watchtower nearby, defending the human settlement and attempting to purge any undead that approach the fields.",al={"scarlet crusade near farm","who protects the farm"}},{q="What comes after Fields of Grief?",a="After turning in the pumpkins, Apothecary Johaan immediately gives a follow-up quest of the same name, sending you back out to collect more sinister research components from the local wildlife.",al={"next quest","fields of grief followup","what is after fields of grief"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This task marks your first military assignment outside Deathknell, proving your willingness to strip your former mortal kin of their livelihood to advance the Royal Apothecary Society.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Tirisfal Glades requires breaking the lingering human presence and dismantling the Scarlet Crusade's influence along the southern roadways.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Apothecaries rely heavily on the twisted flora of Tirisfal to formulate their deadly concoctions, making every local root and crop a reagent of war."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","deathguard simmer","deathknell","fields of grief","royal apothecary society","scarlet crusade","tirisfal pumpkin"},rel={"npc:deathguard-simmer","npc:apothecary-johaan","subzone:brill","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade"},m={start="Deathguard Simmer",["end"]="Apothecary Johaan",level="7",faction="Horde",id=365},src={"Fields of Grief (Classic)"}}
E["quest:366"] = {t="quest",n="Return the Book",z="tirisfal",s="Bethor Iceshard enchants Gunther Arcanus's stolen spellbook to prove his own freedom and recruit his former Kirin Tor colleague to the Forsaken cause. Taking the tome back to Gunther's island retreat reveals that neither former wizard is a thrall to the Lich King.",h="Bethor Iceshard enchants Gunther Arcanus's stolen spellbook to prove his own freedom and recruit his former...",sec={{t="A Message in Arcane Ink",b="After discovering that the renegade necromancer on Brightwater Lake was his old companion Gunther Arcanus, Bethor Iceshard devised an ingenious method of communication. Having previously ordered the theft of Gunther's spellbook to uncover the necromancer's identity, Bethor weaves an intricate dweomer into its pages. Rather than a demand or an armed parley, the enchantment serves as an arcane signature, proving that Bethor is not only active in Lordaeron, but completely liberated from the Lich King's mental yoke.",sp=0},{t="The Old Circle of Dalaran",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, Bethor Iceshard, Gunther Arcanus, and Thule Ravenclaw were fellow students and friends within the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. All three succumbed to the horrors of the Plague, but their paths diverged sharply in death. Thule embraced the Scourge and continues to serve the Lich King, while Bethor broke free alongside Queen Sylvanas. Believing Gunther was either dead or enslaved, Bethor's realization that Gunther also achieved self-willed undeath sparked an urgent effort to draw him into the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="Mistrust on the Island",b="When approached on his solitary island, Gunther initially lashes out in fury, assuming anyone trespassing on Brightwater Lake is an agent of the Scourge seeking to re-enslave him or the thief who plundered his magic. The sight of his personal grimoire, accompanied by Bethor's familiar magical resonance, catches the solitary mage off guard. Recognizing that someone from his mortal past broke the Scourge's shackles forces Gunther to reconsider his absolute isolation.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why did Bethor enchant Gunther's spellbook?",a="Bethor enchanted the stolen grimoire with a personal magical signature to prove to Gunther that he was truly free from the Lich King. Knowing Gunther's deep paranoia and hatred of the Scourge, a mundane messenger would have been rejected or destroyed on sight.",al={"why enchant the book","gunthers book spell","what did bethor do to the book"}},{q="Who was Gunther Arcanus before he died?",a="Gunther Arcanus was a human mage and scholar of the Kirin Tor in Dalaran. He studied alongside Bethor Iceshard and Thule Ravenclaw before the Third War, eventually falling victim to the Scourge's Plague of Undeath.",al={"who is gunther arcanus","gunther backstory","gunther lore"}},{q="Why is Gunther hiding on Brightwater Lake?",a="After breaking free from the Lich King's control, Gunther believed he was entirely alone in his freedom. He secluded himself on an island in Brightwater Lake to avoid being hunted down and re-enslaved by the Scourge or killed by living enemies.",al={"why is gunther on the island","gunthers retreat lore","why did gunther leave"}},{q="Who is Thule Ravenclaw?",a="Thule Ravenclaw was the third member of Bethor and Gunther's circle of Kirin Tor students in Dalaran. Unlike Bethor and Gunther, who broke their shackles, Thule willingly remains a loyal necromancer serving the Scourge in Silverpine Forest.",al={"who is thule","thule ravenclaw lore","third friend"}},{q="Why does Gunther think the player is a thief?",a="Earlier on, Bethor instructed Forsaken adventurers to sneak into Gunther's sanctum and steal his spellbook so Bethor could verify who was practicing necromancy on the lake. Gunther correctly recognizes the returning adventurer as the person who robbed him.",al={"why does gunther call me a thief","did i steal gunthers book","stolen book"}},{q="Does Gunther immediately join the Forsaken?",a="Not right away. While stunned to learn Bethor lives and possesses free will, Gunther remains skeptical of the Forsaken and requires a demonstration of loyalty against his former friend-turned-Scourge necromancer, Thule Ravenclaw, before fully committing.",al={"does gunther join sylvanas","gunther allegience","what happens next with gunther"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Gunther's plight mirrors the foundational struggle of the Forsaken: waking from the nightmare of mindless servitude only to face an isolated, hostile world.",["class:Mage"]="This exchange highlights the deep bonds among former Kirin Tor magi, who continue to recognize one another's distinct magical signatures across the veil of undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="Recruiting independent undead sorcerers like Gunther bolsters Undercity's arcane strength against both the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","dalaran","gunther arcanus","gunther's retreat","gunther's spellbook","kirin tor","return the book","thule ravenclaw","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","npc:bethor-iceshard","quest:357","quest:409","subzone:gunther-s-retreat","quest:446","subzone:dalaran","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Bethor Iceshard",["end"]="Gunther Arcanus",level="8",faction="Horde",id=366},src={"Return the Book"}}
E["quest:367"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="A New Plague is an introductory task in Brill that reveals the Forsaken's overarching strategic ambition. Apothecary Johaan tasks recruits with harvesting the blood of wild darkhounds to lay the groundwork for a virulent pathogen commissioned directly by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",h="A New Plague is an introductory task in Brill that reveals the Forsaken's overarching strategic ambition.",sec={{t="A Royal Mandate",b="In the damp village of Brill, Apothecary Johaan works on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society under a mandate directly from the Dark Lady. Sylvanas Windrunner has charged her alchemists with crafting a disease unlike anything Azeroth has ever seen. While the original plague of undeath served the Lich King by slaughtering humanity and binding their souls, this new creation is explicitly designed to annihilate Arthas Menethil and lay waste to his Scourge legions.",sp=0},{t="Raw Ingredients",b="Developing a biological weapon capable of destroying the undead requires grim experimentation. Johaan believes that the blood of indigenous beasts, starting with the fierce darkhounds roaming the gloom of Tirisfal Glades, holds vital chemical properties. By harvesting vials of this tainted animal blood, Johaan begins isolating elements to test whether the natural resilience and predatory biology of native creatures can catalyze a lethal contagion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of the new plague?",a="Lady Sylvanas tasked the Royal Apothecary Society with brewing a disease deadlier than any other on Azeroth. Its primary strategic objective is the complete destruction of Arthas and his Scourge army.",al={"why make a new plague","purpose of new plague","what does the plague do"}},{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Johaan is a member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in the town of Brill. He handles early field experiments, testing biological compounds gathered from Tirisfal's local fauna.",al={"who is johaan","apothecary johaan lore"}},{q="Why does Johaan need darkhound blood?",a="Johaan's research indicates that the blood of native beasts may serve as a crucial foundation for his alchemical formulas. He needs darkhound blood to test his preliminary theories in the laboratory.",al={"why darkhound blood","what is the blood for"}},{q="How does this plague differ from the Scourge's plague?",a="The original Plague of Undeath was designed by the Lich King to slaughter the living and raise them as thralls. Sylvanas's new plague is specifically engineered as a weapon intended to bring ruin to Arthas's undead legions.",al={"difference between plagues","scourge plague vs forsaken plague"}},{q="Who ordered the creation of this plague?",a="Lady Sylvanas Windrunner directly commanded the Royal Apothecary Society to invent it, believing that Forsaken alchemy combined with newfound magic is the key to defeating Arthas.",al={"who started the plague research","who wants the plague"}},{q="What happens after gathering the blood?",a="Gathering darkhound blood is only the first step of an ongoing series of experiments. Johaan uses the samples to begin refining the pathogen through further field tests across the Glades.",al={"what is the next step","does the plague work"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This quest marks your first direct contribution to the Royal Apothecary Society's master project: creating the weapon that Sylvanas plans to wield against Arthas.",["faction:Horde"]="While the Forsaken have joined the Horde, their alchemical endeavors in Tirisfal focus entirely on a grim biological weapon aimed at Northrend."},kw={"apothecary","arthas","brill","darkhound","johaan","plague","scourge","sylvanas","tirisfal"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","topic:royal-apothecary-society","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",level="6",faction="Horde",id=367},src={"A New Plague"}}
E["quest:368"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="Tasked by Apothecary Johaan in Brill, this errand requires gathering scales from the local Vile Fin murlocs prowling the Tirisfal coast. The Royal Apothecary Society aims to harness unique biological reagents to refine their budding new contagion, ensuring it can spread beyond isolated victims to engulf larger populations.",h="Tasked by Apothecary Johaan in Brill, this errand requires gathering scales from the local Vile Fin murlocs...",sec={{t="Scaling Up the Contagion",b="Poisoning a single target is simple alchemy, but formulating a plague capable of sweeping across entire lands demands more complex components. Apothecary Johaan's ongoing research in Brill hinges on creating a disease that can self-propagate and endure in the wild. To engineer this transmissibility, he turns his attention toward the shoreline wildlife of Tirisfal Glades, identifying the resilient biology of the coastal Vile Fin murlocs as a promising source of raw material.",sp=0},{t="The Vile Fin Reagents",b="The northern and western shores of Tirisfal Glades are plagued by aggressive murloc tribes known as the Vile Fin. Harvesting their scales provides Johaan with organic compounds adapted to damp, harsh conditions. By incorporating the murlocs' slick, resilient scales into his developing cauldron, the apothecary seeks to bolster the virulence and environmental stability of the Royal Apothecary Society's new plague.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the goal of Apothecary Johaan's research?",a="Johaan is developing a new plague on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society and Lady Sylvanas. His goal goes far beyond crafting simple toxins; he is working on a contagion designed to spread across entire populations and lands, targeting both the living and the Scourge.",al={"why make a new plague","johaan plague goal","what is johaan doing"}},{q="Why does Johaan need murloc scales specifically?",a="Johaan discovered during his initial brewing that simple poisons lack the biological complexity to spread effectively. The tough, slime-coated scales of the Vile Fin murlocs provide specific biological compounds needed to refine the contagion's ability to survive in the wild and transmit between hosts.",al={"why murloc scales","vile fin scale purpose","why scales for plague"}},{q="Where can the Vile Fin murlocs be found?",a="The Vile Fin murlocs inhabit the coasts of Tirisfal Glades, primarily concentrated along the northern beaches bordering the Great Sea and along the western shores near Brightwater Lake.",al={"where are murlocs tirisfal","vile fin location","murloc spots"}},{q="Who does Apothecary Johaan answer to?",a="Apothecary Johaan is an operative of the Royal Apothecary Society, an alchemical guild headquartered in the Undercity under Grand Apothecary Putress and answering directly to Queen Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who leads the apothecaries","johaan boss","royal apothecary society leader"}},{q="What is the next step in this quest chain?",a="After bringing the Vile Fin scales to Johaan, he continues refining the formula, which requires sourcing further biological components and eventually putting the newly brewed strain to the test.",al={"what comes next","after vile fin scales","next plague quest"}},{q="Are the Forsaken concerned about using murloc parts?",a="Not at all. The Royal Apothecary Society is notoriously pragmatic and amoral, readily harvesting parts from whatever local flora, fauna, or beasts yield the biochemical traits needed for their experiments.",al={"murloc alchemy dangerous","why harvest murlocs"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, helping Apothecary Johaan is a direct contribution to their race's ultimate weapon and defense: the creation of a deadly plague engineered specifically to protect their sovereign realm and destroy their foes.",["faction:Horde"]="While Forsaken apothecaries pursue these dark concoctions openly in Tirisfal Glades, knowledge of the plague's full intent and potency remains a delicate matter kept mostly quiet from their less ruthless allies in the Horde."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","murloc","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades","vile fin scale"},rel={"quest:367","npc:apothecary-johaan","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:murloc"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",level="9",faction="Horde",id=368},src={"A New Plague (2)"}}
E["quest:369"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan turns his attention toward developing a potent new biological agent for the Forsaken. By studying ancient texts, he discovers that a historic, deadly plague survived through the venom of eastern Tirisfal's night web spiders, prompting an urgent retrieval effort.",h="In Brill, Apothecary Johaan turns his attention toward developing a potent new biological agent for the...",sec={{t="Unearthing Ancient Contagions",b="While pursuing his alchemy for the Royal Apothecary Society in Brill, Apothecary Johaan scours aged tomes in search of deadlier mixtures. He uncovers records of an ancient pestilence that once ravaged thousands of lives. Crucially, the texts indicate that the deadly pathogen survived across generations by harboring within the local arachnids of Tirisfal Glades, making their venom an invaluable biological reagent.",sp=0},{t="Hunting the Venomweb Vale",b="To acquire a viable sample of the pathogen, Johaan directs agents toward the eastern reaches of Tirisfal Glades. South of the Scarlet Monastery lies Venomweb Vale, a fog-shrouded hollow infested with vicious night web spiders. Harvesters must venture into their dens to extract fresh venom glands, securing the final ingredient needed to finalize Johaan's experimental brew.",sp=0},{t="Brewing the Final Formulation",b="Upon receiving the harvested venom, Johaan incorporates it into a simmering cauldron alongside previously gathered reagents. With the mixture boiled down and primed, the contagious element from the spiders completes the compound, bringing the Royal Apothecary Society one step closer to practical field trials.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan want spider venom?",a="Johaan uncovered an old text describing an ancient plague that killed thousands, whose virulent strain was naturally preserved in the venom of Tirisfal's night web spiders. He intends to harness that contagious element for his concoction.",al={"why spider venom","apothecary johaan spiders","spider venom use"}},{q="Where do the vicious night web spiders live?",a="They dwell in eastern Tirisfal Glades within Venomweb Vale, located just south of the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"where are night web spiders","night web spider location","venomweb vale location"}},{q="What is the goal of the Royal Apothecary Society's research here?",a="The society seeks to synthesize a lethal new strain capable of exterminating both the Scourge and the living, cementing the Forsaken's survival and independence in Lordaeron.",al={"why make a new plague","forsaken plague goals","royal apothecary society plague"}},{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Johaan is a Forsaken researcher stationed in Brill under the Royal Apothecary Society. He oversees local chemical and biological experiments, blending dark alchemy with field-harvested Tirisfal reagents.",al={"who is johaan","apothecary johaan lore"}},{q="What happens after this venom is gathered?",a="Once Johaan boils the venom down into his brew, he prepares to test the compound directly to determine if the resulting toxic agent produces the desired lethality.",al={"what happens next","new plague quest sequel","after a new plague 3"},sp=1},{q="Is this the same plague that created the Scourge?",a="No. The Scourge spread the Plague of Undeath created by the Lich King. The Forsaken's apothecaries are deliberately formulating an entirely distinct biological weapon of their own design.",al={"is this scourge plague","plague of undeath difference"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, crafting an original weapon offers the only lasting security against relentless Scourge remnants and Scarlet crusaders on their doorstep.",["faction:Horde"]="While Forsaken researchers welcome assistance from orc or tauren allies, the visceral nature of their biological experiments frequently unsettles the wider Horde."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","night web spider","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades","venom","venomweb vale"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","subzone:brill","subzone:venomweb-vale","zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","quest:367"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",level="11",faction="Horde",id=369},src={"A New Plague (3)"}}
E["quest:370"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="Executor Zygand directs Forsaken champions to strike down Captain Perrine and her garrison stationed at a ruined tower southwest of Brill. Using intelligence recovered in Deathknell, the Forsaken aim to push back the zealous crusaders threatening their borders.",h="Executor Zygand directs Forsaken champions to strike down Captain Perrine and her garrison stationed at a...",sec={{t="Intelligence Put to Use",b="Documents recovered from the Scarlet Crusade in Deathknell by Executor Arren revealed active troop movements across Tirisfal Glades. Rather than waiting for the fanatics to mount an offensive against the newly fortified town of Brill, Executor Zygand uses this captured intelligence to orchestrate preemptive strikes against their field commanders.",sp=0},{t="The Threat at the Ruined Tower",b="Stationed at a dilapidated watchtower southwest of Brill, Captain Perrine oversees a contingent of Scarlet Zealots and Missionaries. From this vantage, the Crusade attempts to monitor Forsaken movements and project power deeper into Tirisfal, making Perrine's death crucial to the defense of the Dark Lady's young kingdom.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Perrine?",a="Captain Perrine is a Scarlet Crusade officer stationed at a ruined watchtower southwest of Brill, tasked with commanding a detachment of Zealots and Missionaries encroaching upon Tirisfal Glades.",al={"captain perrine","perrine","who is perrine"}},{q="Where did the Forsaken get information on Captain Perrine?",a="Executor Arren recovered strategic Crusade documents during the initial defense of Deathknell, which detailed troop assignments and outpost locations, including Perrine's post.",al={"strategic documents zygand","arren's documents","scarlet documents deathknell"}},{q="Why are Scarlet Missionaries and Zealots in Tirisfal?",a="The Scarlet Crusade considers all undead abominations that must be exterminated, regardless of whether they serve the Scourge or the Forsaken. Their missionaries and zealots push deep into Tirisfal to wage a holy war and reclaim Lordaeron for the living.",al={"why is scarlet crusade in tirisfal","scarlet missionaries tirisfal","scarlet zealots"}},{q="How does this quest fit into the campaign against the Crusade?",a="This is the second step in the Tirisfal campaign against the Crusade. Slaying Perrine dismantles their local scouting post before Executor Zygand escalates operations against larger encampments further across the glades.",al={"at war with the scarlet crusade chain","what comes next after perrine"}},{q="Can this quest be done together with anything else nearby?",a="Yes, it pairs directly with Proof of Demise, which also directs Forsaken adventurers to Perrine's ruined tower to retrieve the captain's signet ring as evidence of her death.",al={"proof of demise pairing","quest pairing perrine","brill tower quests"}},{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is the primary military commander stationed in Brill, responsible for securing Tirisfal Glades and directing strategic offensives on behalf of Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"zygand","executor zygand brill"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, eliminating the Scarlet Crusade is an existential necessity; the zealots draw no distinction between free-willed undead and the Scourge.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms relies on the Forsaken securing Tirisfal Glades against hostile human zealots."},kw={"brill","captain perrine","executor arren","executor zygand","proof of demise","ruined tower","scarlet crusade","scarlet missionary","scarlet zealot","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:374","subzone:brill","npc:executor-arren","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="9",faction="Horde",id=370},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (2)"}}
E["quest:371"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="This military operation tasks Forsaken defenders with striking at the Scarlet Crusade encampment near the Balnir Farmstead in southeastern Tirisfal Glades. Under orders from Executor Zygand, players eliminate Captain Vachon and his accompanying friars to stall Crusader raids threatening the Dark Lady's domain.",h="This military operation tasks Forsaken defenders with striking at the Scarlet Crusade encampment near the...",sec={{t="A Looming Encroachment",b="As the Forsaken strive to secure the perimeter around Brill and the Undercity, the Scarlet Crusade maintains fortified pockets across the countryside. Reports funneling into town from Executor Arren alert the military command to active Crusader incursions operating out of a crumbling guard tower in southeastern Tirisfal Glades, uncomfortably close to the abandoned Balnir Farmstead.",sp=0},{t="Severing the Chain of Command",b="Recognizing that disorganized zealots are far less perilous than coordinated squads, Executor Zygand focuses the offensive on their field leadership. By eliminating Captain Vachon alongside the Scarlet Friars who bolster his men with holy magic, the Forsaken aim to shatter this cell's operational cohesion and suppress human raids into nearby Forsaken territories.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who orders this strike?",a="Executor Zygand, stationed in the town of Brill, issues the orders. He acts on frontline intelligence compiled and delivered by Executor Arren regarding Crusade movements near the Balnir Farmstead.",al={"quest giver","who gives this quest","who is zygand"}},{q="Where is Captain Vachon located?",a="Captain Vachon and his retinue of Scarlet Friars are based at a ruined watchtower in southeastern Tirisfal Glades, just east of the Balnir Farmstead.",al={"vachon location","where is vachon","where are scarlet friars"}},{q="Why does Executor Zygand target Scarlet Friars specifically?",a="Scarlet Friars provide essential magical and spiritual support to the rank-and-file zealots. Cutting down their spellcasters deprives the Crusade squad of defensive wards and healing, leaving their field operations completely crippled.",al={"why kill friars","scarlet friars"}},{q="What threat does the ruined tower pose to Brill?",a="The tower provides the Scarlet Crusade with elevated sightlines and a fortified launching point. From there, Crusader patrols can easily ambuscade Forsaken travelers and disrupt supply roads leading east out of Brill.",al={"tower threat","why attack tower","balnir tower"}},{q="How does this fit into the broader conflict with the Crusade?",a="This mission forms the third phase of Executor Zygand's tactical campaign to systematically eradicate Scarlet Crusade strongholds from the Tirisfal Glades, pushing zealot forces back before they can besiege the Undercity.",al={"scarlet war chain","war with the scarlet crusade lore"}},{q="What happens after Captain Vachon is slain?",a="While Vachon's defeat slows Crusader advances in southeastern Tirisfal, Executor Zygand promptly directs attention toward larger Scarlet Crusade fortifications elsewhere in the region.",al={"next quest","what after vachon","vachon aftermath"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every Crusader post cleared around Tirisfal Glades secures your newborn nation's borders and protects Lady Sylvanas's realm from living purifiers.",["faction:Horde"]="Neutralizing Scarlet zealots keeps the approach to the Undercity open and secures Horde communication routes through northern Lordaeron.",["class:Priest"]="Clashing with the Scarlet Friars pits your mastery of the Shadow and distorted Holy power against the dogmatic, unyielding fanaticism of human zealots."},kw={"arren","balnir","brill","crusader","friar","tirisfal","tower","vachon","zygand"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:balnir-farmstead","subzone:brill","npc:executor-arren","quest:370","quest:1882","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="10",faction="Horde",id=371},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (3)"}}
E["quest:372"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="This mission represents the culmination of Executor Zygand's early campaign to secure Tirisfal Glades against Scarlet Crusade incursions. Operating out of Brill, Forsaken agents are directed to strike directly at Captain Melrache and his personal vanguard at a ruined watchtower past Faol's Rest.",h="This mission represents the culmination of Executor Zygand's early campaign to secure Tirisfal Glades against...",sec={{t="A Strike at the Vanguard",b="While the Forsaken consolidate their hold over the ruins of Lordaeron, the Scarlet Crusade relentlessly probes the borders of Tirisfal. From an elevated watchtower situated in northern Tirisfal past Faol's Rest, zealous crusaders have organized raiding parties against Forsaken patrols and territory. Rather than waiting to repel another assault, Executor Zygand chooses decapitation: eliminating the command structure that directs the local raids.",sp=0},{t="Captain Melrache's Hold",b="Commanding this northern encampment is Captain Melrache, an uncompromising officer flanked constantly by two sworn bodyguards. Melrache's position gives the Crusade observation over the coastal roads and surrounding woods. Slaying him breaks the immediate coordination of the crusaders near Brill, neutralizing a direct threat to Lady Sylvanas's fledgling kingdom and driving the zealots back toward their stronger fortifications further east.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Melrache?",a="Captain Melrache is a field commander of the Scarlet Crusade overseeing a raiding camp at a ruined tower in northern Tirisfal Glades, beyond Faol's Rest. He leads aggressive incursions into Forsaken lands alongside his personal bodyguards.",al={"melrache","captain melrache lore","who is the scarlet captain"}},{q="Where is the ruined tower located?",a="The tower stands in the northern wilderness of Tirisfal Glades, perched on the bluffs just past the graveyard of Faol's Rest, overlooking the northern coast.",al={"melrache location","where is the tower","faol's rest tower"}},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want Melrache dead?",a="Melrache's contingent has been actively raiding out of their tower base, harassing Forsaken troops and threatening the security of Brill and the Undercity. Zygand orders his assassination to break the Crusade's local offensive momentum.",al={"why kill melrache","zygand's motive"}},{q="How does this fight connect to the wider war against Arthas?",a="Executor Zygand views the Scarlet Crusade as a dangerous distraction. Removing aggressive Crusade officers allows the Forsaken to solidify control over Tirisfal and preserve strength for their ultimate vengeance against the Lich King.",al={"arthas connection","why mention arthas"}},{q="Does slaying Melrache clear the Scarlet Crusade from Tirisfal?",a="No. Melrache's death eliminates an immediate raiding cell and weakens northern pressure on Brill, but the Crusade maintains massive strongholds nearby, including the Scarlet Monastery to the east.",al={"is scarlet crusade defeated","do they leave tirisfal"}},{q="What is Faol's Rest?",a="Faol's Rest is a secluded, solemn burial site in northern Tirisfal named after Alonsus Faol, the former Archbishop of the Church of the Holy Light. Melrache's tower sits in the rugged hills just beyond it.",al={"faols rest","faol resting place"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, every crusader slain is one less fanatic denying their right to exist in the homeland they inhabited in life.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing the perimeter of Tirisfal protects the Horde's solitary, vulnerable foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms.",["class:Rogue"]="Striking deep behind enemy lines to isolate a commander from his surrounding army is the quintessential work of Deathstalkers."},kw={"brill","captain melrache","executor zygand","faol's rest","scarlet bodyguard","scarlet crusade","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","subzone:brill","subzone:faol-s-rest","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal","quest:370"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="12",faction="Horde",id=372},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (4)"}}
E["quest:374"] = {t="quest",n="Proof of Demise",z="tirisfal",s="Proof of Demise is a military directive issued by Deathguard Burgess in Brill to thin the ranks of the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades. Initiated on the orders of Varimathras, Sylvanas Windrunner's dreadlord lieutenant, it tests a soldier's loyalty to the Forsaken cause. Recruits are ordered to strip signet rings from fallen crusaders as tangible evidence of their slaughter.",h="Proof of Demise is a military directive issued by Deathguard Burgess in Brill to thin the ranks of the...",sec={{t="A Mandate from the Dreadlord",b="The campaign across northern Tirisfal Glades is not merely defensive; it is a coordinated war of eradication. Varimathras, the dreadlord who surrendered and pledged his blade to Sylvanas Windrunner, oversees many of the Forsaken's aggressive military maneuvers against the living. His directives trickle down to commanders like Executor Zygand and frontline officers such as Deathguard Burgess. Burgess makes the directive clear: the human race is viewed as vermin to be purged from Lordaeron, and the zealous crusaders nearby are the immediate target.",sp=0},{t="Tokens of Slaughter",b="Words alone do not satisfy the commanders in Brill. To prove obedience to the Dark Lady and her lieutenant, soldiers must plunder Scarlet Insignia Rings straight from the fingers of slain zealots. These rings bear the iconography of the Scarlet Crusade, marking their bearers as sworn enemies of the Forsaken. Returning with a handful of these trophies serves as unassailable proof of dead crusaders and a demonstration of uncompromising allegiance.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who assigns the task to collect these rings?",a="Deathguard Burgess, a Forsaken guard stationed in the town of Brill, gives the order. He acts on reports from Executor Zygand and follows the overarching military goals set by Varimathras.",al={"who gives proof of demise","quest giver","deathguard burgess quest"}},{q="Why does Burgess demand Scarlet Insignia Rings specifically?",a="Scarlet Insignia Rings serve as indisputable physical proof that a crusader has been slain. They are personal tokens carried by the zealots, making them convenient, undeniable trophies of war that confirm a soldier's loyalty to the Forsaken leadership.",al={"why rings","scarlet rings purpose","what are insignia rings"}},{q="Who is Varimathras and why is he mentioned?",a="Varimathras is a dreadlord who allied with Queen Sylvanas Windrunner after the Forsaken broke free from the Lich King. Currently serving as her chief lieutenant in the Undercity, he directs military strategy against remaining human enclaves in Lordaeron, including the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"who is varimathras","dreadlord in undercity","why varimathras"}},{q="Where are the Scarlet Crusaders located for this task?",a="Scarlet zealots maintain several armed encampments across Tirisfal Glades, particularly around their watchtowers, garrisons, and outposts in the northern and eastern reaches of the woods.",al={"where to find scarlet crusade","scarlet crusader locations","crusader camps tirisfal"}},{q="How does this connect to Executor Zygand's orders?",a="Executor Zygand oversees the broader campaign against the Scarlet Crusade from Brill. While Zygand directs recruits to break the crusaders' field presence, Burgess follows up by requiring personal trophies as proof of obedience directly to Varimathras and the Dark Lady.",al={"executor zygand connection","at war with the scarlet crusade link"}},{q="Why is the Forsaken leadership so hostile to the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade considers all undead abominations destined for holy fire, making no distinction between the mindless Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken. Because they aggressively hunt down the Forsaken on their own borders, Sylvanas and her officers view them as a dangerous existential threat that must be annihilated.",al={"why fight scarlet crusade","forsaken vs scarlet crusade","why do forsaken hate humans"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, every crusader ring brought to Brill represents one fewer fanatic sworn to cleanse Lordaeron of free-willed undead.",["faction:Horde"]="This task demonstrates the ruthless, total-war mindset of Sylvanas's regime in the north, orchestrated in part by the dreadlord Varimathras."},kw={"brill","dark lady","deathguard burgess","executor zygand","proof of demise","scarlet crusade","scarlet insignia ring","tirisfal glades","varimathras"},rel={"npc:deathguard-burgess","quest:370","npc:executor-zygand","npc:varimathras","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Burgess",level="7",faction="Horde",id=374},src={"Proof of Demise (quest)"}}
E["quest:398"] = {t="quest",n="Wanted: Maggot Eye",z="tirisfal",s="Wanted: Maggot Eye is an official death bounty posted on the Brill notice board by the town's Forsaken leadership. A notorious gnoll has been looting nearby graveyards and farms to supply dead bodies directly to the Lich King's Scourge. Executor Zygand requires proof of the creature's execution to secure the lands around Garren's Haunt.",h="Wanted: Maggot Eye is an official death bounty posted on the Brill notice board by the town's Forsaken...",sec={{t="A Grave Crime",b="In Tirisfal Glades, the dead are far from resting peacefully. The gnoll known as Maggot Eye earned a severe death sentence not merely for scavenging, but for active collaboration with the Lich King. While gnolls are generally viewed as savage brutes driven by simple hunger, Maggot Eye has been systematically digging up corpses and collecting remains to fuel the ranks of the Scourge army.",sp=0},{t="Justice in Brill",b="For the Forsaken, whose entire existence hinges on breaking free from the Lich King's dominion, feeding dead kin back into the Scourge war machine is among the highest offenses possible. Executor Zygand, overseeing local military enforcement in Brill, commissioned this bounty to put an end to the grave robberies near Garren's Haunt. To collect the prize, the executioner must sever Maggot Eye's paw as unmistakable proof that the beast will trouble Tirisfal no longer.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Maggot Eye?",a="Maggot Eye is an infamous gnoll prowling the northern regions of Tirisfal Glades. Considered vile even among his kind, he pillages the farms near Garren's Haunt and gathers corpses for the Scourge.",al={"maggot eye lore","who is maggot eye","maggot eye gnoll"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken want him dead?",a="He was sentenced to death for directly supplying freshly looted corpses to the Lich King's Scourge army. Denying soldiers and resources to the Scourge is essential to Forsaken survival.",al={"why kill maggot eye","maggot eye crimes","why bounty maggot eye"}},{q="Where is Maggot Eye usually found?",a="He can be found lurking inside an old ruined hut in Garren's Haunt, a ruined farmstead located to the northeast of Brill.",al={"maggot eye location","where is maggot eye","find maggot eye"}},{q="Who pays the reward for the bounty?",a="Executor Zygand in the center of Brill accepts proof of the kill and distributes the town's reward on behalf of the Forsaken military authority.",al={"who turns in maggot eye","maggot eye quest turn in","brill bounty rewarder"}},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want his paw?",a="In classic frontier justice, taking a unique physical trophy like Maggot Eye's paw ensures indisputable proof of death before the bounty funds are paid out.",al={"why maggot eye paw","paw proof","maggot eyes paw"}},{q="Are gnolls allied with the Scourge?",a="Generally gnolls act independently out of hunger and greed, but Maggot Eye specifically trades or funnels dead bodies to the Scourge, making him an exceptionally dangerous collaborator.",al={"gnolls and scourge","do gnolls work for lich king","scourge gnolls"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every corpse stolen by Maggot Eye is a fallen sibling turned back into an enslaved puppet of the Lich King. Putting him down is a matter of both national defense and personal vengeance.",["faction:Horde"]="Tirisfal's northern borders must be pacified if the Horde is to maintain a secure foothold in Lordaeron against remnants of the Scourge."},kw={"bounty","brill","executor zygand","garren's haunt","gnoll","graverobber","lich king","maggot eye","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:garren-s-haunt","npc:executor-zygand","subzone:brill","quest:358","topic:gnoll","topic:forsaken","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Wanted!",["end"]="Executor Zygand",level="10",faction="Horde",id=398},src={"Wanted: Maggot Eye"}}
E["quest:404"] = {t="quest",n="A Putrid Task",z="tirisfal",s="A Putrid Task is an early military assignment offered by Deathguard Dillinger in Brill. It directs adventurers to push back the mindlessly aggressive Scourge encroaching upon the old bridge west of the settlement. Collecting proof of the monsters' destruction secures the road and eases pressure on Tirisfal's defenders.",h="A Putrid Task is an early military assignment offered by Deathguard Dillinger in Brill.",sec={{t="Holding the Bridge",b="Brill sits at a critical crossroads in eastern Tirisfal Glades, making any enemy approach a direct threat to the Forsaken power base. Mindless Scourge remnants constantly seep westward across the waterways, clustering around the broken remnants of the old stone bridge. Without regular patrols beating them back, the shambling corpses would quickly choke transit between Brill and the western farmsteads.",sp=0},{t="A Grudge Against the Mindless",b="For the Forsaken, Scourge roaming their borders is not merely a strategic nuisance; it is an insult. Every mindless ghoul and rotting corpse represents the servitude and torment that Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's followers broke away from. Deathguards like Dillinger take grim satisfaction in crushing their former captors, demanding severed claws as brutal proof that the mindless dead have been put to rest for good.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Deathguard Dillinger, an officer of the Forsaken guard stationed at the western exit of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, assigns this mission.",al={"quest giver","where to get putrid task","deathguard dillinger quest"}},{q="Why does Deathguard Dillinger want putrid claws?",a="The claws serve as gruesome proof of death. The Deathguards need confirmation that wandering Scourge have been thoroughly destroyed, rather than merely driven slightly off the main road.",al={"why putrid claws","claws reason"}},{q="Where are the rotting dead found?",a="They wander the overgrown fields and riverbanks immediately west of Brill, clustered heavily around the old stone bridge.",al={"rotting dead location","where are the ghouls","old bridge location"}},{q="Why are there Scourge in Tirisfal Glades?",a="Although the Forsaken wrested control of Lordaeron's capital and the surrounding glades from the Scourge, wild remnants of the Lich King's armies still linger in corners of the woods, wandering aimlessly without necromantic commanders.",al={"why scourge here","scourge in tirisfal"}},{q="What happens after completing this task?",a="Clearing the bridge uncovers deeper trouble on the nearby farmsteads, prompting Deathguard Dillinger to dispatch you further west to inspect the overrun mills.",al={"next quest","what follows putrid task"},sp=1},{q="Are the Forsaken and the Scourge not the same thing?",a="No. The Forsaken are free-willed undead who broke the Lich King's telepathic control and fight to protect their autonomy. The Scourge remain mindless thralls bound to the Iron Will of the Frozen Throne.",al={"difference between forsaken and scourge","aren't they all undead"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Destroying Scourge is deeply personal for the Forsaken, serving as vengeance against the relentless force that once held their minds captive.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Brill ensures that the fledgling Horde presence in the Eastern Kingdoms maintains a secure foothold against the Scourge."},kw={"a putrid task","brill","deathguard dillinger","putrid claw","ravaged corpse","rotting dead","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",level="6",faction="Horde",id=404},src={"A Putrid Task (Classic)"}}
E["quest:407"] = {t="quest",n="Fields of Grief",z="tirisfal",s="Fields of Grief concludes Apothecary Johaan's experiment to weaponize ordinary pumpkins gathered from Solliden Farmstead. Having infused the crop with his latest alchemical concotion, Johaan dispatches you to feed the laced vegetable to a captive Scarlet Crusader languishing in Brill.",h="Fields of Grief concludes Apothecary Johaan's experiment to weaponize ordinary pumpkins gathered from...",sec={{t="A Weapon of Ingenuity",b="Apothecary Johaan of the Royal Apothecary Society believes the Forsaken must exploit every tactical advantage to fend off the Scourge from the north and human incursions from the south. Rather than relying solely on raw blade-work or dark sorcery, the Society seeks to harness ordinary staples of the land. By tainting the pumpkins recovered from the mortal farmers of Solliden Farmstead, Johaan intends to prove that even common produce can be transformed into an instrument of death on behalf of the Dark Lady.",sp=0},{t="The Cellar Test",b="The test subject awaits beneath the floorboards of the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. Chained and starved, the captured Scarlet Zealot greets Forsaken callers with typical fanatic defiance, invoking the Holy Light to purge the undead. Hunger quickly breaks the crusader's resolve, however. Mistaking the tainted pumpkin for genuine relief, the captive devours it eagerly, only to rapidly deform into a rotting ghoul before collapsing lifeless in the dirt.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Apothecary Johaan use a pumpkin for his poison?",a="Johaan wants to demonstrate that mundane crops can be turned into subtle, effective weapons against the living. By lacing everyday produce from nearby human farms with alchemical mixtures, the Royal Apothecary Society tests delivery methods that prey on the basic survival needs of mortal foes.",al={"why a pumpkin","why poison pumpkin","laced pumpkin lore"}},{q="Who is the prisoner in the tavern cellar?",a="The prisoner is a Captured Scarlet Zealot, a fanatic of the Scarlet Crusade captured by Forsaken forces in Tirisfal Glades. Weakened by starvation and isolation, the zealot clings to religious fervor until presented with food.",al={"who is captured zealot","zealot in gallows end","brill cellar prisoner"}},{q="What happens to the Scarlet Zealot after eating the pumpkin?",a="Upon consuming the laced pumpkin, the zealot mutates rapidly into a ravenous ghoul, wanders aimlessly across the cellar floor, and collapses dead shortly thereafter, proving the fatal potency of Johaan's formulation.",al={"what happens to zealot","zealot transformation","does zealot turn into ghoul"},sp=1},{q="Where is the Gallows' End Tavern cellar?",a="The cellar is located directly beneath the Gallows' End Tavern in Brill. A ramp behind the front counter leads down into the holding area where Forsaken guards keep prisoners.",al={"how to find cellar","where is zealot located","gallows end cellar entrance"}},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society trying to achieve here?",a="The Society works under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner to invent biological and alchemical agents capable of destroying both the Scourge and mortal threats like the Scarlet Crusade. Small-scale experiments on captives in Brill serve as trial runs for these concoctions.",al={"apothecary society goal","why test plague","royal apothecary society tirisfal"}},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade active in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Scarlet Crusade considers all undead abominations that must be exterminated, making no distinction between the mindless Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken. They maintain camps and garrisons across the former kingdom of Lordaeron to reclaim the land by holy fire.",al={"scarlet crusade tirisfal","why are scarlets here","crusade presence brill"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, this experiment showcases the ruthless pragmatism required to survive surrounded by mortal zealots to the south and the Lich King's armies to the north.",["faction:Horde"]="The Royal Apothecary Society's biochemical research often unsettles the Forsaken's new allies, yet it remains central to securing Tirisfal Glades for the Horde."},kw={"apothecary johaan","brill","captured scarlet zealot","fields of grief","gallows end tavern","laced pumpkin","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:captured-scarlet-zealot","quest:365","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","topic:light"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",["end"]="Captured Scarlet Zealot",level="7",faction="Horde",id=407},src={"Fields of Grief (2)"}}
E["quest:408"] = {t="quest",n="The Family Crypt",z="tirisfal",s="The Family Crypt is a Horde quest tasking players with confronting the Scourge inside the Agamand Family Crypt. Commanded by Magistrate Sevren in Brill, adventurers must destroy the raised Agamand ancestors and slay the skeletal Scourge commander, Captain Dargol.",h="The Family Crypt is a Horde quest tasking players with confronting the Scourge inside the Agamand Family...",sec={{t="A Foxtrot in Tirisfal",b="While the Forsaken have carved out a fragile dominion in Tirisfal Glades, remnants of the Lich King's Scourge remain deeply entrenched in the countryside. The Agamand Mills, once a prosperous flour-producing heartland of Lordaeron, have become a dangerous Scourge stronghold. Magistrate Sevren in Brill watches this military buildup with grave concern, knowing that every inch yielded to mindless undead undermines the Forsaken's independence.",sp=0},{t="Defiling the Tomb",b="The center of the local Scourge occupation is the Agamand Family Crypt, where the skeletal commander Captain Dargol has set up headquarters. Using dark necromancy, Dargol has dragged generations of Agamand family dead from their rest, twisting them into Rotting and Wailing Ancestors to swell his ranks. Sevren dispatches Forsaken agents to purge the crypt, lay the disturbed dead back to rest, and severed Dargol's head to shatter Scourge coordination in northern Tirisfal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Captain Dargol?",a="Captain Dargol is a skeletal Scourge officer stationed within the Agamand Family Crypt. From this tomb, he commands local Scourge forces and uses necromancy to reanimate the Agamand family ancestors to march against the Forsaken.",al={"captain dargol","who is dargol","dargol lore"}},{q="Why does Magistrate Sevren care about the Agamand Mills?",a="Agamand Mills represents a major Scourge foothold dangerously close to Brill and the Undercity. Left unchecked, Captain Dargol's growing force of reanimated ancestors could mount an offensive against the newly liberated Forsaken settlements.",al={"why brill cares","sevren agamand","agamand importance"}},{q="Who are the Wailing and Rotting Ancestors?",a="They are the deceased forebears of the wealthy Agamand lineage. Rather than resting peacefully in their ancestral burial grounds, their bodies and spirits have been corrupted and bound to the will of the Scourge by Captain Dargol's dark arts.",al={"wailing ancestors","rotting ancestors","agamand ancestors"}},{q="What happens after Dargol is killed?",a="Returning Captain Dargol's skull to Magistrate Sevren breaks the Scourge's centralized leadership at the mills. Sevren hails the victory as a critical strike for the Forsaken and an early step toward purging the Lich King's influence from Lordaeron entirely.",al={"crypt aftermath","end of agamand chain","dargol defeated"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Captain Dargol represents everything they fought to escape: enslavement to the Lich King's will. Putting down the raised ancestors is both an act of self-defense and a grim duty to break the Scourge's grip on their homeland.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Tirisfal Glades is vital to anchoring the Horde's presence in the Eastern Kingdoms, removing immediate threats to their northern stronghold."},kw={"agamand family crypt","agamand mills","brill","captain dargol","magistrate sevren","rotting ancestor","scourge","the family crypt","tirisfal glades","wailing ancestor"},rel={"subzone:agamand-family-crypt","subzone:agamand-mills","npc:magistrate-sevren","quest:355","quest:362","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},m={start="Magistrate Sevren",["end"]="Magistrate Sevren",level="13",faction="Horde",id=408},src={"The Family Crypt (Classic)"}}
E["quest:409"] = {t="quest",n="Proving Allegiance",z="tirisfal",s="Proving Allegiance is the crucial trial presented by Gunther Arcanus to determine whether you truly serve the free-willed Forsaken or the Lich King. To earn the solitary necromancer's trust, you are sent to summon and destroy Lillith Nefara, a dangerous Scourge operative lurking near his island.",h="Proving Allegiance is the crucial trial presented by Gunther Arcanus to determine whether you truly serve the...",sec={{t="A Recluse's Suspicions",b="Gunther Arcanus has isolated himself on an island in Brightwater Lake since rising into undeath, fiercely clinging to his autonomy. Though Bethor Iceshard's magical enchantments on Gunther's spellbook confirmed the emissary does not carry the foul taint of the Scourge, words and charms are not enough for the paranoid hermit. To earn his confidence, an outsider must demonstrate active hostility toward the minions of the Lich King through decisive violence.",sp=0},{t="The Slaying of Lillith Nefara",b="Just south of Gunther's refuge stands a bloodstained ritual altar used by Lillith Nefara, a formidable Scourge agent operating in the Tirisfal Glades. Using a specialized Candle of Beckoning, the petitioner awakens Lillith from the shadows to face her in open combat. Striking down the agent shatters Gunther's long-held conviction that he was the only undead creature capable of breaking free from the Lich King's iron grip.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Gunther Arcanus need proof?",a="Gunther has survived as an independent undead by trusting no one. Surrounded by the Scourge, the Scarlet Crusade, and other threats in Tirisfal, he assumes any undead visitor could be an agent sent by the Lich King to subjugate him until they shed Scourge blood.",al={"why does gunther doubt me","gunther trust"}},{q="Who is Lillith Nefara?",a="Lillith Nefara is a powerful Scourge agent active along the southern shores of Brightwater Lake. She operates around an ancient, bloody altar near Gunther's island, serving the Lich King's reach in the glades.",al={"who is lillith","lillith nefara lore"}},{q="What is the Candle of Beckoning?",a="The Candle of Beckoning is a ritual item retrieved from a crate on Gunther's island. Placing and lighting it upon the bloody altar summons Lillith Nefara from her resting place so she can be engaged in battle.",al={"candle of beckoning","how to summon lillith"}},{q="What realization does Gunther come to upon Lillith's defeat?",a="Defeating Lillith forces Gunther to accept the astonishing truth that he is not unique. Until this trial, he genuinely believed he was the only undead in Lordaeron who had broken free from the Lich King's telepathic domination.",al={"gunther reaction","gunther epiphany"},sp=1},{q="Where does this confrontation take place?",a="The ritual occurs at an altar situated on the lakeshore just off the southern coast of Gunther's island in Brightwater Lake, within eastern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is the altar","lillith location"}},{q="What happens after proving your allegiance?",a="With Gunther's doubts resolved, he finally agrees to listen to the emissaries of the Undercity and reconsider his solitary exile, setting the stage for his formal recruitment into Lady Sylvanas's Forsaken.",al={"what next after proving allegiance","after lillith dies"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, breaking Gunther's isolation is personal; it proves to a brother in undeath that none of them have to face the wrath of the Scourge or the living alone.",["class:Mage"]="Bethor Iceshard and Gunther Arcanus represent significant arcane and necromantic talents in Lordaeron; demonstrating your capability earns the professional respect of a powerful fellow caster."},kw={"bethor iceshard","brightwater lake","candle of beckoning","gunther arcanus","lillith nefara","proving allegiance","scourge altar","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:411","quest:366","quest:431","npc:gunther-arcanus","topic:scourge","topic:lich-king","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Gunther Arcanus",level="12",faction="Horde",id=409},src={"Proving Allegiance"}}
E["quest:410"] = {t="quest",n="The Dormant Shade",z="tirisfal",s="The Dormant Shade is a dark ritual performed within the ruined homesteads of Tirisfal Glades. By placing a mystic candle upon an old, blood-soaked table, a traveler summons forth a restless spirit tied to the Forsaken's dark rites of loyalty.",h="The Dormant Shade is a dark ritual performed within the ruined homesteads of Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Altar",b="Amid the blighted ruins of Tirisfal Glades rests a battered, bloody dinner table. Far from an ordinary piece of neglected domestic furniture, it serves as the physical focus for a sinister conjuration. Stained with dried gore and abandoned to the shadows, the table acts as a makeshift ritual slab where death and dark magic linger.",sp=0},{t="The Candle of Beckoning",b="To awaken whatever lurks attached to the site, one must place the Candle of Beckoning upon the bloodied surface and ignite its flame. The candle's light cuts through the Tirisfal gloom, calling forth the spirit of Lillith Nefara from the veil of death. It is an intentional act of necromantic disturbance designed to challenge those who seek to prove their mettle and allegiance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of lighting the candle on the table?",a="Lighting the Candle of Beckoning on the battered, bloody table summons the shade of Lillith Nefara, a dangerous apparition who must be vanquished.",al={"why light candle","dormant shade objective","table ritual"}},{q="Who is summoned by this ritual?",a="The ritual draws forth Lillith Nefara, an undead spirit haunting the ruined homesteads of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who spawns","dormant shade ghost","who is the shade"}},{q="How does this relate to proving allegiance to the Forsaken?",a="Summoning and destroying Lillith Nefara is an essential test in the quest Proving Allegiance, demonstrating a Forsaken initiate's willingness and ability to root out stubborn apparitions in Tirisfal.",al={"proving allegiance connection","why kill lillith","forsaken test"}},{q="Where does this ritual take place?",a="The ritual occurs at an old ruined homestead in Tirisfal Glades, at a battered wooden dinner table stained with dried blood.",al={"table location","where is the table","lilliths dinner table"}},{q="Can anyone light the candle?",a="Anyone possessing the Candle of Beckoning who is undertaking the trials of allegiance for the Forsaken can ignite the flame upon the altar.",al={"who can do the ritual","class requirements","candle ritual"}},{q="Is the table naturally haunted?",a="The table itself is a grim relic of Lordaeron's fall, steeped in violence and residual dark energies that allow the Candle of Beckoning to anchor and manifest the dormant shade.",al={"is the table magical","why the bloody table"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, performing rituals over the bloodied ruins of Lordaeron's former homes is a grim reminder that their new existence is forged through death, dark magic, and unyielding loyalty to the Dark Lady.",["class:Warlock"]="Warlocks understand the resonant power of binding spirits to blood-drenched altars, making this ritual a familiar exercise in manipulating the boundary between life and death.",["class:Priest"]="Shadow priests recognize the call of the candle as an exercise in shadowy communion, pulling a restless lingering soul back into physical conflict."},kw={"bloody table","candle of beckoning","dormant shade","forsaken ritual","lillith nefara","proving allegiance","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:409","zone:tirisfal","topic:light"},m={start="Lillith's Dinner Table",level="10",faction="Horde",id=410},src={"The Dormant Shade"}}
E["quest:426"] = {t="quest",n="The Mills Overrun",z="tirisfal",s="Tasked by Deathguard Dillinger in Brill, this mission sends Forsaken soldiers to break the Scourge's foothold at the nearby Agamand Mills. Mindless undead gather among the ruined windmills, threatening to establish a forward base dangerously close to Tirisfal Glades' settlements. To halt this staging ground, recruits must shatter the ranks of skeletal soldiers and bonecasters.",h="Tasked by Deathguard Dillinger in Brill, this mission sends Forsaken soldiers to break the Scourge's foothold...",sec={{t="A Looming Threat on the Mills",b="The Agamand Mills once anchored the agricultural heart of Tirisfal Glades, but in the wake of the Third War, their windmills overlook a far grimmer harvest. Scourge forces under the Lich King's thrall have begun massing on the grounds. If these mindless thralls successfully secure the mills, they will have an entrenched base of operations from which to push deeper into Tirisfal and strike directly at the fledgling Forsaken holdings.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Destruction",b="Deathguard Dillinger wastes little time on sentiment. Tasked with fortifying Brill and policing the territory, Dillinger orders recruits to hunt down Rattlecage and Cracked Skull Soldiers alongside Darkeye Bonecasters. By demanding notched ribs and blackened skulls as proof of their destruction, Dillinger ensures the skeletal ranks are being physically battered apart, throwing the mindless remnants back toward the Plaguelands before their offensive can truly begin.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the Scourge gathering at Agamand Mills?",a="The Scourge are attempting to establish a forward staging ground in western Tirisfal. If they entrench themselves at Agamand Mills, they can stage coordinated raids deeper into the glades and directly threaten nearby Forsaken settlements like Brill.",al={"why agamand mills","scourge at the mills","why the mills"}},{q="Who is Deathguard Dillinger?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is a Forsaken sentry stationed in Brill. He coordinates tactical strikes against regional hazards in Tirisfal Glades, particularly the encroaching Scourge presence and hostile gnoll packs that threaten the road.",al={"deathguard dillinger lore","who is dillinger","dillinger brill"}},{q="Where are the Agamand Mills located?",a="Agamand Mills sits north of the main western highway in Tirisfal Glades. Traveling west from Brill over the river bridge and following the north fork leads straight to the prominent ruined windmills.",al={"where is agamand mills","mills location","how to get to the mills"}},{q="Why does Dillinger want ribs and skulls?",a="Dillinger requires tangible proof that the Scourge front line has been shattered. Bringing back notched ribs from the skeletal infantry and blackened skulls from the bonecasters guarantees the force has been battered and culled.",al={"notched ribs blackened skulls","why ribs and skulls"}},{q="What is the relationship between the Forsaken and the Scourge here?",a="The Forsaken are undead who broke free of the Lich King's mental domination. The Scourge remain mindless, obedient slaves bound to the Lich King's will, actively seeking to wipe out the Forsaken and reclaim Lordaeron for their master.",al={"forsaken vs scourge","why fight other undead"}},{q="What happens after clearing these Scourge?",a="Clearing the foot soldiers proves only an opening gambit against the infestation at Agamand Mills. Dillinger and the Deathguards continue pushing deeper into the mills to dismantle the lingering commanders and dark forces entrenched there.",al={"what comes next","after the mills overrun"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, driving the Scourge out of Agamand Mills is deeply personal: it protects their new sovereign lands while crushing the mindless slaves of the Lich King who once held them in thrall.",["faction:Horde"]="Holding Tirisfal Glades is critical to securing the Horde's solitary foothold in northern Lordaeron, making the elimination of Scourge staging grounds a tactical priority.",["class:Warrior"]="Clashing with the armored skeletons at Agamand Mills serves as a brutal trial by combat against relentless enemies who feel no pain and give no quarter."},kw={"agamand mills","blackened skulls","brill","darkeye bonecaster","deathguard dillinger","notched ribs","scourge","the mills overrun","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:agamand-mills","npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:brill","topic:scourge","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Dillinger",level="8",faction="Horde",id=426},src={"The Mills Overrun (Classic)"}}
E["quest:427"] = {t="quest",n="At War With The Scarlet Crusade",z="tirisfal",s="Executor Zygand in Brill coordinates the Forsaken campaign against the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades. Using intelligence recovered by Executor Arren, you are dispatched to eliminate Scarlet Warriors stationed at a guard tower west of the Solliden Farmstead. This assault marks the Forsaken military's opening offensive to purge the zealous crusaders from their borders.",h="Executor Zygand in Brill coordinates the Forsaken campaign against the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Two-Front War",b="The fledgling Forsaken state under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner faces simultaneous threats on multiple fronts. While the Deathguard keeps a wary vigil against the swelling armies of the Lich King, the fanatical mortals of the Scarlet Crusade contest Forsaken dominance over their former homeland. The Crusade considers all undead abominations to be purged with fire and blade, blind to the fact that the Forsaken have broken free of the Scourge's control.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Western Outpost",b="Thanks to intelligence documents secured by Executor Arren at Deathknell, Executor Zygand now knows the exact encampments and outposts held by the zealots across Tirisfal Glades. With regular Deathguard garrisons occupied by Scourge containment, independent Forsaken champions are commissioned to strike out directly. The first strike falls upon the guard tower west of Solliden Farmstead, where Scarlet Warriors muster and threaten the western approaches to Brill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade hostile toward the Forsaken?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is an extremist human order dedicated to eradicating the undead. They make no distinction between the mindless Scourge controlled by the Lich King and the free-willed Forsaken loyal to Lady Sylvanas, viewing every undead being as a plague-ridden monster that must be burned.",al={"why scarlet hate undead","scarlet crusade motivation","why are they attacking"}},{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is the senior military officer of the Forsaken Deathguard stationed in Brill. He directs tactical deployments, defends the roads surrounding the capital's approaches, and oversees offensive strikes against nearby Scarlet and Scourge encroachments.",al={"who is zygand","brill quest giver executor","zygand lore"}},{q="How did the Forsaken get intelligence on Scarlet positions?",a="Crucial tactical documents were recovered by recruits serving Executor Arren in Deathknell. These papers laid out Scarlet patrol routes, outposts, and encampments throughout Tirisfal, giving Executor Zygand the information needed to orchestrate targeted counter-attacks.",al={"scarlet documents","arren intelligence","how did they find the tower"}},{q="Where are the Scarlet Warriors located?",a="The Scarlet Warriors garrison a defensive tower located to the west of the Solliden Farmstead, in the western countryside of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"scarlet warrior location","where is the tower","solliden farmstead tower"}},{q="Why doesn't the Deathguard handle the Crusade directly?",a="The Deathguard's formal ranks are stretched thin monitoring the Scourge, whose forces grow in number each night under the Lich King's reach. Because regular soldiers cannot be spared from containment, Zygand relies on ambitious, unassigned champions to cull the Crusaders.",al={"why send players","where is the deathguard","why help zygand"}},{q="Does this mission end the Scarlet presence in Tirisfal?",a="No. This attack on the western watchtower is merely the first strike in a four-part campaign directed by Executor Zygand to dismantle Scarlet command and outposts across the region.",al={"is this the last scarlet quest","scarlet crusade quest chain"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Scarlet Crusade represents a bitter irony: living former countrymen who brand them monsters and seek their eradication rather than mourning the tragic fall of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Establishing a secure border around Tirisfal Glades and the Undercity is essential to giving the Horde a permanent foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"brill","deathguard","scarlet crusade","scarlet warriors","solliden farmstead","sylvanas","tirisfal glades","zygand"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","subzone:solliden-farmstead","npc:executor-arren","topic:lich-king"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="8",faction="Horde",id=427},src={"At War With The Scarlet Crusade (Classic)"}}
E["quest:431"] = {t="quest",n="Candles of Beckoning",z="tirisfal",s="Candles of Beckoning is a brief task centered around salvaging specialized ritual tapers discovered in Tirisfal Glades. These eerie tallow candles are steeped in dark practices and recovered directly from crates left among the shadows of Lordaeron's ruins.",h="Candles of Beckoning is a brief task centered around salvaging specialized ritual tapers discovered in...",sec={{t="Tallow and Dark Rites",b="Across Tirisfal Glades, dark magic lingers in neglected crypts, decaying farms, and cultist encampments. Tapers such as the Candles of Beckoning are not everyday illumination; they are crafted specifically to focus shadowy energies, invoke unseen presences, or channel forbidden incantations. Recovering them from discarded caches prevents them from fueling rogue practitioners or Scourge infiltrators.",sp=0},{t="A Reclaimed Relic",b="When Forsaken scouts locate crates containing these candles, securing them becomes an immediate concern. Taking possession of even a single candle provides vital reagents or wards that can be studied in the Undercity or turned toward bolstering the Forsaken hold on the shattered glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Candles of Beckoning?",a="These candles are ritualistic tapers imbued with shadowy intent, often utilized in occult ceremonies to focus magical summonings or invoke lingering entities throughout Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what are candles of beckoning","purpose of candles","what do candles do"}},{q="Where are these candles found?",a="They are stored within scattered supply crates situated in the shadowy corners and encampments of Tirisfal Glades, left behind amid ongoing factional skirmishes and occult operations.",al={"where to find candles of beckoning","candle crate location","crate of candles"}},{q="Who crafted these candles?",a="While their exact origins often tie to occultists, cultists, or rogue necromancers operating in Lordaeron's ruins, they are typically found stored in nondescript supply crates intended for ritual use.",al={"who made candles of beckoning","candle creator","who made the crate"}},{q="Why does the Horde or Forsaken want them?",a="Securing ritual implements denies their use to hostile groups—such as the Scourge or Scarlet Crusade—and offers Forsaken apothecaries and spellcasters valuable materials for their own defensive and arcane studies.",al={"why forsaken need candles","why retrieve candles","why horde candles"}},{q="Can just anyone use the candle?",a="While physically simple to take and store in a pack, the magical effects tied to ritual beckoning require specific incantations and ceremonial preparation.",al={"can i light it","how to use candle","use candle of beckoning"}},{q="Are the candles linked to the Scourge?",a="Cults aligned with dark magic and Scourge remnants frequently employ ritual items of this kind to summon or direct the undead across the northern ruins.",al={"is this scourge magic","are candles scourge","scourge cult candles"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, salvaging occult implements in Tirisfal is a matter of both survival and study, ensuring dangerous artifacts do not fall into hostile hands.",["class:Warlock"]="Practitioners of the dark arts readily recognize the distinct tallow and magical resonance used in ritual beckoning.",["class:Priest"]="Shadow priests understand the delicate balance required when handling items crafted to invoke lingering spirits and call forth unseen presences."},kw={"candles of beckoning","crate of candles","forsaken","occult","ritual taper","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Crate of Candles",level="10",faction="Horde",id=431},src={"Candles of Beckoning"}}
E["quest:492"] = {t="quest",n="A New Plague",z="tirisfal",s="This quest marks the grim culmination of Apothecary Johaan's initial research in Brill on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society. Having harvested venom, blood, and vile concoctions across Tirisfal Glades, Johaan sends you to the cellar of Gallows' End Tavern to test his lethal brew on a captive dwarven mountaineer.",h="This quest marks the grim culmination of Apothecary Johaan's initial research in Brill on behalf of the Royal...",sec={{t="A Deadly Concoction",b="Throughout your time aiding Apothecary Johaan, your efforts have steadily built toward refining a lethal toxin. The Royal Apothecary Society pursues an ambitious and shadowy agenda on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner: crafting a new plague that bypasses undead biology while annihilating the living. In this final step, Johaan brews what he euphemistically calls a 'special drink' and tasks you with administering it directly to an imprisoned enemy of the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="The Gallows' End Cellar",b="Beneath Gallows' End Tavern in Brill, the Deathguard maintains a damp cellar used as a makeshift holding cell for captives awaiting interrogation or disposal. Among them sits a captured Dwarven Mountaineer, an operative of the Ironforge reconnaissance units trespassing in Tirisfal Glades. Defiant and thirsty, he eagerly accepts a drink, completely unaware of its true alchemical payload.",sp=0},{t="A Chilling Demonstration",b="When offered the flask, the mountaineer gladly drinks, comparing it wistfully to Rhapsody Malt and boasting that dwarven steam tanks are coming to save him. The poison takes effect almost instantly, killing him on the spot. Johaan's parting words ring with chilling clarity: this lethal draft is merely a taste of what the Dark Lady envisions for the rest of Azeroth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Johaan?",a="Apothecary Johaan is a member of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in the town of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He directs early research into creating a new plague tailored for Forsaken warfare, employing adventurers to gather lethal reagents from the surrounding wilderness.",al={"apothecary johaan","who gives a new plague","johaan brilliance"}},{q="Why is there a dwarf captured in Brill?",a="Ironforge Mountaineers actively scout the northern kingdoms to monitor Forsaken movements and investigate the plaguelands. The Deathguard apprehended this particular scout in Tirisfal and locked him in the tavern cellar until the apothecaries found a use for him.",al={"dwarf in cellar","captured mountaineer","why is dwarf in tirisfal"}},{q="What happens when you give the prisoner the drink?",a="The dwarf takes the flagon gladly, desperate to quench his thirst after his capture. Moments after drinking, the toxic brew kills him on the spot, demonstrating the ruthless effectiveness of Johaan's latest plague formulation.",al={"does the dwarf die","drink result","mountaineer death"},sp=1},{q="What is the purpose of the New Plague research?",a="The Forsaken seek to invent a new plague under the orders of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Their goal is to develop a biological weapon potent enough to destroy both the mindless Scourge and the living races who threaten their sovereign territory.",al={"why make new plague","royal apothecary society goal","dark lady plague"}},{q="Where is the Captured Mountaineer located?",a="The Captured Mountaineer is imprisoned downstairs in the cellar of Gallows' End Tavern, located in the center of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"find captive dwarf","gallows end cellar","where is mountaineer"}},{q="Does this quest chain continue beyond this dwarf?",a="This four-part assignment for Apothecary Johaan concludes with the mountaineer's death. However, research into the New Plague remains a central, ongoing endeavor across Lordaeron, leading you to further testing assignments in the Undercity and the Sepulcher.",al={"next quest","a new plague followup","after mountaineer dies"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Carrying out Johaan's experiment offers a firsthand glimpse into the uncompromising survival doctrine of the Forsaken and the lethal work of the Royal Apothecary Society.",["race:Dwarf"]="The unfortunate prisoner represents the far-reaching presence of Ironforge Mountaineers, who risk death and covert interrogation to keep watch over Tirisfal Glades.",["faction:Alliance"]="The fate of the captive mountaineer illustrates the absolute ruthlessness of the Forsaken toward Alliance intruders discovered in Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="While your Kalimdor allies may fight for honor and survival, the Forsaken pursue victory through cold-blooded alchemical warfare that spares neither friend nor foe."},kw={"a new plague","apothecary johaan","brill","captured mountaineer","gallows end","plague","poison","royal apothecary society","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:apothecary-johaan","npc:captured-mountaineer","quest:367","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Apothecary Johaan",["end"]="Captured Mountaineer",level="11",faction="Horde",id=492},src={"A New Plague (4)"}}
E["quest:5481"] = {t="quest",n="Gordo's Task",z="tirisfal",s="Gordo's Task is an errand in Tirisfal Glades given by Gordo, a wandering abomination trying to gather flora along the road to Brill. Unsuited for delicate fieldwork, he recruits travelers to pick Gloom Weed and deliver it to his handler, Junior Apothecary Holland.",h="Gordo's Task is an errand in Tirisfal Glades given by Gordo, a wandering abomination trying to gather flora...",sec={{t="A Clumsy Laborer",b="Gordo is an abomination who trudges back and forth along the countryside between Deathknell and Brill. While abominations excel at brute combat and heavy hauling, their massive, sutured hands make fine manipulation almost impossible. Sent into the meadows to gather ingredients for the Royal Apothecary Society, Gordo quickly realizes his blunt fingers crush more stems than they pluck, prompting him to bully or bribe passersby into doing the tedious work for him.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Frustrations",b="Junior Apothecary Holland awaits the delivery in the graveyard behind Brill's town hall, but the errand goes awry. Gordo completely misunderstands his orders, directing travelers to collect harmless Gloom Weed instead of the volatile Doom Weed required for alchemical research. Holland is thoroughly exasperated by the stitched giant's incompetence, treating the mistaken delivery as proof of the abomination's uselessness before immediately assigning the player to correct the error.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Gordo?",a="Gordo is an abomination bound to the service of the Royal Apothecary Society. He patrols the meadows west of Brill, attempting to complete labor tasks assigned by his master, Junior Apothecary Holland.",al={"who is gordo","gordo tirisfal","gordo npc","what is gordo"}},{q="Why does Gordo need help gathering weeds?",a="Gordo's hands are enormous, clumsy appendages of stitched dead flesh. He simply lacks the dexterity required to pick delicate plants without ruining them, so he recruits traveling Forsaken adventurers to gather the flora instead.",al={"why does gordo need weeds","why can't gordo pick weeds","gordo hands"}},{q="Who is Master Holland?",a="Junior Apothecary Holland is an alchemist with the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in the Brill graveyard. He oversees Gordo and conducts research on the local flora and blighted soil to aid the Forsaken war effort.",al={"master holland","who is holland","apothecary holland"}},{q="Why is Holland upset when the Gloom Weed is delivered?",a="Holland never wanted Gloom Weed. Gordo completely misunderstood his orders and sent adventurers after the wrong plant. Holland actually needed Doom Weed, a far more potent and dangerous ingredient for his concoctions.",al={"why is holland mad","gloom weed mistake","wrong weed"},sp=1},{q="Where can Gloom Weed be found?",a="Gloom Weed sprouts low to the ground in the wild fields between Deathknell and Brill, particularly in the open meadows east of the Solliden Farmstead.",al={"where to find gloom weed","gloom weed locations","finding gloom weed"}},{q="What happens after completing Gordo's Task?",a="Upon receiving the useless Gloom Weed, Junior Apothecary Holland immediately sends you back out into the fields on the quest 'Doom Weed' to gather the actual volatile plants he originally requested.",al={"what comes next","gordo's task follow up","next quest after gordo"},sp=1}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="Trained herbalists will find this task effortless, as their tracking sense easily highlights Gloom Weed patches nestled amidst the blighted grass.",["race:Undead"]="For newly risen Forsaken leaving Deathknell, this task provides a first encounter with the clunky realities of abomination labor and the sharp temper of the Royal Apothecary Society."},kw={"abomination","apothecary","brill","doom weed","gloom weed","gordo","holland","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","subzone:deathknell","subzone:solliden-farmstead","topic:horde"},m={level="5",faction="Horde",id=5481},src={"Gordo's Task (Classic)"}}
E["quest:5650"] = {t="quest",n="Garments of Darkness",z="tirisfal",s="Garments of Darkness is a foundational rite of passage for fledgling Forsaken priests in Brill. Dark Cleric Beryl tasks initiates with healing and fortifying an injured Deathguard, testing their grasp of supportive magics before they delve deeper into the shadows.",h="Garments of Darkness is a foundational rite of passage for fledgling Forsaken priests in Brill.",sec={{t="A Balance of Dark and Light",b="While the Forsaken priesthood draws renown and distinct identity from shadow and darkness, its elders recognize the enduring pragmatic necessity of restoration. Dark Cleric Beryl teaches that understanding the dark demands an understanding of the light and restorative arts. A priest who seeks only ruin is cautioned to study arcane magic instead; the priesthood's true calling involves strengthening and preserving comrades just as much as afflicting enemies.",sp=0},{t="A Duty in the Graveyard",b="To demonstrate mastery, the initiate is sent north of Brill's cemetery to aid Deathguard Kel. Stationed against prowling gnoll packs, Kel has sustained injuries holding the line. By binding his wounds with healing spells and bolstering his stamina with protective enchantments, the acolyte proves capable of maintaining the defenders of Tirisfal Glades, earning Beryl's vestment and acceptance into the priesthood's higher mysteries.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why do Forsaken priests use healing magic if their power comes from darkness?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl explains that while Forsaken priests draw exceptional strength from shadow, healing remains essential. Before mastering darkness, an acolyte must understand supportive and restorative magic to keep Forsaken defenders standing on the battlefield.",al={"why do undead heal","forsaken priest healing lore","shadow vs light undead"}},{q="Who is Deathguard Kel?",a="Deathguard Kel is a Forsaken sentry stationed north of the cemetery in Brill. He defends the local settlements against aggressive gnoll packs wandering the woods and requires aid when injured in the line of duty.",al={"deathguard kel lore","who is deathguard kel","wounded deathguard"}},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl, the priest trainer located in Brill within Tirisfal Glades, offers the quest after you complete the preliminary task, In Favor of Darkness.",al={"who starts garments of darkness","garments of darkness quest giver"}},{q="What vestments are granted upon finishing the trial?",a="Beryl awards a tailored robe as a badge of station and accomplishment, symbolizing that the priest has mastered their fundamental duties and is recognized by their peers.",al={"what robe do you get","garments reward priest"}},{q="What threats was Deathguard Kel fighting?",a="Kel was wounded while fighting the local gnolls that infest the surrounding wilderness of Tirisfal Glades north of the Brill cemetery.",al={"what attacked kel","kel gnolls"}},{q="What darker powers does Dark Cleric Beryl hint at?",a="Beryl hints at shadow techniques unique to the Forsaken priesthood—distinctive manifestations of shadow magic and mental affliction not practiced by priests of other races.",al={"forsaken priest unique spells","darker powers hint"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This rite encapsulates the Forsaken philosophy of the priesthood: balancing the grim utility of shadow with the irreplaceable duty of fortifying and healing allies.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, healing magic is a pragmatic tool of survival used to sustain front-line soldiers like Deathguard Kel against gnolls and Scourge remnants."},kw={"brill","dark cleric beryl","deathguard kel","fortitude","garments of darkness","lesser heal","priest","shadow","tirisfal glades"},rel={"quest:5651","npc:dark-cleric-beryl","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:light","topic:gnoll"},m={start="Dark Cleric Beryl",level="4",faction="Horde",id=5650},src={"Garments of Darkness"}}
E["quest:5651"] = {t="quest",n="In Favor of Darkness",z="tirisfal",s="In Favor of Darkness marks a Forsaken priest's transition beyond the starting crypts of Deathknell toward advanced instruction in Brill. Entrusted by Dark Cleric Duesten, the fledgling disciple travels to study under Dark Cleric Beryl to master the delicate balance between the Holy Light and the Shadow.",h="In Favor of Darkness marks a Forsaken priest's transition beyond the starting crypts of Deathknell toward...",sec={{t="A Path Carved in Rot",b="While priests of other races revere the Holy Light as an unblemished source of moral virtue, the Forsaken approach faith through the harsh lens of their own undeath. As Dark Cleric Duesten teaches, the Forsaken were forged in corruption and discarded like carrion. Their survival demands understanding both Light and Shadow without sentimentality. In Favor of Darkness directs new disciples out of Deathknell's cloistered graveyard to confront the wider reality awaiting them in Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0},{t="Instruction in Brill",b="The road leading northeast out of Deathknell brings the fledgling priest over a wooden covered bridge and into the ruined hamlet of Brill. There, in the upper quarters of the local inn, Dark Cleric Beryl waits to test the initiate's resolve. Beryl values ambition and cold practicality over blind devotion, demanding that a Forsaken priest wield divine power as a weapon and a tool rather than a moral crutch.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It serves as a rite of passage for Forsaken priests leaving Deathknell. Dark Cleric Duesten sends you to Dark Cleric Beryl in Brill to continue your training and receive your next priestly challenge.",al={"what does this quest do","why in favor of darkness","in favor of darkness purpose"}},{q="Why do Forsaken priests use the Light if they embrace darkness?",a="Forsaken clerics acknowledge that the world operates on a balance between Light and Shadow. Even though the Holy Light causes excruciating pain to undead flesh and their origins lie in rot and darkness, they study both forces out of practicality and necessity.",al={"why do undead priests use light","forsaken priest lore","light and shadow undead"}},{q="Where do I find Dark Cleric Beryl?",a="Dark Cleric Beryl is located in the town of Brill, northeast of Deathknell. She resides on the second floor of the Gallows' End Tavern on the eastern side of the settlement.",al={"where is dark cleric beryl","beryl location","find beryl"}},{q="What does this quest lead into?",a="Speaking with Dark Cleric Beryl completes this task and opens the follow-up quest, Garments of Darkness, where she tests your ability to mend and sustain allies using your newfound disciplines.",al={"what comes next","next quest after in favor of darkness","in favor of darkness followup"}},{q="Who is Dark Cleric Duesten?",a="Dark Cleric Duesten is the priest trainer stationed in Deathknell. He guides newly awakened Forsaken priests in understanding their painful existence and utilizing their spiritual powers.",al={"who gives this quest","duesten lore","dark cleric duesten"}},{q="Why does Beryl mention ambition over faith?",a="Forsaken priests view traditional pious faith as insufficient after being abandoned by the powers they worshipped in life. Dark Cleric Beryl expects disciples to rely on personal ambition, urgency, and practical strength to survive.",al={"beryl dialogue meaning","why ambition not faith","forsaken faith"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="This quest encapsulates the fundamental philosophy of Forsaken priesthood: wielding both Holy Light and Shadow with cold discretion rather than religious reverence.",["race:Undead"]="The journey from Deathknell to Brill is the standard first excursion into the broader Forsaken realm, showing initiates how their people rebuild in the ruins of Lordaeron."},kw={"beryl","brill","deathknell","duesten","light","priest","shadow","tirisfal"},rel={"quest:5650","npc:dark-cleric-beryl","subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:light"},m={start="Dark Cleric Duesten",["end"]="Dark Cleric Beryl",level="4",faction="Horde",id=5651},src={"In Favor of Darkness"}}
E["quest:5847"] = {t="quest",n="Welcome!",z="tirisfal",s="This errand delivers a unique gift voucher to Claire Willower in the Forsaken hamlet of Brill. Honoring notable travelers upon their arrival in Tirisfal Glades, the gesture grants a rare miniature companion to accompany them through Azeroth. It marks one of the warmest greetings an undead traveler will find in these shadowy lands.",h="This errand delivers a unique gift voucher to Claire Willower in the Forsaken hamlet of Brill.",sec={{t="A Rare Greeting in Brill",b="Newly arisen travelers making their way south from Deathknell eventually cross the mist-laden road into Brill. Among the somber alchemists and bitter magistrates, Claire Willower stands ready to greet specific heroes who carry an unusual token of patronage. Exchanging the voucher provides a harmless pet to follow along on the long journey ahead.",sp=0},{t="A Touch of Warmth in Tirisfal",b="Tirisfal Glades is an inhospitable expanse haunted by Scourge remnants, zealous crusaders, and rot. Having a dedicated small companion following at one's heels offers a strange sliver of cheer amid the dreary decay of Lordaeron's fallen heartlands.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It allows newly arrived adventurers who possess a special voucher to exchange it with Claire Willower in Brill for a unique miniature pet to accompany them on their travels.",al={"why do i have this voucher","what does this quest do","brill gift voucher quest"}},{q="Who is Claire Willower?",a="Claire Willower is a Forsaken resident stationed in the town of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. She collects these unique vouchers and distributes exotic pets to travelers.",al={"where is claire willower","who takes the voucher in brill","claire willower"}},{q="Where do you turn in the voucher?",a="The voucher is turned in directly to Claire Willower inside the town of Brill, just a short walk south from the starting crypts of Deathknell.",al={"where to turn in brill gift voucher","turn in location","voucher drop off"}},{q="Is this quest available to everyone?",a="No. The starting voucher is only carried by specific adventurers arriving in Azeroth with recognized patronage, specifically from the collector's edition of the journey.",al={"who gets this quest","why don't i have this quest","how do you get the voucher"}},{q="What kind of companions can you receive?",a="Turning in the voucher lets you choose a small vanity pet, such as a miniature diablo, a panda cub, or a zergling leash, providing a harmless companion on your adventures.",al={"what are the pets","what gift do i get","pet choices"}},{q="Does this companion fight in combat?",a="No. The companion is entirely passive, following you as an ornamental companion rather than participating in battles.",al={"do collector pets fight","pet combat abilities","can pet attack"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, whose existence is marked by blight, rot, and vengeance, traveling with a playful companion is a bizarrely wholesome diversion on the road across Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="Brill serves as the primary gateway for Horde adventurers operating in northern Eastern Kingdoms, making Claire Willower's station a prominent stop for incoming travelers."},kw={"brill","claire willower","collector","companion","gift voucher","pet","tirisfal glades","welcome"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Brill Gift Voucher",["end"]="Claire Willower",level="1",faction="Horde",id=5847},src={"Welcome! (Brill)"}}
E["quest:8652"] = {t="quest",n="Graveborn the Elder",z="tirisfal",s="Graveborn the Elder is a Lunar Festival encounter situated near the town of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. During the celebration, travelers seek out Elder Graveborn among the blighted groves to honor the ancient forebears of Azeroth. Paying respects to this spirit earns his blessing and a token of the holiday.",h="Graveborn the Elder is a Lunar Festival encounter situated near the town of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Ghostly Vigil in Brill",b="While the Forsaken dwell among ruined manors and grave sites in Tirisfal Glades, the Lunar Festival brings an unexpected communion with ancient times. Elder Graveborn appears as a spectral elder stationed just outside Brill. Even in a realm shattered by the Scourge and reclaimed by the undead, he welcomes pilgrims who pause to honor the ancient ways.",sp=0},{t="Honoring the Olden Races",b="The Lunar Festival marks a time when the great spirits of long-past eras return to offer wisdom and gratitude. When travelers approach Elder Graveborn, he remarks on how heartening it is that the inhabitants of Tirisfal still offer homage to the ancestors despite the land's current decay, bestowing a Coin of Ancestry upon those who greet him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Elder Graveborn located?",a="Elder Graveborn is found near the settlement of Brill in Tirisfal Glades, standing quietly near the roadside outside the town.",al={"elder graveborn location","where is graveborn","graveborn coords"}},{q="What happens when you speak to Elder Graveborn?",a="Upon greeting him, Elder Graveborn commends you for honoring the ancient peoples of Azeroth and awards a Coin of Ancestry as part of the Lunar Festival celebrations.",al={"graveborn reward","lunar festival graveborn","what does he give you"}},{q="Why is an ancient elder standing in Tirisfal Glades?",a="During the Lunar Festival, the spirits of ancient ancestors manifest across all of Azeroth, from the kaldorei forests to lands torn by war and plague. Elder Graveborn watches over the northern reaches of Lordaeron to ensure its history is not entirely eclipsed by death.",al={"why is he in tirisfal","graveborn lore","who is elder graveborn"}},{q="Can Alliance players visit Elder Graveborn?",a="Elder Graveborn himself is a neutral spirit of wisdom and will speak with members of both the Alliance and the Horde. However, because he is right outside the Forsaken town of Brill, Alliance adventurers must beware the local guards.",al={"can alliance talk to graveborn","alliance graveborn the elder","graveborn hostile"}},{q="What is the Coin of Ancestry used for?",a="Coins of Ancestry gathered from elders like Graveborn can be traded in Moonglade during the Lunar Festival for festive garments, firework recipes, and other celebratory tokens.",al={"coin of ancestry use","what are lunar coins for"}},{q="Is Elder Graveborn one of the Forsaken?",a="No. Despite his name and ghostly visage near Brill, Elder Graveborn is one of the ancient spirits celebrated during the Lunar Festival, belonging to the long lineage of Azeroth's elders rather than Sylvanas's Forsaken.",al={"is graveborn undead","is elder graveborn forsaken"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken living in Brill, the arrival of ancient ancestral spirits provides a stark reminder of Azeroth's deeper history beyond the recent tragedies of the Scourge.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers seeking out Elder Graveborn must tread carefully through Tirisfal Glades, as Brill is a heavily fortified Forsaken haven.",["class:Druid"]="Druids reverence the Lunar Festival elders as links to the ancient world before the Sundering, heedless of the troubled faction boundaries they inhabit."},kw={"brill","coin of ancestry","elder graveborn","graveborn","lunar festival","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:elder-graveborn","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Elder Graveborn",id=8652},src={"Graveborn the Elder"}}
E["quest:86784"] = {t="quest",n="Sticks and Bones",z="tirisfal",s="Sticks and Bones is a local task offered by Deathguard Bartholomew in Tirisfal Glades. He sends travelers to gather dry branches across the blighted woodland to deliver to Eleanor Shackleton, an experienced survivalist camped in the western hills.",h="Sticks and Bones is a local task offered by Deathguard Bartholomew in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Friendly Gesture",b="While Deathguards in Tirisfal Glades are usually consumed by military patrol duty and guarding against the Scourge or Scarlet crusaders, Deathguard Bartholomew takes a moment to look out for an acquaintance. Knowing that Eleanor Shackleton spends her unlife out in the harsh elements, he encourages passing adventurers to collect dry branches for her camp fire.",sp=0},{t="Life in the Wilds",b="Eleanor Shackleton prides herself on surviving the blighted wilderness of Tirisfal alone. Despite being undead, the Forsaken still feel the damp, bitter chill that rolls off the northern moors. Eleanor's philosophy on wood gathering is simple: whenever you think you have collected enough firewood, collect five times more. Grateful for the extra timber, she lets the courier keep Bartholomew's basket and shares the warmth of her fire.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who starts the quest Sticks and Bones?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew in Tirisfal Glades gives this task to passing adventurers, asking them to help his associate Eleanor Shackleton.",al={"who gives sticks and bones","sticks and bones quest starter"}},{q="Where is Eleanor Shackleton camped?",a="Eleanor Shackleton maintains a small camp out in the hills to the west in Tirisfal Glades, surviving the elements away from the settlements.",al={"eleanor shackleton location","where is eleanor","where to turn in sticks and bones"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken need firewood if they are undead?",a="While the Forsaken do not freeze to death like the living, they still feel the persistent damp and bitter cold of the Tirisfal wilderness. A campfire provides comfort, keeps their stiff joints warm, and maintains a livable camp in the wilds.",al={"do undead get cold","why firewood for undead","forsaken cold"}},{q="What advice does Eleanor give about gathering wood?",a="According to Deathguard Bartholomew, Eleanor's golden survival rule is: 'When you think you have enough firewood, gather five times more.'",al={"eleanor firewood rule","eleanor advice"}},{q="What item do you use to collect the branches?",a="Deathguard Bartholomew provides a collecting basket to carry the six dry branches found across the glades, which Eleanor lets you keep upon completing the delivery.",al={"basket for dry branch","how to gather branches"}},{q="Does this quest lead to further survival training?",a="Eleanor welcomes you to her camp and shares advice on traveling the wilds as an adventurer, providing a friendly contact point in the Tirisfal wilderness.",al={"sticks and bones followup","what does eleanor do next"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Even in Lordaeron's blighted woods, Forsaken travelers like Eleanor Shackleton must adapt the old habits of survival to their new unlife.",["faction:Horde"]="Outlying campers like Eleanor offer friendly stopping points for young Horde adventurers striking out across Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"collecting basket","deathguard bartholomew","dry branch","eleanor shackleton","firewood","sticks and bones","survival","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:deathguard-bartholomew","npc:eleanor-shackleton","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Deathguard Bartholomew",["end"]="Eleanor Shackleton",level="7",faction="Horde",id=86784},src={"Sticks and Bones (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:90902"] = {t="quest",n="Rediscovering the Light",z="tirisfal",s="Offered by Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell, this task challenges newly raised Forsaken paladins to embrace the Holy Light once more. Calling upon holy powers inflicts intense agony upon undead flesh, requiring fledgling paladins to channel healing into injured Deathguards despite the burning torment.",h="Offered by Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell, this task challenges newly raised Forsaken paladins to embrace...",sec={{t="A Painful Reunion",b="For former champions of the Silver Hand and fallen knights of Lordaeron, awakening in undeath means confronting a horrifying reality: the Holy Light still answers their call, but it burns their withered bodies from within. Aramis Hammerhand instructs newly risen Forsaken paladins that abilities once practiced as second nature now bring excruciating pain. Because holy energy naturally conflicts with the foul magic sustaining undeath, channeling the Light requires raw willpower and agonizing perseverance.",sp=0},{t="Purification Through Suffering",b="Rather than allowing this torment to deter them, Forsaken paladins view the pain as an enduring testament of faith. Deathguard throughout Deathknell suffer grievous wounds combating mindless zombies, and it falls upon these undead knights to restore them. Aramis teaches that pushing through the burning pain is like exercising an atrophied muscle—the agony itself is treated as a badge of honor and living proof that the Light has not forsaken them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does using the Light hurt Forsaken paladins?",a="The Holy Light is fundamentally opposed to the necrotic energies that sustain undeath. While a Forsaken's will and conviction allow them to channel the power of the Light, circulating that sacred energy through dead flesh inflicts excruciating, burning pain.",al={"why does light hurt undead","holy light burning undead","why pain when healing"}},{q="Who is Aramis Hammerhand?",a="Aramis Hammerhand is an undead paladin trainer stationed in Deathknell. He guides newly risen Forsaken paladins as they reforge their shattered connection to the Holy Light.",al={"who is aramis hammerhand","aramis hammerhand lore","quest giver"}},{q="Why are the Deathguards in Deathknell injured?",a="The Deathguard are the soldiers defending Deathknell from mindless undead, feral Scourge remnants, and hostile wildlife that surround the settlement as the newly risen awaken from their graves.",al={"why are deathguards hurt","injured deathguard lore","deathknell defenders"}},{q="Can undead naturally wield the Holy Light?",a="Yes, provided they retain the faith, willpower, and memory of their former vows. The Light responds to genuine conviction, though it exacts a brutal physical toll upon dead bodies.",al={"can forsaken be paladins","undead using the light","forsaken paladin lore"}},{q="What does Aramis mean when he calls pain a badge of honor?",a="Aramis views the burning agony not as a curse, but as undeniable proof that the Light still listens. Forsaken paladins endure the searing heat of their spells to demonstrate their unyielding loyalty and purpose.",al={"pain purifying property","badge of honor meaning","aramis speech"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="It takes place entirely within Deathknell, the secluded starter haven in northwestern Tirisfal Glades where newly raised Forsaken first emerge into their undead existence.",al={"where is this quest","quest location","deathknell quest"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For an undead paladin, reconnecting with the Light is a crucible of faith and endurance, proving that holy vows can survive death itself despite the blistering agony it brings.",["race:Undead"]="This rite demonstrates the fierce resilience of the Forsaken, who turn even the searing torment of the Light into a disciplined weapon for their survival."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","deathguard","deathknell","forsaken paladin","holy light","rediscovering the light","tirisfal glades","undead paladin"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","subzone:deathknell","topic:light","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",level="2",faction="Horde",id=90902},src={"Rediscovering the Light"},fv=true}
E["quest:91208"] = {t="quest",n="Coming to Terms",z="tirisfal",s="Offered by Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell, this quest tasks newly risen paladins with reaching out to a fellow knight struggling to accept undeath. Fleeing into the hills in terror, the newly returned warrior faces the agonizing realization of becoming what she once fought against.",h="Offered by Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell, this quest tasks newly risen paladins with reaching out to a...",sec={{t="A Bitter Resurrection",b="Awakening from death into the ranks of the Forsaken is jarring for anyone, but for former paladins of the Silver Hand, the shock is visceral. Having dedicated their mortal lives to destroying the undead in service to the Holy Light, these individuals suddenly find their souls tethered back to decomposing flesh. While some adapt under the guidance of Aramis Hammerhand, others are overwhelmed by horror and confusion, fleeing into the Tirisfal wilderness rather than confronting their grim new existence.",sp=0},{t="A Merciful Release",b="Aramis Hammerhand hopes that a fellow knight can reach the panicked paladin who hid in the hills west of the chapel with compassion and understanding. Tragically, the weight of the transformation drives her into complete madness. When approached, she lashes out blindly in fear and fury, leaving no choice but to strike her down. For those Forsaken whose minds shatter upon the grave, a swift end is the only remaining mercy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the frightened paladin?",a="She is a recently risen Forsaken who practiced as a paladin in life. Overcome with dread upon waking as an undead creature, she fled Deathknell into the nearby western hills in total panic.",al={"frightened paladin","who is the paladin in the hills","who do i find in coming to terms"}},{q="Why does the frightened paladin attack?",a="The psychological agony of waking up as the exact monster she spent her life battling shatters her sanity. Consumed by terror and madness, she cannot be reasoned with and violently attacks anyone who tries to reach out.",al={"why does she turn hostile","why attack","can you save the frightened paladin"},sp=1},{q="Who gives the quest Coming to Terms?",a="Aramis Hammerhand, a paladin mentor situated at the church in Deathknell, offers the task to newly risen knights who need to understand the fragile mental state of their resurrected peers.",al={"quest giver coming to terms","aramis hammerhand quest","where to start coming to terms"}},{q="Can Forsaken still wield the Light?",a="Yes, through profound willpower and faith, though channeling holy energy causes intense physical agony to an undead vessel. Mentors like Aramis Hammerhand strive to preserve their spiritual bonds despite the pain of their condition.",al={"undead paladins light","do forsaken paladins use the light","undead use light"}},{q="Where is the frightened paladin located?",a="She fled directly west from the church in Deathknell, hiding among the wooded hills overlooking the settlement.",al={"frightened paladin location","where is she","where in deathknell"}},{q="What happens after completing Coming to Terms?",a="After reporting the tragic outcome to Aramis Hammerhand, he offers a prayer for her departed soul and directs you toward further training to hone your discipline as a Forsaken paladin.",al={"next quest coming to terms","after coming to terms"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="This task strikes at the heart of the paladin's dilemma in undeath: confronting the horror of having become what you were sworn to purge.",["race:Undead"]="The psychological toll of awakening in Tirisfal breaks many minds; dealing with those lost to panic is a tragic reality of early Forsaken life."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","coming to terms","deathknell","frightened paladin","holy light","paladin","tirisfal glades","undead paladin"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","quest:91209","subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","topic:light","zone:tirisfal","quest:6381"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",level="4",faction="Horde",id=91208},src={"Coming to Terms (quest)"},fv=true}
E["quest:91209"] = {t="quest",n="Continue Your Training",z="tirisfal",s="This quest directs newly risen Forsaken paladins to leave Deathknell and travel to Brill for advanced instruction. Entrusted by Aramis Hammerhand, the journey introduces the fledgling holy warrior to the wider perils of Tirisfal Glades. It also serves as a stark warning about the deep suspicion that holy practitioners face among the undead.",h="This quest directs newly risen Forsaken paladins to leave Deathknell and travel to Brill for advanced...",sec={{t="Leaving Deathknell",b="Once a newly awakened soul has mastered the rudiments of martial combat and channelled holy power within Deathknell's cloistered graveyard, Aramis Hammerhand sends them east into the broader expanse of Tirisfal Glades. Their destination is Brill, a bustling regional outpost serving as the administrative hub for central Tirisfal. There, Shari Stilwell oversees the advancement of those who dare walk the path of the paladin in undeath.",sp=0},{t="A Precarious Calling",b="Aramis offers parting advice that underlines the fraught reality of being an undead paladin. While Lordaeron still requires defenders against external threats, wielding the Holy Light under Sylvanas Windrunner's banner draws bitter suspicion. Countless Forsaken suffered agony or death at the hands of holy zealots, and the mere presence of the Light breeds distrust among their undead peers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where do I find them?",a="The quest is provided by Aramis Hammerhand, the paladin trainer stationed in Deathknell within Tirisfal Glades.",al={"quest giver","where to start","aramis hammerhand location"}},{q="Where do I turn in Continue Your Training?",a="You turn the quest in to Shari Stilwell, the paladin trainer located in the town of Brill, just east along the main road from Deathknell.",al={"where to turn in","shari stilwell location","turn in spot"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken distrust paladins?",a="Many Forsaken hold deep-seated grudges against the Holy Light, both because of the agony it causes undead bodies and due to brutal persecution by holy orders like the Scarlet Crusade. Walking the path of a paladin puts one in uncomfortable proximity to forces most undead fear or despise.",al={"why do undead hate paladins","forsaken paladin prejudice","proximity to light"}},{q="Can any Forsaken class take this quest?",a="No. This quest is explicitly the introductory transition quest for Forsaken paladins moving from the starting grounds of Deathknell to the wider world at Brill.",al={"is this quest paladin only","class requirement"}},{q="What is Brill?",a="Brill is a key town in central Tirisfal Glades serving as the primary hub for Forsaken travelers, guards, and tradesfolk just north of the Undercity ruins.",al={"what is brill","brill town lore"}},{q="What threats does Lordaeron face according to Aramis?",a="Though shattered, Lordaeron remains under constant threat from rampaging Scourge remnants, hostile wildlife, and vengeful living factions such as the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"threats to lordaeron","why protect lordaeron"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For an undead paladin, this transition is a sobering reminder that wielding holy power makes you an outsider even among your fellow Forsaken.",["race:Undead"]="The quest highlights the internal tensions within Forsaken society, where loyalty to Lordaeron's soil clashes with lingering trauma surrounding the Holy Light."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","brill","continue your training","deathknell","forsaken paladin","holy light","shari stilwell","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","npc:shari-stilwell","subzone:deathknell","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:light","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",["end"]="Shari Stilwell",level="4",faction="Horde",id=91209},src={"Continue Your Training"},fv=true}
E["quest:96656"] = {t="quest",n="The Adventurer",z="tirisfal",s="The Adventurer is an introductory task given by Executor Arren to seasoned young Forsaken champions outside Deathknell. Having proven reliable in strikes against the Scarlet Crusade, you are dispatched up the road toward Brill to investigate a stranger lingering near the settlement. Rather than uncovering another zealot spy, the task introduces you to Eleanor Shackleton, an independent traveler eager to teach the practical survival skills of the wild.",h="The Adventurer is an introductory task given by Executor Arren to seasoned young Forsaken champions outside...",sec={{t="A Suspicious Watch",b="Executor Arren maintains a vigilant watch over Deathknell and the surrounding approaches. With Scarlet Crusaders actively spying on the region and infiltrating northern Lordaeron, any newcomer spotted wandering near Brill warrants immediate scrutiny. Having demonstrated your dedication by eliminating crusader threats along the border, Arren turns to you to investigate the unknown figure quietly, determining whether she poses a hidden danger to the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="A Traveler in the Woods",b="Upon tracking down Eleanor Shackleton along the roadside near Brill, her intentions prove far removed from Crusade fanatical plots or Scourge necromancy. An independent traveler pausing before her next journey into the wilds, Eleanor harbors no hostility toward the risen dead. Instead, she recognizes the spark of an adventurer in those sent to check on her, offering to share the practical essentials of surviving open wilderness and making camp.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Executor Arren want Eleanor investigated?",a="Deathknell and Brill are constantly threatened by Scarlet Crusade infiltrators and hostile spies. Anyone unfamiliar lurking along the high road is treated with suspicion until their motives are proven benign.",al={"why investigate eleanor","who sent me to eleanor","arren eleanor task"}},{q="Who is Eleanor Shackleton?",a="Eleanor Shackleton is an independent adventurer camping along the road near Brill. She has no loyalty to the Scarlet Crusade and is focused purely on exploring the wilderness and sharing survival know-how with fellow travelers.",al={"who is eleanor","eleanor shackleton lore","who is the adventurer npc"}},{q="Is Eleanor connected to the Scarlet Crusade?",a="No. Upon arriving at her camp, Eleanor quickly clarifies that she has no affiliation whatsoever with the zealous crusaders threatening Tirisfal Glades.",al={"is eleanor scarlet crusade","eleanor enemy","is eleanor a spy"}},{q="Where does this quest lead?",a="Reporting to Eleanor opens the quest 'The Great Outdoors,' where she begins teaching you the basics of wilderness survival and setting up camp.",al={"what comes after the adventurer","next quest after adventurer","eleanor shackleton follow up"}},{q="Where can Eleanor Shackleton be found?",a="She makes her camp just off the main road leading east toward the town of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"eleanor location","where is eleanor shackleton","eleanor camp tirisfal"}},{q="Why did Executor Arren choose you for this mission?",a="You earned Arren's trust through your successful service rooting out Scarlet Crusade agents and messengers near Deathknell, proving you can handle sensitive reconnaissance.",al={"why pick me","arren trust","why executor arren sends you"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For fresh Forsaken venturing beyond Deathknell, meeting neutral travelers like Eleanor is an early lesson that not every living mortal in Lordaeron immediately raises a weapon against the reclaimed dead.",["faction:Horde"]="While Executor Arren guards the fledgling borders of the Forsaken realm, opening peaceful dialogue with wandering survivalists secures valuable practical skills for Horde initiates."},kw={"brill","camping","deathknell","eleanor shackleton","executor arren","scarlet crusade","the adventurer","the great outdoors","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:eleanor-shackleton","npc:executor-arren","quest:96607","subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:scarlet-crusade"},m={start="Executor Arren",["end"]="Eleanor Shackleton",level="6",faction="Horde",id=96656},src={"The Adventurer (Tirisfal Glades)"},fv=true}
E["quest:98389"] = {t="quest",n="A Light in the Darkness",z="tirisfal",s="Offered by Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell, this quest tasks Forsaken adventurers with rescuing newly raised undead trapped in Night's Web Hollow. It highlights the delicate relationship between undead wielders of the Holy Light and a populace that deeply distrusts them. By aiding their fallen kin, these holy practitioners hope to prove their loyalty to Sylvanas and the Forsaken cause.",h="Offered by Aramis Hammerhand in Deathknell, this quest tasks Forsaken adventurers with rescuing newly raised...",sec={{t="A Precarious Faith",b="The Holy Light is notoriously agonizing and hazardous to the undead, yet some Forsaken retain their connection to the sacred magic they wielded in life. In Deathknell, figures like Aramis Hammerhand strive to demonstrate that their faith has not turned them against their people. To combat the suspicion that holy practitioners will turn on other undead as monstrosities, they actively use their abilities and compassion to safeguard their kin.",sp=0},{t="Night's Web Hollow",b="Northwest of Deathknell lies Night's Web Hollow, a dank cavern crawling with vicious spiders. Freshly raised undead, still disoriented by their awakening and lacking the wits to defend themselves, frequently stumble into the hollow and end up cocooned in sticky webbing. Rescuing these unfortunate Forsaken serves a dual purpose: saving new recruits for the Dark Lady and proving to leaders like Executor Arren that practitioners of the Light are devoted servants of the Forsaken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Light in the Darkness?",a="The quest is given by Aramis Hammerhand, a holy practitioner stationed in Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"quest giver","who starts a light in the darkness","aramis hammerhand quest"}},{q="Where is Night's Web Hollow located?",a="Night's Web Hollow is located northwest of Deathknell within the hills of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"nights web hollow location","where are the webbed victims","where is the cave"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken distrust wielders of the Light?",a="The Holy Light is deeply searing and dangerous to undead flesh. Many Forsaken fear that anyone wielding holy powers might view them as abominations to be eradicated rather than brethren to be embraced.",al={"why fear the light","why do forsaken hate paladins","forsaken holy fear"}},{q="Who are the victims trapped in the webs?",a="The victims inside the cocoons are newly awakened Forsaken adventurers who blundered into the spider caves before finding their bearings.",al={"who is webbed","what is inside the webs","trapped victims"}},{q="Who is Executor Arren, and why does Aramis want to impress him?",a="Executor Arren oversees military and civic order in Deathknell. Gaining his trust is essential for holy wielders who wish to integrate smoothly into the Forsaken forces.",al={"who is executor arren","why arren matters"}},{q="Can the undead really wield the Holy Light?",a="Yes, through incredible willpower and devotion, some undead retain their bond with the Light, even though channeling it causes immense discomfort and their own society views them with suspicion.",al={"can forsaken use light","undead light lore"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This task demonstrates the complex internal struggles of the Forsaken, showing how individuals can overcome prejudice among their own freshly risen people.",["class:Priest"]="For Forsaken who channel holy energy, this mission illustrates the delicate tightrope walked between lingering mortal faith and the harsh reality of undeath."},kw={"aramis hammerhand","deathknell","executor arren","forsaken","holy light","night's web hollow","tirisfal glades","webbed victims"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","subzone:deathknell","npc:executor-arren","topic:light","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Aramis Hammerhand",level="4",faction="Horde",id=98389},src={"A Light in the Darkness (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:98601"] = {t="quest",n="A Difficult Path",z="tirisfal",s="A Difficult Path marks the formal beginning of a Forsaken paladin's training in Deathknell. After dealing with the mindless undead rising from the crypts, newly awakened champions of the Light are directed to Aramis Hammerhand within the village church to confront the agonizing reality of wielding holy energy in undeath.",h="A Difficult Path marks the formal beginning of a Forsaken paladin's training in Deathknell.",sec={{t="A Reeking Scroll",b="When a freshly awakened Forsaken paladin finishes culling the feral undead outside the crypt, Shadow Priest Sarvis hands over an unexpected delivery. The Consecrated Scroll radiates holy energy so intensely that the shadow priest visibly recoils, bluntly asking the bearer to step aside. To a practitioner of shadow and decay, the very aura of the Holy Light feels like an open flame.",sp=0},{t="The Crucible of Holy Fire",b="Inside the desecrated church of Deathknell awaits Aramis Hammerhand, the Forsaken paladin trainer. Where other races wield the Light naturally and joyfully, undead who call upon it endure searing, visceral agony. Aramis makes no attempt to soften the blow: channeling holy power through a rotting vessel is sheer torment, but he demands his disciples embrace the pain rather than flinch away, using it as a crucible to temper their newfound resolve.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Shadow Priest Sarvis dislike the scroll?",a="Shadow Priest Sarvis is devoted to shadow magic and the preservation of his fellow undead. The Consecrated Scroll radiates pure holy energy, which is inherently hostile to undead flesh and deeply unsettling to practitioners of the Shadow.",al={"sarvis holy scroll","why is sarvis uneasy","shadow priest reacts to scroll"}},{q="Can Forsaken truly wield the Holy Light without dying?",a="Forsaken can wield the Light through sheer willpower and faith, but doing so causes them intense internal pain and rekindles deadened nerve endings, making them feel their own decay. It demands immense mental endurance to channel.",al={"forsaken paladins lore","undead using the light","does the light hurt forsaken"}},{q="Who is Aramis Hammerhand?",a="Aramis Hammerhand is the paladin trainer stationed in the Deathknell chapel. He guides newly risen Forsaken paladins, teaching them to withstand the agony of wielding the Light in undeath and forge it into an effective weapon.",al={"who is aramis hammerhand","deathknell paladin trainer","aramis role"}},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="The quest begins with Shadow Priest Sarvis in the central clearing of Deathknell and concludes just steps away inside the village's ruined chapel, where Aramis Hammerhand resides.",al={"where is a difficult path","quest location","where is deathknell church"}},{q="Do I have to read the Consecrated Scroll to complete the quest?",a="No, reading the scroll is not strictly required to complete the objective; speaking directly to Aramis Hammerhand inside the church will advance your training.",al={"read consecrated scroll","is scroll reading required","skip reading scroll"}},{q="Why is the path called 'difficult'?",a="The name reflects the brutal path of the Forsaken paladin. While other warriors of the Light draw comfort and solace from their faith, an undead paladin must withstand searing holy fire coursing through dead flesh every time they cast a blessing or strike.",al={"why difficult path","meaning of quest name"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="This quest represents the foundational trial of the Forsaken paladin, framing holy power not as an easy blessing, but as an agonizing crucible of discipline and endurance.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, calling upon the Light proves that devotion and discipline can survive physical death, even if the magic actively burns the vessel channeling it."},kw={"a difficult path","aramis hammerhand","consecrated scroll","deathknell","forsaken paladin","holy light","shadow priest sarvis","tirisfal glades"},rel={"npc:aramis-hammerhand","npc:shadow-priest-sarvis","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:light","topic:scourge"},m={start="Shadow Priest Sarvis",["end"]="Aramis Hammerhand",level="1",faction="Horde",id=98601},src={"A Difficult Path (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:99134"] = {t="quest",n="Discipline",z="tirisfal",s="Discipline is a task issued by Executor Zygand in Tirisfal Glades. Unimpressed by the competence of the local Deathguard garrison, Zygand commissions outside adventurers to administer physical punishment to slackening undead sentries.",h="Discipline is a task issued by Executor Zygand in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Enforcing Order in Undeath",b="The Deathguard form the military spine of the Forsaken across Lordaeron, but freedom from the Lich King's iron will brings its own complications: apathy, fatigue, and negligence. Taskmasters like Executor Zygand have little patience for slackening discipline, especially with threats from the Scarlet Crusade and Scourge prowling Tirisfal's borders. To keep the troops sharp, officers rely on blunt instruments and aggressive oversight to maintain military readiness.",sp=0},{t="The Executor's Ledger",b="Executor Zygand deliberately employs independent operators rather than ranks from within the garrison to administer his punishments. Using the Executor's Motivator, outsiders remind negligent Deathguards that survival in service to the Dark Lady requires absolute vigilance. Those who fail in their duties quickly learn that unlife offers no shelter from consequence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the Discipline quest?",a="Discipline is given by Executor Zygand, an exacting Forsaken officer stationed in Tirisfal Glades who oversees regional defenses and demands strict obedience from his troops.",al={"discipline quest giver","who starts discipline","executor zygand quest"}},{q="Why does Executor Zygand want the Deathguard punished?",a="Zygand views the Deathguards under his command as incompetent and lacking proper drive. Because complacency threatens Forsaken survival in Tirisfal, he enforces harsh discipline to shock the sentries into alertness.",al={"why hit deathguards","why motivate deathguard","zygand deathguard reason"}},{q="Why does Zygand use an adventurer instead of another soldier?",a="Zygand notes that as an outsider who is not yet part of the Deathguard, you have not had the opportunity to disappoint him. Employing a fresh hand also prevents internal garrison squabbles or soldiers showing mercy to their comrades.",al={"why me discipline","why use outsiders zygand"}},{q="What is the Executor's Motivator?",a="The Executor's Motivator is a punitive disciplinary tool provided by Executor Zygand. It is used to deliver a painful reprimand to idling Deathguards stationed across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"executors motivator","what is the motivator zygand"}},{q="What happens if you refuse Zygand's order?",a="Zygand warns that hesitation or refusal will result in your own name being inscribed in his ledger, marking you as the next target for someone else to discipline.",al={"zygand threats","ledger threat zygand"}},{q="How do the Forsaken view pain?",a="Though undead bodies are dulled to many sensations, sharp physical pain remains one of the few visceral feelings they retain. For officers like Zygand, inflicting and experiencing it serves as a morbid satisfaction and an effective motivator.",al={"do undead feel pain","forsaken pain lore"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, military discipline is a matter of species survival. Sentries who succumb to apathy endanger the entire territory of Tirisfal Glades.",["faction:Horde"]="The grim methods of Forsaken commanders illustrate the stark, unforgiving realities of life and governance within the northern reaches of the Horde."},kw={"dark lady","deathguard","discipline","executor zygand","forsaken","motivator","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","zone:tirisfal"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="6",faction="Horde",id=99134},src={"Discipline (Forever)"},fv=true}
E["quest:99141"] = {t="quest",n="Patience",z="tirisfal",s="Patience is a task assigned by Executor Zygand in Tirisfal Glades, demanding strict military accountability for the Dark Lady. With routine field reports overdue, Zygand dispatches an adventurer to collect updates from nearby Deathguards and an unusual sentry. The assignment highlights the rigorous, uncompromising discipline enforced across Forsaken holdings.",h="Patience is a task assigned by Executor Zygand in Tirisfal Glades, demanding strict military accountability...",sec={{t="Enforcing the Dark Lady's Will",b="Executor Zygand holds command over local security in Tirisfal Glades and tolerates no lapses in vigilance. To Zygand, serving Lady Sylvanas requires nothing less than absolute efficiency. When regular field dispatches fail to arrive at his post on schedule, he sees it as an unacceptable breach of duty rather than a minor delay. Rather than abandon his post to investigate, he sends incoming Forsaken agents to rein in delinquent subordinates and ensure that the borders remain secure.",sp=0},{t="Sentinels of the Glades",b="The dispatches involve sentries stationed at critical vantage points surrounding Brill. Deathguard Dillinger keeps watch over the graveyard to the west, where rogue undead and Scourge remnants often stir. To the east, Deathguard Kristof oversees a waystation guarding the approaches to the Capital City and the eastern roads. Most unusual among them is Gordo, a hulking abomination wandering near Stillwater Pond whose simple mind makes military record-keeping a deeply dubious expectation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Executor Zygand?",a="Executor Zygand is a high-ranking Forsaken officer tasked with maintaining order and defense around Brill in Tirisfal Glades. He answers directly to the command hierarchy serving Lady Sylvanas and demands flawless execution from all troops under his oversight.",al={"zygand","who is zygand","executor zygand role"}},{q="Why does Zygand send an adventurer to collect reports?",a="Several field sentries have failed to submit their scheduled reports on time. Lacking patience for delays and unwilling to abandon his central post, Zygand employs newly proven Forsaken to run down the overdue dispatches across the countryside.",al={"why do patience","why fetch reports"}},{q="Who is Gordo and why does he have a report?",a="Gordo is an abomination who wanders west near Stillwater Pond. Zygand expected a status report from him just like any other field sentry, though upon receiving it, the Executor quickly realizes that expecting written intelligence from an abomination was an embarrassing lapse in judgment.",al={"gordo","why does an abomination have a report","who is gordo"},sp=1},{q="Where is Deathguard Dillinger located?",a="Deathguard Dillinger is posted just west of Brill, standing watch near the local graveyard to monitor lingering Scourge activity and newly risen corpses.",al={"dillinger location","find dillinger","where is dillinger"}},{q="Where is Deathguard Kristof stationed?",a="Deathguard Kristof is stationed at the waystation along the road to the east of Brill, guarding the approaches against intruders and monitoring road traffic.",al={"kristof location","find kristof","where is kristof"}},{q="What happens when Gordo's report is turned in?",a="Executor Zygand concedes that expecting an abomination to produce a coherent written report was a foolish mistake. He quietly accepts the outcome and asks that the embarrassing oversight be kept strictly between you and him.",al={"gordo report outcome","gordo writing"},sp=1}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For newly liberated Forsaken, carrying out Zygand's orders reinforces the harsh realities of survival in Lordaeron: complete devotion to the Dark Lady and zero tolerance for failure.",["faction:Horde"]="The quest offers visiting Horde allies a glimpse into the grim, highly disciplined command structure that Sylvanas Windrunner's officers enforce throughout Tirisfal."},kw={"brill","dark lady","deathguard","dillinger","gordo","kristof","patience","stillwater pond","tirisfal glades","zygand"},rel={"npc:executor-zygand","npc:deathguard-dillinger","subzone:stillwater-pond","zone:tirisfal","quest:938"},m={start="Executor Zygand",level="6",faction="Horde",id=99141},src={"Patience (quest)"},fv=true}
E["subzone:agamand-family-crypt"] = {t="subzone",n="Agamand Family Crypt",z="tirisfal",s="Tucked into the hills just north of Agamand Mills, the Agamand Family Crypt is the ancient resting ground of one of Tirisfal's wealthiest farming dynasties. Now claimed by the Scourge under Captain Dargol, its tombs have been ripped open, and the slumbering ancestors raised as mindless terrors.",h="Tucked into the hills just north of Agamand Mills, the Agamand Family Crypt is the ancient resting ground of...",sec={{t="Restless Ancestors",b="Before the Third War, the Agamand family held expansive estates across northern Tirisfal Glades, entombing their forebears within this hillside mausoleum. When the Plague brought ruin to the kingdom, the crypt fell into the clutches of Captain Dargol, an agent of the Scourge. Rather than letting the wealthy lineage rest in peace, Dargol employed dark necromancy to awaken the entombed skeletons and vengeful apparitions, transforming a sacred burial ground into an aggressive Scourge foothold right on the edge of Forsaken territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Agamand Family Crypt located?",a="The crypt is carved into the hillside just north of Agamand Mills in the northern reaches of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"agamand crypt location","where is the crypt","how to find agamand crypt"}},{q="Who controls the crypt right now?",a="The tomb is held by Captain Dargol, a servant of the Scourge who orchestrates the dark magic within and commands the raised dead.",al={"who is in agamand crypt","crypt boss","captain dargol"}},{q="What will I encounter inside the crypt?",a="The crypt is filled with awakened skeletons and restless spirits of the Agamand ancestors. Driven by dark magic, these vengeful undead assault anyone who steps into the tombs.",al={"crypt enemies","what is inside agamand crypt","agamand crypt mobs"}},{q="Are the undead inside the crypt allied with the Forsaken?",a="No. The creatures inside are thralls of the Scourge answering to Captain Dargol, making them hostile to the Forsaken and living travelers alike.",al={"are they forsaken","agamand crypt friendly","why attack undead"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Captain Dargol's occupation of the crypt is an intolerable Scourge presence in Tirisfal, mocking the dead and threatening the Undercity's northern frontier."},kw={"agamand family crypt","agamand mills","captain dargol","crypt","mausoleum","scourge","skeletons","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:agamand-mills","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Agamand Family Crypt"}}
E["subzone:agamand-mills"] = {t="subzone",n="Agamand Mills",z="tirisfal",s="Agamand Mills is a sprawling farm and windmill complex nestled in the northern heights of Tirisfal Glades. Once the proud estate of the wealthy Agamand dynasty, it has fallen into ruin and stands as the largest Scourge stronghold in the region.",h="Agamand Mills is a sprawling farm and windmill complex nestled in the northern heights of Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A House Divided",b="Centuries ago, wealthy noble immigrants from Strom established the Agamand estate, building a vast milling network across northern Tirisfal. When the Third War broke out and the Scourge swept across Lordaeron, the patriarch Gregor Agamand refused to flee, fortifying the compound and convincing his retainers and laborers to make their stand. Their provisions and stone walls might have held, but their youngest son, Devlin Agamand, betrayed his blood. Devlin slaughtered the estate watchmen and let the walking dead into the sleeping quarters. Crippled from within, the remaining defenders were wiped out, and the family joined the mindless ranks of the undead.",sp=0},{t="A Bastion of Rot",b="Today, the Agamand Mills are the most entrenched bastion of the Scourge in Tirisfal Glades, posing an immediate threat to the Forsaken realm. The rotting windmills now churn above infested fields of wights, zombies, and skeletal horrors. Beneath the estate, Captain Dargol commands the garrison from the deep Agamand Family Crypt, practicing necromancy to reanimate generations of Agamand ancestors. From Brill, Magistrate Sevren and the Deathguards wage an active campaign to clear the mills and purge the Scourge presence before it can march upon the Undercity.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Agamand Mills overrun with Scourge?",a="When the Scourge ravaged Lordaeron, the Agamand family fortified their estate and attempted to hold out against the undead horde. However, the youngest son, Devlin Agamand, betrayed his family and opened the gates to the Scourge, leading to the slaughter and reanimation of everyone within.",al={"what happened to agamand mills","why are there undead at the mills","agamand mills lore"}},{q="Who controls the mills right now?",a="The estate serves as a regional forward outpost for the Scourge, led by Captain Dargol. Dargol operates deep within the fortified Agamand Family Crypt, where he uses dark magic to raise ancestral corpses into new soldiers.",al={"who leads agamand mills","scourge leader tirisfal","who is in charge at the mills"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken care about this place?",a="The mills represent the largest concentration of mindless Scourge forces remaining in Tirisfal Glades. If left unchecked, Captain Dargol's force threatens Brill and could choke off roads leading south to the Undercity.",al={"why brill attacks agamand","forsaken interest in agamand mills"}},{q="Who was the Agamand family?",a="They were an ancient, wealthy human noble house descended from Stromgarde immigrants who purchased rich farmlands in Tirisfal over a millennium ago. Today, its reanimated scions—including Gregor, Nissa, Thurman, and Devlin—wander the grounds as mindless thralls.",al={"who are the agamands","agamand lineage","gregor agamand"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming Agamand Mills is not merely tactical—it is personal vengeance against the Scourge and a settling of scores by former estate servants like Coleman Farthing."},kw={"agamand","agamand family crypt","agamand mills","captain dargol","devlin agamand","gregor agamand","scourge","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:agamand-family-crypt","quest:426","quest:408","quest:354","subzone:brill","npc:magistrate-sevren","npc:coleman-farthing","topic:scourge"},src={"Agamand Mills"}}
E["subzone:balnir-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Balnir Farmstead",z="tirisfal",s="The Balnir Farmstead is a derelict estate in eastern Tirisfal Glades, northeast of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Once renowned for raising the famed white horses favored by Lordaeron's royal family, the lands now lie ruined and infested by wandering Scourge. Today, the estate stands as a somber monument to Prince Arthas Menethil's early life and the site where he claimed his undead steed.",h="The Balnir Farmstead is a derelict estate in eastern Tirisfal Glades, northeast of the Ruins of Lordaeron.",sec={{t="A Legacy of Royal Steeds",b="For generations, the Balnir family bred the legendary white stallions of Lordaeron from their homestead in the rolling hills of Tirisfal. As a boy, Prince Arthas Menethil frequently visited the farm to escape royal court life, befriending the young Jarim Balnir. It was here that Arthas assisted in the foaling of the colt he named Invincible. Years later, after a tragic riding accident claimed the steed's life, Invincible was laid to rest in the soil of the farmstead upon Arthas's personal request.",sp=0},{t="Desolation and Scourge Infiltration",b="When Prince Arthas returned from Northrend and sacked Capital City, the Scourge wiped out the Balnir family without mercy. Newly fallen as a death knight, Arthas marched to the farmstead to exhume and resurrect Invincible with Frostmourne, leaving behind an open, ransacked grave. In the wake of the Third War, the ruins serve as a foothold for mindless Scourge slipping past the Bulwark. Forsaken deathguards watch the farm warily, while Undercity magi harvest surviving snapdragons from the garden to test how deeply plague corruption has crept into the soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Balnir Farmstead significant to Prince Arthas?",a="Arthas spent much of his youth sneaking away to the farmstead to play with the breeder's son. He was present for the birth of his beloved horse, Invincible, and later buried the beast here after a fatal fall. Following his descent into darkness, Arthas returned to exhume and raise Invincible into undeath.",al={"arthas farm","invincible birthplace","balnir arthas connection"}},{q="Who lived at the farmstead before the plague?",a="The farm was managed by Jorum Balnir, his wife Vara, and their son Jarim. They were master horse breeders who raised prized white horses for Lordaeron's nobility. The entire family was slaughtered when Arthas's Scourge swept through Tirisfal during the Third War.",al={"who owned balnir farm","balnir family","jorum balnir"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken monitoring the farm now?",a="Mindless Scourge often slip past the Bulwark from the Plaguelands and gather at the farmstead, threatening the eastern approaches to Tirisfal. Additionally, Undercity scholars study the resilient snapdragons still growing in the gardens to measure the spread of plague contamination.",al={"why forsaken care about balnir","rear guard patrol lore","balnir snapdragons"}},{q="What is the open grave on the property?",a="The disturbed plot marks the burial place of Invincible, Prince Arthas's childhood mount. After murdering his father, the fallen prince unearthed the horse and reanimated it as his monstrous skeletal charger, leaving the grave uncovered.",al={"balnir open grave","empty grave tirisfal","invincible grave"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the farmstead is a bitter reminder of the prince who doomed Lordaeron, as well as a nagging security breach where Scourge from the Plaguelands slip behind the Bulwark.",["class:Mage"]="Forsaken magi are dispatched to these blighted grounds to gather surviving Balnir snapdragons, studying them to detect the lingering magical taint of the Scourge."},kw={"arthas","balnir","farmstead","horses","invincible","jorum","snapdragon","tirisfal"},rel={"topic:arthas-menethil","zone:tirisfal","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","quest:1882","quest:356","subzone:bulwark","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},src={"Balnir Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:bandarion-keep"] = {t="subzone",n="Bandarion Keep",z="tirisfal",s="Bandarion Keep is a fortified redoubt associated with Tyr's Watch, nestled in the western reaches of Tirisfal Glades near the Whispering Forest. Named in honor of Garek Bandarion, the outpost serves as an isolated bulwark amidst lingering threats across the woodland frontier. Its defenders contend with everything from hostile coastal murlocs to roving zealots and unstable undead.",h="Bandarion Keep is a fortified redoubt associated with Tyr's Watch, nestled in the western reaches of Tirisfal...",sec={{t="A Bastion on the Western Border",b="Situated near the secluded Whispering Forest in western Tirisfal Glades, Bandarion Keep stands as a solitary sentinel for the Forsaken. Named after Garek Bandarion, this stronghold is closely tied to Tyr's Watch. Quartermasters like Jorin Croge work diligently to keep the garrison supplied despite its remote and challenging position far from the bustling courtyards of the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Surrounded by Threats",b="Holding the keep is no quiet assignment. The outpost faces constant danger from Vile Fin murloc raids along nearby waters, probing skirmishes by the Scarlet Crusade, and stray, mindless Scourge thralls shambling through the gloom. Worse still are internal perils: certain paladins struggling to adjust to their unlife as Forsaken have succumbed to madness, turning their weapons against their own kindred.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bandarion Keep located?",a="Bandarion Keep lies in the far western wilderness of Tirisfal Glades, positioned near the enigmatic Whispering Forest.",al={"bandarion keep location","where is bandarion keep","how to find bandarion keep"}},{q="Who was Bandarion Keep named after?",a="The stronghold is named in honor of Garek Bandarion, a notable figure associated with the order stationed there.",al={"who is bandarion","garek bandarion","bandarion keep name origin"}},{q="What is Tyr's Watch?",a="Tyr's Watch refers to the order of Forsaken paladins and guardians operating in the region, an organization deeply entwined with the foundation and defense of Bandarion Keep.",al={"tyrs watch","what is tyrs watch"}},{q="What dangers threaten the keep?",a="The keep's defenders regularly fend off Vile Fin murlocs, skirmish with Scarlet Crusade zealots, dispatch wandering mindless Scourge, and put down unstable Forsaken paladins who lose their minds and attack their own allies.",al={"who attacks bandarion keep","threats to bandarion keep","bandarion enemies"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For holy warriors facing the cold reality of undeath, Bandarion Keep represents both a refuge and a warning: some paladins who cannot reconcile the Light with their unlife have broken and turned their weapons against their Forsaken peers.",["race:Undead"]="Standing far on Tirisfal's western rim, this keep proves that the Forsaken must stay vigilant not only against the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade, but also against inner turmoil within their own ranks."},kw={"bandarion","bandarion keep","garek bandarion","jorin croge","tirisfal","tyr's watch","whispering forest"},rel={"subzone:whispering-forest","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge","topic:murloc","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Bandarion Keep"}}
E["subzone:brightwater-lake"] = {t="subzone",n="Brightwater Lake",z="tirisfal",s="Brightwater Lake is the largest body of water in Tirisfal Glades, stretching across the mist-shrouded lowlands northeast of Brill. Once a tranquil retreat for the kingdom of Lordaeron, its waters now lie cold and dark, surrounding a central isle where an outcast necromancer conducts his forbidden research.",h="Brightwater Lake is the largest body of water in Tirisfal Glades, stretching across the mist-shrouded...",sec={{t="Waters of the North",b="Spanning the northern plains between the town of Brill and the Scarlet Watch Post, Brightwater Lake is a quiet and eerie landmark in the heart of Tirisfal. Thousands of years ago, its misty banks bore witness to ancient conflicts, including early clashes against the dreadlord Kathra'natir. In the peaceful centuries that followed under the Kingdom of Lordaeron, the lake served as a scenic country haven. Today, like the rest of the glades, its pristine character is long gone. The Plaguelands lie not far to the east, and the murky, chilled waters reflect only grey skies, withered trees, and the constant threat of roving murlocs and hostile undead.",sp=0},{t="The Hermit's Refuge",b="Rising from the center of Brightwater Lake is an island known as Gunther's Retreat. Here dwells Gunther Arcanus, a powerful necromancer who broke free of the Lich King's grasp by his own formidable willpower. Suspicious of the Dark Lady and the newly established Forsaken in the Undercity, Gunther chose seclusion over servitude, raising his own skeletal defenders to guard the island perimeter. His stubborn independence draws keen interest from Forsaken magistrates, who are eager to either recruit his formidable talents or ensure his autonomous existence poses no threat to Sylvanas's realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Brightwater Lake located?",a="Brightwater Lake sits in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, just northeast of the Forsaken hub of Brill. It lies directly south of the jagged North Coast and west of the Scarlet Watch Post that guards the mountain passes toward the Western Plaguelands.",al={"brightwater lake location","where is brightwater lake","find brightwater lake"}},{q="Who lives on the island in the middle of the lake?",a="The island, known as Gunther's Retreat, is inhabited by Gunther Arcanus. He is a rogue necromancer who managed to shatter the Lich King's mental enslavement entirely on his own. Rather than joining the Forsaken in the Undercity, he remains secluded in his camp with his personal skeletal minions.",al={"who is on the island","gunther arcanus","brightwater island npc"}},{q="What threats are found around the waters?",a="Travelers along the shorelines frequently encounter aggressive vile fins and murlocs scavenging the banks. Approaching the central island brings danger from the reanimated skeletons and servants sworn to protect Gunther Arcanus from intruders.",al={"lake monsters","brightwater enemies","dangers at brightwater lake"}},{q="Why do the guards in Brill talk about a summer camp here?",a="Town deathguards in Brill dryly joke that the Forsaken attempted to run a children's summer camp along the shores of Brightwater Lake, but were forced to shut it down due to masked psychos terrorizing the grounds—a morbid local quip mirroring human campfire tales.",al={"summer camp rumor","brill guards lake joke","masked psycho camp"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, securing Brightwater Lake is vital for defending Brill's eastern approaches and assessing whether the autonomous necromancer Gunther Arcanus will become an asset or an enemy.",["class:Mage"]="The lake holds lingering arcana from ancient battles fought in Tirisfal, as well as the unique, unguided mastery displayed by the renegade wizard Gunther Arcanus."},kw={"brightwater lake","brill","gunther arcanus","gunther's retreat","necromancer","scarlet watch post","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"subzone:gunther-s-retreat","zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","subzone:scarlet-watch-post","subzone:north-coast","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron","subzone:crystal-lake"},src={"Brightwater Lake"}}
E["subzone:brill"] = {t="subzone",n="Brill",z="tirisfal",s="Brill is the primary Forsaken settlement in the heart of Tirisfal Glades, situated just north of the Ruins of Lordaeron. Once a prosperous human town, it now serves as the administrative and military hub for newly awakened undead stepping beyond the confines of Deathknell.",h="Brill is the primary Forsaken settlement in the heart of Tirisfal Glades, situated just north of the Ruins of...",sec={{t="From Plague Ground to Bastion",b="Before the Third War, Brill was a lively village under the sway of regional nobles such as the Barov and Agamand families. That prosperity ended when Kel'Thuzad chose the area for the Cult of the Damned's earliest experiments with the Plague of Undeath. The devastating blight swept through the population so quickly that local militia were driven out, leaving a sprawling mass graveyard in its wake.\n\nNow rebuilt by the Forsaken under the leadership of Magistrate Sevren, the town retains its weathered Lordaeron architecture beneath an atmosphere of grim purpose. Brill functions as the regional command center, coordinating defenses against Scarlet Crusade incursions, roaming Scourge remnants, and native beasts warped by necromantic decay.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of Northern Lordaeron",b="Beyond local defense, Brill is an essential crossroads linking Tirisfal Glades to the wider Horde. Overhead, the goblin-operated zeppelin tower provides transit south toward Durotar and deep into Stranglethorn Vale. Within the settlement, Gallows' End Tavern serves not only as a dark shelter for travelers, but also as a makeshift laboratory where captured Scarlet zealots are interrogated and subjected to apothecarial testing.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who rules Brill?",a="Magistrate Sevren oversees the civil administration and local defenses of Brill on behalf of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken.",al={"brill leader","who is in charge of brill","magistrate of brill"}},{q="Why is there such a massive graveyard outside Brill?",a="Kel'Thuzad conducted some of his very first live experiments with the Plague of Undeath in Brill. The contagion wiped out the local human population with horrifying speed, necessitating a mass graveyard to inter the victims before they rose as Scourge.",al={"brill graveyard","cemetery near brill","why so many graves"}},{q="What is Gallows' End Tavern used for?",a="Aside from lodging weary travelers, the tavern's cellar serves as a base for apothecaries conducting chemical and toxicological experiments on captured Scarlet Crusade zealots.",al={"gallows end","brill inn","what is happening in the brill tavern"}},{q="Where does the zeppelin tower outside Brill travel to?",a="The zeppelin tower operated by goblin crews connects Lordaeron directly to Kalimdor outside Orgrimmar, as well as south to Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"brill zeppelin destinations","where do blimps go brill","brill flight paths"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken venturing out from Deathknell, Brill is the first glimpse of civilization and the starting ground for proving loyalty to the Dark Lady.",["faction:Horde"]="The zeppelin dock outside town serves as the northern Horde's primary link between Lordaeron and allied strongholds in Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"brill","forsaken","gallows end","lordaeron","magistrate sevren","tirisfal glades","zeppelin"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill-town-hall","subzone:gallows-end-tavern","npc:magistrate-sevren","subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:grom-gol-base-camp"},src={"Brill"}}
E["subzone:brill-town-hall"] = {t="subzone",n="Brill Town Hall",z="tirisfal",s="Brill Town Hall is the administrative heart of the settlement of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades. Standing as the most prominent structure in town, it serves as the civic headquarters from which the Forsaken govern their local holdings and coordinate the defense of the glades.",h="Brill Town Hall is the administrative heart of the settlement of Brill in central Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Civic Seat of the Forsaken",b="While much of Lordaeron lies shattered and ruined, Brill Town Hall remains standing as a functioning civic center under undead rule. Inside, Magistrate Sevren directs town affairs from his podium, handing out vital commissions and directives to Forsaken adventurers. Aside from the Defiler's Den in the Arathi Highlands, it is one of the only recognized town halls in the known world actively run by the Forsaken, serving as a bleak parody and functional continuation of old Lordaeron's municipal bureaucracy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Brill Town Hall used for?",a="It serves as the local seat of government for the settlement of Brill. Forsaken leadership, particularly Magistrate Sevren, uses the building to coordinate local defense, issue decrees, and assign critical tasks to travelers and newly awakened undead.",al={"brill town hall purpose","what is this building","why visit brill town hall"}},{q="Who is in charge here?",a="Magistrate Sevren presides over the town hall from his podium, managing municipal affairs on behalf of the Forsaken and directing operations throughout central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who runs brill town hall","brill town hall leader","who is the magistrate"}},{q="Why is this town hall notable compared to others?",a="Town halls are typically relics of living human kingdoms. Brill Town Hall is notable for being one of the only active civic halls maintained and operated by the Forsaken, mirroring only places like the Defiler's Den in Arathi.",al={"unique forsaken town hall","are there other forsaken town halls"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken venturing out from Deathknell, the town hall represents the first taste of structured civic governance under Queen Sylvanas's realm, where local defense and reclamation efforts are formally organized.",["faction:Horde"]="Allies of the Horde arriving in Tirisfal can visit the town hall to understand how the Forsaken maintain civil authority and martial order in their darkened homelands."},kw={"brill","forsaken","lordaeron","magistrate sevren","sevren","tirisfal glades","town hall"},rel={"subzone:brill","npc:magistrate-sevren","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},src={"Brill Town Hall"}}
E["subzone:calston-estate"] = {t="subzone",n="Calston Estate",z="tirisfal",s="Calston Estate is a Forsaken encampment situated west of Stillwater Pond in Tirisfal Glades. Under the eye of Sedrick Calston, the estate serves as an operational base for securing northern Tirisfal against nearby human holdouts and gathering research materials along the coastline.",h="Calston Estate is a Forsaken encampment situated west of Stillwater Pond in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Northern Outpost",b="Positioned between Stillwater Pond and the contested farms of northern Tirisfal, Calston Estate acts as a staging ground for the Forsaken war effort. The estate's namesake, Sedrick Calston, maintains residency here alongside representatives of the Royal Apothecary Society and various military trainers. From this quiet cluster of darkened buildings, the Forsaken monitor human remnants at Solliden Farmstead and coordinate expeditions toward the blighted northern coast, providing field agents a local refuge without the need to retreat all the way south to Brill.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who owns Calston Estate?",a="The estate belongs to Sedrick Calston, a lonely Forsaken who remains on the grounds while opening his property to the Forsaken military and the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"who owns calston estate","who is sedrick calston","sedrick calston"}},{q="What is the strategic purpose of this estate?",a="It serves as an advance camp in northern Tirisfal Glades. From here, the Forsaken launch incursions against the living humans defending the Solliden Farmstead and conduct alchemical gathering expeditions along the northern shore.",al={"why is calston estate important","purpose of calston estate","what do forsaken do here"}},{q="Where is Calston Estate located?",a="It is located in the northern reaches of Tirisfal Glades, just west of Stillwater Pond and east of the Solliden Farmstead.",al={"where is calston estate","calston estate location","how to find calston estate"}},{q="Why are apothecaries stationed here?",a="Agents of the Royal Apothecary Society use the estate as a forward outpost to conduct research and gather reagents from the nearby coastline and blighted waterways without traveling back to the Undercity.",al={"royal apothecary society calston","apothecaries at calston estate"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The estate stands as another converted piece of Lordaeron property turned toward the defense and expansion of the Forsaken realm.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde champions operating far from Brill or the Undercity, the estate provides vital logistical support, trainers, and supplies on the northern front."},kw={"apothecary","calston","estate","sedrick","solliden","stillwater","tirisfal"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:stillwater-pond","subzone:solliden-farmstead","subzone:brill","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:forsaken","topic:horde"},src={"Calston Estate"}}
E["subzone:cold-hearth-manor"] = {t="subzone",n="Cold Hearth Manor",z="tirisfal",s="Cold Hearth Manor is a blighted farmstead located just east of Brill along the main road of Tirisfal Glades. Once a bustling, hospitable estate known for bountiful crops, the outbreak of the Plague of Undeath wiped out its residents, leaving the surrounding fields choked with mindless Scourge. Today, the Forsaken have secured the main farmhouse as an outpost and waystation for travelers.",h="Cold Hearth Manor is a blighted farmstead located just east of Brill along the main road of Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Chilled Hearth",b="Before the Third War, this homestead bore a reputation for warmth and hospitality, supporting rich harvests in the heart of Lordaeron. When the Plague swept through the kingdom, the entire family and their laborers succumbed, rising again as husks bound to the Scourge. While feral undead still stumble through the ruined fields, Forsaken forces managed to push the mindless dead out of the main farmhouse, reclaiming the structure to serve as a trading post and foothold along the road toward the eastern glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the people who lived here?",a="The farmers and workers who tended the estate were completely wiped out when the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron. Rather than finding peace in death, they were raised as mindless zombies that still haunt the surrounding fields.",al={"who lived at cold hearth","manor backstory","what happened to the family"}},{q="Why is it called Cold Hearth Manor?",a="The estate originally had a reputation for its warm atmosphere and welcoming fires. The grim moniker was likely adopted by the Forsaken as an ironic nod to its former life, marking how cold, dead, and blighted the farm has become.",al={"cold hearth name meaning","why cold hearth"}},{q="Who controls the manor right now?",a="The Forsaken have taken control of the primary farmhouse, using it as a safe stop for travelers and traders along the road from Brill. However, the open fields and barns surrounding the manor remain infested with hostile Scourge.",al={"who owns cold hearth manor","is cold hearth friendly"}},{q="Why don't the Forsaken clear out the fields?",a="The Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades are stretched thin, fighting off mindless Scourge remnants while warding off Scarlet Crusade crusaders. Securing the farmhouse and main road provides immediate utility, leaving the scattered dead in the fields as a nuisance rather than an immediate threat to Brill.",al={"why are there zombies in the fields","why scourge here"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, reclaiming places like Cold Hearth Manor is a bitter reminder of their lost mortal lives, converting former human sanctuaries into grim defensive outposts against both the Scourge and the Scarlet Crusade.",["faction:Horde"]="The manor offers a secure vantage along the road between Brill and the eastern reaches of Tirisfal, providing a safe waypoint for travelers navigating the plagued countryside."},kw={"brill","cold hearth manor","farmstead","forsaken","scourge","tirisfal glades","zombies"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath"},src={"Cold Hearth Manor"}}
E["subzone:crusader-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Crusader Outpost",z="tirisfal",s="Crusader Outpost is a fortified watchtower perched atop the rugged hills of eastern Tirisfal Glades. Manned by zealous members of the Scarlet Crusade, it guards the approaches leading toward their stronghold at the Scarlet Monastery. From this height, Crusaders observe travel along the road and stand ready to repel any Forsaken incursion.",h="Crusader Outpost is a fortified watchtower perched atop the rugged hills of eastern Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Eyes Over Tirisfal",b="Built into the bluffs overlooking the eastern road, the Crusader Outpost serves as a primary early-warning station for the Scarlet Crusade. From their elevated tower, sentries watch over movement between Brill and the eastern reaches of Lordaeron, ensuring that wandering undead or scouting parties are spotted long before reaching the Monastery gates. The tower also grants the garrison tactical flanking capability against any force seeking to march up the valley toward their holy bastion.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn in the Dark Lady's Side",b="Under the command of Scarlet officers like Captain Vachon, the garrison stationed here maintains unwavering vigilance. They see the surrounding woods not as sovereign territory of the Forsaken, but as unhallowed soil stolen from humanity by monstrosities. For travelers loyal to the Undercity, the outpost represents an ever-present ambush point where crossbow bolts and cleansing steel await anyone straying too close to the bluffs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crusader Outpost?",a="It is a fortified scouting tower held by the Scarlet Crusade in eastern Tirisfal Glades. It monitors the road passing below and protects the southern approach to the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"what is this tower","crusader outpost tirisfal","scarlet watchtower"}},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="The outpost is manned by zealots of the Scarlet Crusade under the command of Captain Vachon. They view all undead as abominations to be eradicated on sight.",al={"who owns crusader outpost","who lives here","scarlet crusade outpost"}},{q="Why is the tower situated in these hills?",a="Its elevated position offers clear sightlines over the main eastern thoroughfare of Tirisfal Glades. This allows Crusaders to detect Forsaken troop movements early and flank any forces attempting an assault on the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"why build here","outpost location","tactical purpose"}},{q="Will the guards here attack me?",a="Yes. The Scarlet Crusade considers all outsiders—particularly the Forsaken and their Horde allies—corrupt enemies who must be purged in holy fire.",al={"is crusader outpost hostile","are they aggressive"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This watchtower sits right on the edge of Forsaken territory, serving as a bitter reminder that zealous living crusaders still hold sovereign pockets within the glades.",["faction:Horde"]="Navigating the eastern trails of Tirisfal requires caution, as Scarlet sentries atop this hill will swiftly attack anyone traveling toward the Monastery."},kw={"captain vachon","crusader outpost","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scout tower","tirisfal glades","watchtower"},rel={"topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Crusader Outpost"}}
E["subzone:crusader-s-outpost"] = {t="subzone",n="Crusader's Outpost",z="tirisfal",s="Crusader's Outpost is a fortified scout tower manned by the Scarlet Crusade in western Tirisfal Glades, standing along the Scarlet Palisade. Situated adjacent to the Solliden Farmstead, it serves as the Crusade's westernmost position in all of Lordaeron. Its perilous distance from the main Scarlet bastions leaves its garrison isolated in the heart of hostile Forsaken territory.",h="Crusader's Outpost is a fortified scout tower manned by the Scarlet Crusade in western Tirisfal Glades...",sec={{t="A Lonely Watchtower",b="Perched inside the Scarlet Palisade just west of Deathknell, this stone tower represents the farthest reach of the Scarlet Crusade's power in Lordaeron. The garrison stationed here works in tandem with the surviving human laborers of the nearby Solliden Farmstead, attempting to hold back the encroaching undead. From the top of the tower, lookouts keep watch over the surrounding pumpkin fields and forest paths, vigilant against both roaming Scourge fiends and patrols from the Undercity.",sp=0},{t="Isolated Behind Enemy Lines",b="Holding the western frontier carries extreme risk. Cut off from their primary strongholds in the Scarlet Monastery and far to the east in Tyr's Hand, the crusaders at this outpost cannot expect swift reinforcements should an attack breach the palisade. Any siege by the Forsaken forces massing across Tirisfal means either holding the tower on their own or facing total annihilation before help can ever arrive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade all the way out here in western Tirisfal?",a="The tower serves as an early warning post and defensive fortification along the Scarlet Palisade. It protects the living human farmers at Solliden Farmstead and watches the western approaches against both feral Scourge and Forsaken advance scouts.",al={"why are scarlet here","scarlet crusaders tirisfal west","crusader outpost purpose"}},{q="Can reinforcements reach this outpost if it gets attacked?",a="Not easily. The outpost is the westernmost Scarlet holding in Lordaeron. Their primary bastions lie far to the east at the Scarlet Monastery and Tyr's Hand, leaving this garrison entirely cut off if Forsaken forces surround them.",al={"can scarlet reinforce","outpost help","how far is help"}},{q="What is the relationship between the tower and Solliden Farmstead?",a="The crusaders have allied with the remaining human farmers at Solliden Farmstead. The soldiers provide protection against the walking dead in exchange for sustenance and a loyal staging ground on the fringes of Lordaeron.",al={"solliden connection","why are crusaders at farm","crusaders and farmers"}},{q="Are there other towers like this in the region?",a="Yes. This tower is one of four similar Crusader's Outposts established by the Scarlet Crusade across Tirisfal Glades to survey and patrol the surrounding lands.",al={"other crusader outposts","more scarlet towers"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the newly risen Forsaken emerging from Deathknell, this nearby tower and the Scarlet zealots guarding it represent an immediate existential threat right on their border.",["faction:Horde"]="The outpost serves as a bitter reminder of the Scarlet Crusade's fanatical refusal to yield Tirisfal to the Forsaken and their Horde allies."},kw={"crusader's outpost","scarlet crusade","scarlet palisade","scout tower","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades","tyr's hand"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-palisade","subzone:solliden-farmstead","zone:tirisfal","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken","subzone:tyr-s-hand","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge"},src={"Crusader's Outpost"}}
E["subzone:darkwalk"] = {t="subzone",n="Darkwalk",z="tirisfal",s="The Darkwalk is a subterranean passage deep within the subterranean reaches of Tirisfal Glades, hidden beneath the surface of the Tomb of Tyr. It forms a ruined conduit connecting the resting vault of Keeper Tyr to the ancient prison holding the remains of the C'Thraxxi horror Zakajz the Corruptor.",h="The Darkwalk is a subterranean passage deep within the subterranean reaches of Tirisfal Glades, hidden...",sec={{t="A Buried Threshold",b="Carved into the deep stone far beneath Tirisfal, the Darkwalk is an underground, partially collapsed hall constructed in the mythic past following the cataclysmic battle between Keeper Tyr and the monstrous servant of the Old Gods, Zakajz the Corruptor. Designed to bridge the vault holding Tyr's remains with the deep containment chamber of his fallen foe, the passage is a silent monument to Titan craft now shrouded in earth, dust, and lingering corruption.",sp=0},{t="Shadows of the Deep",b="Though long forgotten by the surface-dwelling Forsaken and the remnants of Lordaeron, the Darkwalk remains suffused with malevolent echoes. Deep within this subterranean labyrinth, ancient Titan architecture sits cracked and worn by time. The proximity to the slumbering evil interred at its terminus means that any passage through these shattered stone galleries remains heavy with an oppressive, unseen dread.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Darkwalk located?",a="The Darkwalk lies buried deep under Tirisfal Glades within the subterranean complex of the Tomb of Tyr. It serves as an intermediary passage connecting Tyr's vault to the lower prison chamber.",al={"darkwalk location","where is darkwalk","how to find darkwalk"}},{q="What connects to the Darkwalk?",a="The passage connects the main chamber of the Tomb of Tyr to the Grave-Prison of Zakajz, bridging the resting place of the Titan keeper and the prison of the defeated monstrosity.",al={"what is in darkwalk","where does darkwalk go"}},{q="Why is the passage collapsed?",a="Millennia of subterranean shifting and the immense violence of the prehistoric battle that shattered the surrounding earth left portions of the Titan-built tunnel collapsed and decayed.",al={"why is darkwalk broken","is darkwalk ruined"}},{q="Do the people of Lordaeron or the Forsaken know about it?",a="No. The subterranean vaults beneath Tirisfal are largely forgotten legends to the surface inhabitants, known only through ancient fragmented myths regarding Tyr's sacrifice.",al={"do forsaken know about darkwalk","is darkwalk common knowledge"}}},ang={["class:Priest"]="The dark echoes lingering through this deep stone corridor serve as a stark reminder of the ancient Void forces that warred against the Titan keepers long before humanity walked Lordaeron."},kw={"darkwalk","passage","tirisfal glades","titan","tomb of tyr","zakajz"},rel={"subzone:tomb-of-tyr","subzone:grave-prison-of-zakajz","zone:tirisfal","topic:titan","topic:old-god"},src={"Darkwalk"}}
E["subzone:death-s-watch-waystation"] = {t="subzone",n="Death's Watch Waystation",z="tirisfal",s="Death's Watch Waystation is a small military outpost positioned southeast of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Staffed by the Forsaken Deathguard, the camp secures the local roadways against Scourge stragglers, beasts, and hostile Scarlet intruders.",h="Death's Watch Waystation is a small military outpost positioned southeast of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Bulwark on the Road",b="Situated just down the road from the town of Brill, Death's Watch Waystation serves as an essential picket post for the Forsaken military. The surrounding glades remain fraught with peril, from feral wildlife warped by plague to prowling remnants of the mindless Scourge. By maintaining a fortified presence at this junction, the Deathguard monitors traffic moving through central Tirisfal, ensuring travelers and couriers can traverse the roads between local strongholds without falling prey to ambushes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Death's Watch Waystation?",a="It serves as a fortified forward post for the Deathguard, protecting the roads southeast of Brill from hostile creatures, Scourge holdouts, and infiltrating enemies.",al={"why is deaths watch waystation here","what is deaths watch","waystation purpose"}},{q="Who maintains the camp?",a="The post is operated by the Deathguard, the standing military and policing force of the Forsaken in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who controls deaths watch","guards at deaths watch","who runs the waystation"}},{q="Where is the waystation located?",a="It lies directly southeast of Brill along the dirt thoroughfare that runs through central Tirisfal Glades.",al={"deaths watch location","how to find deaths watch waystation","where is it"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Waystations like this are vital lifelines across Tirisfal, demonstrating the Deathguard's tireless vigilance in carving out a secure homeland from the ruins of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers from Kalimdor navigating the gloomy woods of Tirisfal, Deathguard encampments like Death's Watch provide reassurance and clear signposts in an unfamiliar land."},kw={"brill","camp","death's watch waystation","deathguard","deaths watch","forsaken","outpost","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Death's Watch Waystation"}}
E["subzone:deathknell"] = {t="subzone",n="Deathknell",z="tirisfal",s="Deathknell is a fortified village nestled in a secluded valley in southwestern Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the primary awakening grounds for newly freed undead breaking free from the Lich King's grasp to join the Forsaken. Besieged by mindless Scourge remnants, local zealots, and aggressive wildlife, the settlement is a harsh proving ground for those claiming a place in Sylvanas Windrunner's kingdom.",h="Deathknell is a fortified village nestled in a secluded valley in southwestern Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Cradle of the Forsaken",b="Tucked away behind jagged hills just north of the Silverpine border, Deathknell is where newly awakened undead first open their eyes to their bleak reality. Unlike most settlements in Tirisfal Glades that preserved their human names from the fallen Kingdom of Lordaeron, Deathknell was explicitly renamed by the undead who claimed it. The town itself is cleaved in two: the Forsaken cling stubbornly to the southern grounds around the old church, while the northern half—including the village forge—remains overrun by mindless Scourge zombies and feral ghouls. Elite Deathguards keep the narrow gorge out of the valley securely sealed against intruders, allowing local caretakers to induct new arrivals into the Banshee Queen's service.",sp=0},{t="A Valley Under Siege",b="Survival in Deathknell is precarious. To the northwest, Night Web's Hollow—a gold mine vital for the Forsaken's fledgling economy—has been lost to monstrous spiders. To the southeast, an aggressive encampment of the Scarlet Crusade maintains constant watch, trading couriers with their strongholds to the east and probing the valley's defenses. Meanwhile, the village caretakers must continually fight off the mindless undead wandering the northern ruins while gathering scrap metal, tools, and supplies to equip newly arisen souls for the long road ahead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was the town renamed Deathknell?",a="While most settlements throughout Tirisfal Glades retained their human Lordaeron names, Deathknell is a notable exception. The Forsaken chose the moniker intentionally upon taking root in the valley, marking the site as both the death of their old human existence and the grim bell sounding their rebirth into undeath.",al={"deathknell name origin","why is it called deathknell","old name of deathknell"}},{q="Why is the northern half of the town overrun by undead?",a="Not every corpse raised in the wake of the Third War broke free with their minds intact. The northern village square and forge are infested by the 'Mindless Ones'—feral zombies, ghouls, and skeletons still driven by the residual, lingering will of the Scourge. Forsaken defenders regularly clear them out to salvage equipment and defend the church.",al={"why are zombies in deathknell","scourge in deathknell","mindless ones deathknell"}},{q="What is the Scarlet Crusade doing near Deathknell?",a="A detachment of the Scarlet Crusade maintains an encampment in the hills southeast of the village. Fanatically dedicated to destroying all undead indiscriminately, they monitor the pass, ambush newly awakened Forsaken, and exchange scouting intelligence with Scarlet strongholds elsewhere in Lordaeron.",al={"scarlet camp deathknell","crusaders outside deathknell","scarlet crusade tirisfal valley"}},{q="Why can't the Forsaken use the local gold mine?",a="Night Web's Hollow, the gold mine situated in the cliffs northwest of the village, is completely overrun by aggressive spiders. Securing natural resources like gold is critical for the Forsaken war effort, but until the infestation is cleared, the settlement cannot exploit the vein.",al={"deathknell mine","night webs hollow","spider mine tirisfal"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every Forsaken adventurer begins here, rising from the cold earth of the Shadow Grave to find purpose and shelter under Lady Sylvanas after the horror of the Plague.",["faction:Horde"]="Though isolated and dark, this valley is the gateway to the Forsaken kingdom, supplying fresh soldiers to bolster the Horde's foothold in the Eastern Kingdoms."},kw={"deathknell","forsaken starting area","mindless ones","night web's hollow","shadow grave","sylvanas","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:shadow-grave","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","subzone:night-web-s-hollow","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:silverpine","subzone:deathknell-graves"},src={"Deathknell"}}
E["subzone:deathknell-graves"] = {t="subzone",n="Deathknell Graves",z="tirisfal",s="The Deathknell Graves comprise the sprawling burial grounds situated around the Shadow Grave in Deathknell. Once a resting place for the deceased inhabitants of northern Lordaeron, this earth now serves as the grim threshold where newly awakened Forsaken pull themselves from the soil.",h="The Deathknell Graves comprise the sprawling burial grounds situated around the Shadow Grave in Deathknell.",sec={{t="A Restless Threshold",b="Spreading out around the stone crypt known as the Shadow Grave, the Deathknell Graves hold the remains of countless Lordaeron citizens who perished during the Third War. As the grasp of the Scourge slips and the Dark Lady's call echoes across Tirisfal Glades, these burial plots have become a scene of grim rebirth rather than eternal rest. Newly self-aware undead claw their way through the damp earth, leaving behind empty pits, broken soil, and weather-worn grave markers as they emerge into free will.",sp=0},{t="Confusion and Madness",b="Not every soul that awakens beneath this sod handles the shock of resurrection with sanity intact. While many newly liberated Forsaken report directly to the caretakers and overseers in Deathknell, others are overcome by fury or despair, degenerating into mindless zombies that wander among the tombstones. Caretakers like Undertaker Mordo keep a watchful eye on the freshly turned plots, dispatching the deranged and guiding the coherent into service to the Dark Lady.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is buried in the Deathknell Graves?",a="These graves primarily hold the fallen citizens of Lordaeron who succumbed to the plague of undeath during the Third War. Originally interred as regular corpses, many have lingered in the earth until breaking free from the Lich King's control.",al={"who is buried here","who are these graves for","deathknell graves history"}},{q="Why are undead rising from these graves?",a="With the Lich King's mental grip fractured across the region, dormant corpses are awakening with their own free will. Those possessing enough mental clarity pull themselves out of the earth and join the ranks of the Forsaken under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"why are zombies rising","how do forsaken awaken","why wake up here"}},{q="Why do some corpses turn into mindless zombies?",a="The shock of resurrection and the lingering trauma of the plague prove too much for many souls. Lacking the mental resilience to claim their free will, they regress into mindless, violent husks that must be destroyed for the safety of the settlement.",al={"mindless zombies deathknell","why are some feral","insane undead"}},{q="Who watches over the graveyard?",a="Caretakers and undertakers, such as Undertaker Mordo, monitor the graves just outside the crypt. They provide initial guidance to coherent arrivals while ordering the extermination of those who succumb to mindless madness.",al={"who oversees the graves","deathknell undertaker"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every Forsaken adventurer remembers the damp earth of these graves, the first place where the fog of the Scourge cleared and true consciousness returned."},kw={"cemetery","deathknell","deathknell graves","forsaken starting area","graveyard","mordo","shadow grave","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:shadow-grave","subzone:deathknell","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Deathknell Graves"}}
E["subzone:faol-s-rest"] = {t="subzone",n="Faol's Rest",z="tirisfal",s="Faol's Rest is a quiet, neglected gravesite situated in eastern Tirisfal Glades, just southwest of the Scarlet Monastery. It was erected as the tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, the revered spiritual patriarch who founded the Knights of the Silver Hand. Today, untended beneath the blighted canopy, it serves as a release graveyard for those who perish near the monastery.",h="Faol's Rest is a quiet, neglected gravesite situated in eastern Tirisfal Glades, just southwest of the...",sec={{t="Tomb of the Archbishop",b="Before the Third War devastated Lordaeron, this secluded hollow was a place of solemn pilgrimage. It holds the stone tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, who led the Church of the Holy Light through the dark days of the Second War and instituted the order of paladins to protect humanity. Faol passed away peacefully prior to the arrival of the Scourge, spared the mortal agony of seeing his kingdom fall. In those brighter years, mourners regularly journeyed up the road from Capital City to leave offerings and pay respects to the beloved patriarch.",sp=0},{t="Desolation in the Shadow of the Monastery",b="When the Plague of Undeath swept across Lordaeron, Tirisfal withered, and the pilgrims vanished. Today, the monument sits abandoned and cracked in the shadows beneath the Scarlet Monastery's high bluffs. The wild brush has reclaimed the pathways, and the tomb itself lies still amid the damp mist. For adventurers striving against the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade or the lingering terrors of Tirisfal, this forgotten resting place now serves primarily as a quiet threshold where fallen spirits briefly regroup before returning to the fray.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Alonsus Faol?",a="Alonsus Faol was the Archbishop of the Church of the Holy Light during the Second War. Revered for his wisdom and compassion, he organized relief for refugees and founded the Knights of the Silver Hand, transforming holy priests and pious knights into humanity's first paladins, including Uther the Lightbringer and Turalyon.",al={"who is faol","alonsus faol lore","who is buried here"}},{q="Why is this monument located near the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The grounds near the Scarlet Monastery were historically significant religious holdings of the Church of the Holy Light in northern Lordaeron. Faol was laid to rest in this tranquil corner of Tirisfal Glades before the kingdom fell, long before the scarlet-clad zealots fortified the nearby monastery.",al={"why near monastery","scarlet monastery connection","location meaning"}},{q="Is anyone maintaining the tomb today?",a="No. Since the fall of Lordaeron to the Scourge, the site has been utterly neglected. The Scarlet Crusade rarely descends into the hollow to tend it, and the Forsaken have little interest in honoring the shrines of the old church, leaving the stone markers weathered and overgrown.",al={"who tends faol's rest","is it abandoned","tomb upkeep"}},{q="What practical purpose does Faol's Rest serve for travelers?",a="Faol's Rest functions as the local spirit graveyard for the surrounding wilderness and the Scarlet Monastery. Adventurers who perish attempting to breach the monastery or traversing eastern Tirisfal find their spirits returning to the Archbishop's quiet monument.",al={"graveyard run","what is this place in game","monastery graveyard"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Every paladin owes their calling to Archbishop Faol, who first gathered Uther and his peers to unite the martial arts with the Holy Light. Standing before his untended tomb is a sobering reminder of the order's beginnings.",["class:Priest"]="As the supreme leader of the Church of the Holy Light through the Second War, Faol was the shepherd of all priesthoods in Lordaeron; seeing his monument ruined reflects the church's tragic ruin in the north."},kw={"alonsus faol","church of the holy light","faol's rest","graveyard","scarlet monastery","silver hand","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","topic:lordaeron","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:scourge","topic:forsaken"},src={"Faol's Rest"}}
E["subzone:gallows-end-tavern"] = {t="subzone",n="Gallows' End Tavern",z="tirisfal",s="Gallows' End Tavern is the principal inn of Brill and the heart of Forsaken hospitality in Tirisfal Glades. Beyond offering shelter and spirits to weary travelers, it serves as an essential hub for class mentors, trade instructors, and covert interrogations.",h="Gallows' End Tavern is the principal inn of Brill and the heart of Forsaken hospitality in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Gathering Place for the Dead",b="Standing prominently along the road in Brill, Gallows' End Tavern serves as the primary gathering place for newly awakened Forsaken leaving Deathknell and journeying south toward the Undercity. Despite their undead condition, Forsaken still frequent its halls for fellowship, trade, and refuge. The inn houses various class instructors—guiding young warriors, priests, mages, rogues, and warlocks—as well as vendors and medical practitioners.",sp=0},{t="Secrets in the Cellar",b="Beneath the creaking floorboards and tavern laughter lies a far grimmer purpose. Down in the cellars, the Forsaken keep prisoners of war bound and guarded away from public view. Among them are a captured Scarlet Zealot and a Dwarven Mountaineer, held beneath the tavern for interrogation and experimentation as the Forsaken fight to secure their borders against both zealous crusaders and Alliance scouts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Gallows' End Tavern located?",a="It is located in the center of Brill, the main Forsaken settlement just north of the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"gallows end location","where is gallows end tavern","brill inn location"}},{q="Why do the undead need an inn or tavern?",a="While the Forsaken do not require sleep or mortal sustenance to survive, taverns like Gallows' End maintain social bonds and cultural habits from their past lives. It also acts as a secure civic center for training, commerce, and official business.",al={"why do undead drink","why do forsaken need taverns","undead inn lore"}},{q="Who is imprisoned in the basement?",a="In the cellars beneath the tavern, the Forsaken hold captive enemies including a Scarlet Zealot from the hostile Scarlet Crusade and an Alliance Dwarven Mountaineer.",al={"tavern prisoners","who is in the cellar","brill tavern dungeon"}},{q="What services and trainers can be found here?",a="The tavern features instructors for warriors, priests, mages, rogues, and warlocks, along with first aid and enchanting trainers, general trade vendors, and an innkeeper.",al={"gallows end trainers","who trains in brill inn","tavern vendors"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As the first major inn encountered outside Deathknell, Gallows' End Tavern serves as the cultural and functional crossroads for newly awakened Forsaken entering the wider world.",["faction:Alliance"]="Beneath the taproom floors, the Forsaken keep captured Alliance scouts and Scarlet Crusade zealots detained for intelligence and interrogation."},kw={"brill","forsaken","gallows end","gallows' end tavern","innkeeper","scarlet zealot","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"subzone:brill","zone:tirisfal","npc:captured-scarlet-zealot","topic:forsaken","quest:365","npc:lars","topic:horde"},src={"Gallows' End Tavern"}}
E["subzone:garren-s-haunt"] = {t="subzone",n="Garren's Haunt",z="tirisfal",s="Garren's Haunt is an abandoned farmstead nestled in northern Tirisfal Glades. Once a prosperous human homestead, the farm fell to ruin when the Scourge wiped out the Garren family, leaving the overgrown grounds overrun by feral Rot Hide gnolls.",h="Garren's Haunt is an abandoned farmstead nestled in northern Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Blighted Homestead",b="Before the Third War, this farmstead supported a family and produced bountiful harvests under the Kingdom of Lordaeron. When the Plague of Undeath swept across the countryside, the Scourge descended upon the farm and slaughtered Garren and his kin. Today, the fields lie gray and withered, the farmhouse and barn decaying under the perpetual gloom of Tirisfal.",sp=0},{t="The Rot Hide Squatters",b="Rather than standard Scourge patrols, Garren's Haunt has been claimed by the Rot Hide gnolls—a pack of undead-tainted scavengers led by the vicious Maggot Eye. These scavengers aggressively defend their reclaimed territory, picking clean whatever remains of the farm and savaging any travelers or Forsaken patrols passing along northern Tirisfal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Garren?",a="Garren was a human farmer who lived here with his family prior to the Third War. They worked the surrounding fields until the Scourge overran Lordaeron, butchering Garren and his entire household during the spread of the plague.",al={"garren lore","who lived here","garren story"}},{q="What creatures occupy the farm now?",a="The farm is primarily infested with Rot Hide gnolls led by Maggot Eye. Additionally, a vicious darkhound known as Plague can often be found lurking within the ruins of the barn.",al={"monsters at garrens haunt","what lives here","who controls the farm"}},{q="Why is it called Garren's Haunt?",a="It bears the name of its murdered owner, Garren, with 'Haunt' denoting the grim, abandoned state of the land after the family was slain and their homestead was left to rot under the pall of Tirisfal.",al={"why called haunt","garren name origin"}},{q="Why haven't the Forsaken reclaimed it?",a="The Forsaken are stretched thin fortifying the Undercity and battling threats like the Scarlet Crusade and active Scourge remnants. Dealing with scavengers like the Rot Hide gnolls at outlying farms is largely left to passing mercenaries and adventurers.",al={"why forsaken ignore it","forsaken garrens haunt"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The ruined farm stands as a stark reminder of the slaughter that birthed the Forsaken, and clearing out the filthy Rot Hide gnolls helps secure northern Tirisfal for the Dark Lady."},kw={"darkhound","farmstead","garren's haunt","maggot eye","plague","rot hide","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","topic:gnoll","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron","quest:358"},src={"Garren's Haunt"}}
E["subzone:grave-prison-of-zakajz"] = {t="subzone",n="Grave-Prison of Zakajz",z="tirisfal",s="The Grave-Prison of Zakajz is an ancient, partially collapsed subterranean cavern hidden deep beneath the western reaches of Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the eternal resting place and seal for Zakajz the Corruptor, a monstrous C'Thrax defeated millennia ago by the titan keeper Tyr.",h="The Grave-Prison of Zakajz is an ancient, partially collapsed subterranean cavern hidden deep beneath the...",sec={{t="The Slumbering Corruptor",b="Buried far beneath the earth and connected to the Tomb of Tyr via the perilous passage known as the Darkwalk, this deep cavern holds the remains of Zakajz the Corruptor. Ages ago, the titan keeper Tyr sacrificed himself in a cataclysmic confrontation to defeat the C'Thrax and protect early humanity. Though vanquished, the immense aberration was sealed away in this shadowy vault to ensure its vile corruption would never seep into the surface world.",sp=0},{t="A Sealed Nightmare",b="The atmosphere of the prison is heavy with ancient malice and decay. While the world above attends to mortal wars, the cavern remains haunted by grotesque horrors, including faceless guardians, flesh spawns, and aberrant remnants loyal to the slumbering beast. Its hidden depths remain undisturbed by the kingdoms of Lordaeron, silent and deadly to any foolhardy enough to breach the ancient seals.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Grave-Prison of Zakajz?",a="It is a subterranean chamber buried deep beneath Tirisfal Glades where the titan keeper Tyr entombed the defeated C'Thrax monstrosity known as Zakajz the Corruptor thousands of years ago.",al={"what is this cavern","who is zakajz buried here","prison of zakajz"}},{q="Where is this cavern located?",a="It lies deep beneath the earth under the Tomb of Tyr in western Tirisfal Glades, accessible only through the shadowy subterranean path known as the Darkwalk.",al={"grave prison location","how to get to grave prison","where is it"}},{q="Who was Zakajz the Corruptor?",a="Zakajz was a terrifying, towering C'Thrax servant of the Old Gods. In the ancient past, it hunted early mortals until the noble titan keeper Tyr battled the beast to the death, sacrificing himself to fell the creature.",al={"who is zakajz","zakajz lore","what is a c'thrax"}},{q="What lurks inside the cavern today?",a="The prison is infested with dark aberrations born of old shadows, including faceless corrupters, mindless flesh spawn, and horrifying monstrosities that guard the sealed remains.",al={"grave prison mobs","what lives here","inhabitants of zakajz prison"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="For knights of the holy order, this deep cavern represents the ultimate resting ground of the titan keeper Tyr's final sacrifice, a legendary act of selflessness from which the Silver Hand draws its very inspiration.",["class:Priest"]="Priests studying the delicate balance of the cosmos recognize this desolate subterranean tomb as a monument to ancient shadow, where cosmic malevolence was put to rest by sacrificial grace."},kw={"c'thrax","corruptor","darkwalk","faceless","tirisfal","tomb","tyr","zakajz"},rel={"subzone:tomb-of-tyr","subzone:darkwalk","zone:tirisfal","topic:titan","topic:light"},src={"Grave-Prison of Zakajz"}}
E["subzone:gunther-s-retreat"] = {t="subzone",n="Gunther's Retreat",z="tirisfal",s="Gunther's Retreat is an isolated island sanctuary set in Brightwater Lake in central Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the refuge of Gunther Arcanus, a renegade necromancer who broke free from the Scourge through raw willpower. Distrustful of all outsiders, the recluse surrounds his campsite with loyal undead minions to keep intruders away.",h="Gunther's Retreat is an isolated island sanctuary set in Brightwater Lake in central Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Recluse in Brightwater Lake",b="Situated amid the misty waters of Brightwater Lake, Gunther's Retreat is an unassuming island encampment easily mistaken for another pocket of the Scourge. Its master, Gunther Arcanus, achieved what few mortal sorcerers could: when raised in undeath, his arcane mastery allowed him to tear away his soul from the Lich King's iron grip without any outside help. Mistrusting everyone, Gunther assumed the rest of the undead wandering Lordaeron were still puppets of the Scourge. He retired to this lonely isle to practice his craft in peace, posting zombie sentinels to tear apart anyone who crosses the water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives at Gunther's Retreat?",a="The island is inhabited by Gunther Arcanus, a powerful necromancer who broke free of the Lich King's control under his own power. He resides there alongside a retinue of undead thralls who guard his camp.",al={"gunther island","who is on the island","gunther's retreat master"}},{q="Why are the undead on the island hostile?",a="Gunther Arcanus believes that every other undead being in Tirisfal is still enslaved by the Scourge. Because he values his independence above all else, his minions are commanded to attack anyone who approaches the island on sight.",al={"why does gunther attack","why hostile","is gunther scourge"}},{q="Is Gunther aligned with the Forsaken?",a="Initially, no. While technically a free-willed undead like the Forsaken, Gunther isolates himself entirely. The authorities in the Undercity seek to prove to him that they too are free of the Lich King's grasp and recruit his talents to their cause.",al={"is gunther in the horde","gunther forsaken","gunther undercity"}},{q="What is the small islet southwest of the retreat?",a="Just off the southwestern edge of Gunther's Retreat lies a tiny, unnamed islet known as Lillith's Dinner Table, a curious and eerie landmark resting quietly in the waters of Brightwater Lake.",al={"lillith dinner table","small island near gunther","table island"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Gunther Arcanus mirrors the Forsaken's own tragedy: free from the Lich King, yet suspicious and guarded against a world he assumes remains in thrall to the Scourge.",["class:Mage"]="Arcanists will appreciate Gunther's rare feat; his magical will was formidable enough to sever the Lich King's mental grip entirely unassisted."},kw={"brightwater lake","gunther arcanus","gunther's retreat","lich","lillith's dinner table","tirisfal glades","undead"},rel={"npc:gunther-arcanus","subzone:brightwater-lake","quest:357","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","topic:scourge"},src={"Gunther's Retreat"}}
E["subzone:night-web-s-hollow"] = {t="subzone",n="Night Web's Hollow",z="tirisfal",s="Night Web's Hollow is a sunken vale and abandoned gold mine located just northwest of Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. Heavily overrun with arachnids, it serves as a testing ground for freshly awakened Forsaken sent to cull the vermin and prove their combat readiness.",h="Night Web's Hollow is a sunken vale and abandoned gold mine located just northwest of Deathknell in Tirisfal...",sec={{t="The Infested Mine",b="Tucked away in the northern hills of Deathknell, Night Web's Hollow was once an ordinary human gold mine before the plague swept through Lordaeron. In the aftermath of the kingdom's fall, the shafts were entirely abandoned to nature. Today, thick strands of webbing shroud the rock walls and suffocating shadows conceal a thriving colony of aggressive night web spiders. Freshly raised Forsaken are routinely dispatched into the hollow and its subterranean tunnels to cull the hatchlings, slay their voracious matriarch, and harden their resolve before moving onward into Tirisfal Glades.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Night Web's Hollow?",a="It is an abandoned gold mine and small ravine northwest of Deathknell. Overgrown with webs and swarming with aggressive spiders, it is one of the earliest proving grounds for new Forsaken recruits.",al={"night webs hollow","spider mine deathknell","spider cave tirisfal"}},{q="Why are the Forsaken clearing out the spiders?",a="The encroaching spiders pose an immediate hazard on the perimeter of Deathknell. Executors in town use the infestation as a trial to ensure newly risen undead have regained control over their motor skills and can handle basic combat.",al={"why kill spiders","deathknell spider quest"}},{q="What lives deep inside the mine shafts?",a="While younger spiders skitter outside in the vale, full-grown Night Web Spiders prowl the mine tunnels. In the deepest, darkest chamber sits the Night Web Matriarch, the broodmother of the entire infestation.",al={"spider boss mine","night web matriarch location"}},{q="Was this always a spider den?",a="No. Before the fall of Lordaeron, it was a working gold mine used by the local human populace. After the Scourge wiped out the region, the shafts fell into disrepair and the spiders moved into the dark, sheltered tunnels.",al={"who dug the mine","deathknell mine history"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the freshly risen, the hollow is one of your very first trials. Slaying the arachnids proves you possess the focus and willpower required to serve the Dark Lady.",["profession:Mining"]="Although the shafts were originally excavated for gold, mineral operations here have long since ceased due to the lethal arachnid infestation."},kw={"deathknell","mine","night web matriarch","night web's hollow","spiders","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken"},src={"Night Web's Hollow"}}
E["subzone:nightmare-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Nightmare Vale",z="tirisfal",s="Nightmare Vale is a shadowed hollow nestled in southwestern Tirisfal Glades, just west of the Scarlet Watchtower. Once a lush forest haven, its trees have withered under the blight, and vicious predators now roam among the twisted trunks.",h="Nightmare Vale is a shadowed hollow nestled in southwestern Tirisfal Glades, just west of the Scarlet...",sec={{t="A Decayed Wilderness",b="Before the Third War, this valley was a verdant part of the Tirisfal countryside, filled with songbirds and standard woodland game. In the wake of the Scourge's plague, the vegetation has blackened and rotted away. Ravenous darkhounds and massive vampire bats have devoured the native wildlife, turning the hollow into a grim haven for scavengers and beasts of prey.",sp=0},{t="Stalkers of the Hollow",b="Lurking in the shadows of Nightmare Vale is Ressan the Needler, an unusually large, pale vampire bat notorious among local travelers. Wedged uncomfortably between the haunted wilderness and the zealous sentries at the nearby Scarlet Watchtower, the vale is an unforgiving expanse where unwary adventurers quickly become prey.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nightmare Vale located?",a="Nightmare Vale lies in the southwestern reaches of Tirisfal Glades, tucked just west of the Scarlet Watchtower.",al={"nightmare vale location","where is nightmare vale","find nightmare vale"}},{q="Why is the valley called Nightmare Vale?",a="Once a peaceful, vibrant forest, the valley succumbed completely to the plague that devastated Lordaeron. Its withered trees and aggressive predators—hungry darkhounds and blood-drinking bats—make it a waking nightmare for anyone passing through.",al={"why nightmare vale","nightmare vale lore"}},{q="What creatures roam Nightmare Vale?",a="The vale is overrun by savage darkhounds and giant vampire bats that have driven out or consumed the native forest animals. The rare white vampire bat, Ressan the Needler, also prowls this hollow.",al={"nightmare vale mobs","monsters in nightmare vale","beasts here"}},{q="Who is Ressan the Needler?",a="Ressan the Needler is a rare, stark-white vampire bat known to stalk the darkened skies and withered canopy of Nightmare Vale.",al={"ressan","ressan the needler","rare bat tirisfal"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The twisted wildlife of Nightmare Vale serves as a reminder of the plague's lingering footprint across Tirisfal, posing an immediate threat to Forsaken travelers venturing beyond Brill.",["class:Hunter"]="The vale is home to vicious darkhounds and vampire bats, including the rare white bat Ressan the Needler, making it a noteworthy proving ground for hunters seeking fearsome beasts."},kw={"darkhounds","nightmare vale","ressan the needler","scarlet watchtower","tirisfal glades","vampire bats"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:scarlet-watchtower"},src={"Nightmare Vale"}}
E["subzone:north-coast"] = {t="subzone",n="North Coast",z="tirisfal",s="The North Coast is a bleak, fog-shrouded stretch of shoreline marking the northern edge of Tirisfal Glades along the Great Sea. Tainted by the fall of Lordaeron, the cold beaches are littered with rotting marine life and aggressively defended by tribes of hostile murlocs.",h="The North Coast is a bleak, fog-shrouded stretch of shoreline marking the northern edge of Tirisfal Glades...",sec={{t="A Blighted Shoreline",b="Before the Third War, these northern waters and stony beaches were part of the peaceful northern boundary of Lordaeron. When the Plague of Undeath swept across the continent, its corrupting blight seeped down the bluffs and poisoned the coast. The waters turned chill and murky, washing up the carcasses of giant sea creatures that now rot upon the sand amid the perennial coastal fog.",sp=0},{t="The Vile Fin Shore",b="With the human kingdom shattered and the Forsaken focusing their attention around Brill and the Capital City, coastal murlocs claimed the desolate sands. The local Vile Fin tribe maintains huts along the surf, utilizing nearby shallows as spawning grounds. Swarms of ravenous murlocs, including notable figures like Deeb and numerous growing tadpoles, violently guard the tideline against any surface-dwellers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What creatures inhabit the North Coast?",a="The beach is primarily occupied by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs, their tadpoles, and scavengers picking at the rotting sea life that washes ashore from the Great Sea.",al={"north coast mobs","what lives on north coast","monsters north coast"}},{q="Who is Deeb?",a="Deeb is an individual murloc who can be found lingering along the North Coast among the huts and shallows of the shore.",al={"deeb","murloc deeb","who is deeb"}},{q="Why is the coast covered in rotting carcasses?",a="The Plague of Undeath that devastated Lordaeron seeped into the coastal ecology, poisoning the surrounding shallows and causing dead marine beasts to wash ashore to decay on the blighted sand.",al={"dead sea monsters","beached whales tirisfal","why dead creatures"}},{q="Is the North Coast contested by any major factions?",a="Neither the Forsaken nor any remnants of the Alliance actively garrison the North Coast. It remains a wild, untamed fringe left largely to murlocs and sea vermin.",al={"who owns north coast","forsaken presence north coast"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="While Forsaken patrol routes cling to the road through Brill, clearing the North Coast of encroaching murlocs ensures the northern flank of Tirisfal Glades remains relatively secure."},kw={"beach","deeb","great sea","murloc","north coast","tirisfal glades","vile fin"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","topic:murloc","subzone:brill","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"North Coast"}}
E["subzone:rotbrain-encampment"] = {t="subzone",n="Rotbrain Encampment",z="tirisfal",s="The Rotbrain Encampment is a hostile encampment situated just outside Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. It is held by newly risen undead who refuse allegiance to Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken, lashing out in confusion and rage.",h="The Rotbrain Encampment is a hostile encampment situated just outside Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Gathering of the Refusal",b="Not all corpses raised from the graves of Tirisfal Glades willingly accept their dark renewal. The Rotbrain Encampment gathers those freshly awakened dead who have succumbed to madness, confusion, or fierce denial. Under the command of Marcus Redpath, these mindless and recalcitrant undead, known as Rotbrains, congregate on the perimeter of Deathknell to plot vengeance against the Dark Lady's realm. Skirmishing incessantly with Deathguard Protectors, the encampment represents an immediate internal threat to the stability of the Forsaken's newborn ranks.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Rotbrain Encampment?",a="It is an outpost just outside Deathknell inhabited by newly resurrected undead who reject joining the Forsaken. Driven by confusion, madness, and denial, they organize under hostile leadership to strike back against Deathknell.",al={"rotbrain camp","deathknell rotbrains","where are the rotbrains"}},{q="Who leads the Rotbrain Encampment?",a="The encampment is rallied under Marcus Redpath, an undead who refuses to serve the Forsaken and seeks vengeance against Sylvanas's followers.",al={"who leads rotbrains","rotbrain leader","marcus redpath camp"}},{q="Why do the Rotbrains attack the Forsaken?",a="Upon waking from the grave, some undead cannot cope with the shock of their horrific transformation. Lost in denial, grief, or outright fury, they view the Forsaken as tormentors rather than liberators and lash out violently.",al={"why are rotbrains hostile","why do rotbrains fight","rotbrain motives"}},{q="What kinds of enemies inhabit the camp?",a="The encampment is fortified with aggressive Rotbrain Berserkers and spellcasting Rotbrain Magi, who constantly skirmish with stationed Deathguard Protectors.",al={"rotbrain types","rotbrain mobs"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The camp is a stark reminder of the tragedy of resurrection, showcasing the fate of those whose minds shatter upon waking into undeath.",["faction:Horde"]="Securing Deathknell's borders from chaotic renegades is crucial for maintaining the Horde's foothold across Lordaeron."},kw={"berserker","darnell","deathknell","forsaken","magi","marcus redpath","rotbrain","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:deathknell","npc:marcus-redpath","topic:forsaken","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Rotbrain Encampment"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery",z="tirisfal",s="Perched in the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery was once a peaceful center of scholarship and worship for the Church of the Holy Light. In the wake of Lordaeron's fall, it has become a heavily fortified redoubt for the fanatical Scarlet Crusade. Anyone approaching without red colors is treated as an infected carrier of the plague and executed on sight.",h="Perched in the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery was once a peaceful center of...",sec={{t="From Sanctuary to Stronghold",b="Before the Third War, this complex was known simply as the Old Monastery. Under the stewardship of Lordaeron's priesthood and the patronage of noble houses, it served as a vital center for theological study, sacred archives, and paladin training. When the Kingdom of Lordaeron fell to the Scourge, surviving remnants of the Silver Hand reclaimed the site as a forward bastion to strike against the undead occupying Capital City. As the defenders devolved into the zealous Scarlet Crusade, they fortified the cloister, turning its peaceful libraries, gardens, and cathedral into an armed citadel.",sp=0},{t="A Bastion of Fanaticism",b="Divided into four distinct wings—a defiled graveyard, an expansive library, an armory, and a grand cathedral—the Monastery now houses a massive garrison commanded by Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane. The Crusaders here view all outsiders, whether living or undead, Alliance or Horde, as plague-bearers. While the Forsaken seek to eliminate the garrison threatening their very doorstep, Alliance leadership increasingly views the Crusade's violent extremism as a dangerous perversion of the Light.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Monastery here?",a="It was originally built during the reign of Lordaeron as a peaceful sanctuary for study, housing sacred scriptures and training paladins. Surviving crusaders seized and fortified it after the kingdom fell to serve as a military staging ground against the undead in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"what is scarlet monastery","why did they build monastery in tirisfal","monastery purpose"}},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade attack Alliance members?",a="The Crusade's zealotry has spiraled into complete paranoia. They believe anyone who has traveled outside their secured compounds could be a carrier of the Scourge's plague of undeath, and they refuse to take chances with outsiders regardless of race or allegiance.",al={"why are scarlet hostile to alliance","are scarlet crusade alliance","why do crusaders attack humans"}},{q="Who leads the forces within the Monastery?",a="The garrison is held by Scarlet Commander Mograine, who directs military operations from within the cathedral, and High Inquisitor Whitemane, a zealous priestess renowned for her devotion and resurrection powers.",al={"who is the boss of scarlet monastery","monastery leaders","who runs the scarlet crusade here"}},{q="What are the four wings of the complex?",a="The complex is split into four distinct areas: the Graveyard, overrun by restless dead and torture chambers; the Library, preserving historical archives and tomes; the Armory, where the Crusade manufactures weapons and armor; and the Cathedral, the spiritual heart and commander's seat.",al={"monastery sections","what wings are in scarlet monastery","monastery layout"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The Monastery sits right on the Undercity's doorstep, making its heavily armed crusaders an active, existential threat to Forsaken territory.",["class:Paladin"]="The complex once trained paladins under the Silver Hand, making its corruption into an intolerant bastion of fanaticism a bitter sight for faithful holy warriors."},kw={"armory","cathedral","graveyard","library","mograine","old monastery","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral","subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory","subzone:scarlet-monastery-library","subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard","npc:scarlet-commander-mograine","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Scarlet Monastery"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-palisade"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Palisade",z="tirisfal",s="The Scarlet Palisade is a fortified redoubt held by the Scarlet Crusade in western Tirisfal Glades. Positioned just west of Solliden Farmstead, this encampment guards the nearby human farms against the Forsaken and any other non-human intruders.",h="The Scarlet Palisade is a fortified redoubt held by the Scarlet Crusade in western Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Crusader Bulwark",b="Erected along the rugged terrain west of Solliden Farmstead, the Scarlet Palisade serves as a forward defensive line for the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades. Heavy wooden stakes, watchtowers, and constant patrols ring the encampment, maintaining a militant perimeter deep within territory claimed by the Forsaken. At the center of these fortifications stands the Crusader's Outpost, coordinating the zealots stationed here.",sp=0},{t="Shielding the Farmstead",b="The primary role of the Scarlet Palisade is securing the adjacent farmland and ensuring that the Crusade retains a foothold over vital agrarian lands in the glades. Scarlet warriors garrisoned at the palisade strike down any outsiders, undead or otherwise, who approach Solliden Farmstead, treating all non-humans as lethal threats to their holy mission.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Scarlet Palisade?",a="The Scarlet Palisade is a heavily fortified Scarlet Crusade military encampment located west of Solliden Farmstead in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"scarlet palisade","what is this camp","scarlet fort tirisfal"}},{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade stationed here?",a="Crusaders garrison the palisade to protect the adjacent Solliden Farmstead and maintain a secure enclave in Tirisfal Glades, attacking any non-humans who stray near.",al={"why are scarlet crusade here","crusade purpose tirisfal","why palisade"}},{q="What building sits in the middle of the camp?",a="At the center of the camp stands the Crusader's Outpost, a fortified redoubt that anchors the palisade's defenses.",al={"center building","tower in palisade","crusaders outpost"}},{q="Are the Crusaders hostile to the Alliance?",a="While originating from the human and dwarven defenders of Lordaeron, the Scarlet Crusade has degenerated into fanatical xenophobia. They view virtually all outsiders and non-humans with suspicion or open hostility.",al={"is scarlet crusade hostile to alliance","will scarlet attack alliance","scarlet friendly"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Palisade represents an entrenched enemy stronghold right on the doorstep of the Undercity, manned by zealots dedicated to the total extermination of the Forsaken.",["faction:Horde"]="The fortified camp poses an immediate danger to traveling Horde scouts moving through western Tirisfal Glades."},kw={"crusader's outpost","crusaders","scarlet crusade","scarlet palisade","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades"},rel={"subzone:crusader-s-outpost","subzone:solliden-farmstead","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Scarlet Palisade"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-watch-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Watch Post",z="tirisfal",s="The Scarlet Watch Post is an isolated watchtower stationed in the rocky hills of northeastern Tirisfal Glades, just north of the Scarlet Monastery. Maintained by a vigilant garrison of Crusaders, its sole purpose is to safeguard the monastery's vulnerable northern flank against flanking assaults.",h="The Scarlet Watch Post is an isolated watchtower stationed in the rocky hills of northeastern Tirisfal...",sec={{t="Guarding the Northern Approach",b="Perched in the rugged heights behind the Scarlet Monastery, the Scarlet Watch Post serves as a critical early-warning bastion for the zealots below. While the southern road up to the monastery gate receives heavy traffic and fortifications, the rugged cliffs along Tirisfal's northern coastline provide a tempting back route for infiltrators. To eliminate this blind spot, the Scarlet Crusade maintains this fortified stone tower—one of several Crusader outposts scattered across Tirisfal Glades. Under the stern command of Captain Melrache, a mixed force of Neophytes, Vanguards, and devout Friars keeps ceaseless vigil over the cliffs, ensuring neither the Scourge nor the Forsaken can surprise the order from behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Scarlet Watch Post?",a="The outpost protects the Scarlet Monastery from being flanked. While the monastery's main entrance faces south toward the Tirisfal roads, its rear slopes toward the northern wilderness, leaving it vulnerable to coordinated assaults. The watch post ensures sentries spot and intercept any intruders attempting a northern bypass.",al={"why is scarlet watch post here","scarlet watch post purpose","crusaders run role"}},{q="Who commands the Scarlet Watch Post?",a="Captain Melrache oversees the garrison stationed at the tower. He commands a defensive retinue including personal bodyguards, front-line Vanguards, aspiring Neophytes, and spellcasting Friars.",al={"scarlet watch post leader","who leads scarlet watch post","captain melrache"}},{q="Is the Scarlet Watch Post related to the other towers in Tirisfal?",a="Yes. It is one of four distinct Crusader outposts ringing the northern and western reaches of Tirisfal Glades. These stone towers create a defensive perimeter to monitor Scourge activity and contain the Forsaken expansion from the Undercity.",al={"tirisfal towers","crusader outposts tirisfal","other scarlet towers"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Scarlet Crusade is an existential threat lingering right on the Undercity's doorstep; purging isolated towers like this disrupts the zealots' communication network and secures northern Tirisfal.",["faction:Horde"]="The Crusaders view all outsiders—living or dead—as tainted carriers of undeath, making this watch post strictly hostile ground to any Horde travelers braving the hills."},kw={"captain melrache","crusader outpost","crusader's run","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scarlet watch post","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","subzone:crusader-s-outpost","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Scarlet Watch Post"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-watchtower"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Watchtower",z="tirisfal",s="The Scarlet Watchtower is a ruined scout outpost nestled in the southern hills of Tirisfal Glades. Held by the zealous Scarlet Crusade, it provides a direct vantage over aerial traffic entering and leaving the Undercity. Its close proximity to the Forsaken capital's rear sewer entrance makes it a constant thorn in the side of the local undead defenders.",h="The Scarlet Watchtower is a ruined scout outpost nestled in the southern hills of Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Thorn at the Gates",b="Perched above the southern ridge of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Watchtower serves as an audacious observation post for the Scarlet Crusade. Standing mere paces away from the sewer back entrance of the Undercity, the ruined tower allows crusader scouts to monitor incoming and outgoing flight routes and surface movements into Queen Sylvanas's capital. Commanded by Captain Perrine, the zealots stationed here dare to gaze directly into the heart of Forsaken territory, seeking any opportunity to gather intelligence or strike at the undead they consider abominations.",sp=0},{t="Network of Zealotry",b="The tower is not an isolated redoubt, but one of four Crusader's Outposts established across Tirisfal Glades. Together, these vantage points form an early-warning web and scouting perimeter for Scarlet forces operating against Lordaeron's new masters. Its position so close to the ruined kingdom's seat of power makes it an intolerable insult to the Royal Apothecary Society and Forsaken commanders, who regularly direct emerging champions to thin the outpost's ranks and silence Captain Perrine.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade so close to the Undercity?",a="The Scarlet Crusade established the watchtower to monitor flight routes and scouting movement coming in and out of the Forsaken capital. Its high vantage point near the southern hills allows them to keep an eye on undead surface operations and the nearby sewer exit.",al={"why scarlet tower near undercity","scarlet watchtower purpose","why are scarlets here"}},{q="Who commands the Scarlet Watchtower?",a="The outpost is commanded by Captain Perrine, a Scarlet Crusade officer who directs local scouts and maintains surveillance over the approaches to the Undercity.",al={"scarlet watchtower boss","tower commander","captain perrine"}},{q="How does this tower fit into the wider Scarlet presence in Tirisfal?",a="This tower is one of four Crusader's Outposts strategically scattered across Tirisfal Glades. Together, they create a scouting network designed to harass Forsaken patrols and keep the Scarlet Crusade informed of undead maneuvers.",al={"other scarlet towers","crusader outposts tirisfal","scarlet network"}},{q="What is the tower's connection to the Sewers of the Undercity?",a="The tower sits directly in the southern hills near the drainage canal leading into the Undercity Sewers. This backdoor passage is an important alternative route into the capital, making the presence of hostile crusaders right above it an active security hazard for the Forsaken.",al={"tower near sewers","undercity back door tower","sewer entrance scarlet"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The existence of an enemy observation tower practically peering into your capital's drainage exits is an unacceptable indignity that local Forsaken authorities are eager to eliminate.",["faction:Horde"]="Travelers and scouts arriving on bat-back to the Undercity risk coming under observation from the zealous sharpshooters stationed on the heights of this tower."},kw={"captain perrine","crusader's outpost","scarlet crusade","scarlet watchtower","sewers","tirisfal glades","undercity"},rel={"topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:crusader-s-outpost","zone:undercity","subzone:sewers","zone:tirisfal","topic:forsaken","quest:94"},src={"Scarlet Watchtower"}}
E["subzone:shadow-grave"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadow Grave",z="tirisfal",s="Shadow Grave is a stone crypt perched atop the sloping burial grounds above Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades. It serves as the physical awakening point where newly liberated Forsaken shake off the stupor of death and the Lich King's faded control.",h="Shadow Grave is a stone crypt perched atop the sloping burial grounds above Deathknell in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="Cradle of the Forsaken",b="Tucked into the rocky foothills behind Deathknell Graves, the Shadow Grave is a simple stone mausoleum with an extraordinary purpose. Inside its damp vaults, corpses raised into the mindless servitude of the Scourge gradually awaken to free will. Under the watchful eye of caretakers like Undertaker Mordo, these freshly liberated undead stand up from their stone slabs and take their first shuddering steps into a world that despises them, setting out down the footpath toward Deathknell to pledge themselves to the Banshee Queen.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Shadow Grave used for?",a="It is the crypt where newly awakened Forsaken rise into consciousness. Instead of remaining mindless Scourge thralls in the dirt, these resurrected individuals regain their free will inside the tomb and begin their second life serving Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"shadow grave purpose","what is shadow grave","shadow grave crypt"}},{q="Where is the Shadow Grave located?",a="Shadow Grave is situated at the top of the hill above the Deathknell Graves, backed against the southern mountains of Tirisfal Glades. A dirt trail winds downhill from its entrance toward the settlement of Deathknell.",al={"where is shadow grave","shadow grave location","shadow grave map"}},{q="Who oversees the newly awakened here?",a="Undertaker Mordo attends the newly awakened within the tomb, assessing whether those rising from the slabs have recovered their minds and are fit to serve the Forsaken cause.",al={"who is in shadow grave","shadow grave npcs","undertaker mordo location"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Every Forsaken adventurer begins their journey on the cold stone slabs of this crypt, opening their eyes to the grim reality of unlife and free will."},kw={"awakening","crypt","deathknell","shadow grave","starting tomb","tirisfal glades","undertaker mordo"},rel={"subzone:deathknell-graves","subzone:deathknell","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Shadow Grave"}}
E["subzone:solliden-farmstead"] = {t="subzone",n="Solliden Farmstead",z="tirisfal",s="Solliden Farmstead is an active human pumpkin farm nestled in western Tirisfal Glades, just north of Deathknell. It represents a rare anomaly in northern Lordaeron: living native farmers who survived the Plague of Undeath and cling fiercely to their soil under the shadow of the Scarlet Crusade.",h="Solliden Farmstead is an active human pumpkin farm nestled in western Tirisfal Glades, just north of...",sec={{t="A Defiant Remnant",b="While most of Lordaeron fell to ruin and rot, the fields of Solliden Farmstead still produce healthy crops. The settlement traces its lineage back centuries to when immigrant noble families from Strom acquired pioneer plots across Tirisfal. Today, these surviving human farmers live under the watchful shield of the Scarlet Crusade garrisoned at the nearby Scarlet Palisade. Traumatized and insular, they defend their homestead with unyielding hostility, striking at any outsiders who draw near—Horde and Alliance alike.",sp=0},{t="Eyes in the Undercity",b="To the Forsaken just emerging from Deathknell, Solliden is both a threat and a resource. The Royal Apothecary Society eyes the farm's pristine pumpkins as prime organic testing material for brewing their New Plague. Meanwhile, Forsaken military officers like Deathguard Simmer view these living enclaves as a dangerous potential foothold for Stormwind or Gilneas, dispatching operatives to cut down the farmers before they can ever organize into a southern-backed offensive.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there living humans farming in Tirisfal Glades?",a="The Solliden farmers are native Lordaeron humans who miraculously escaped infection during the Third War. Shielded by the nearby Scarlet Crusade at the Scarlet Palisade, they stubbornly continue cultivating the land rather than fleeing their ancestral home.",al={"why are they alive","who are these farmers","living humans in tirisfal"}},{q="Why are the Solliden farmers hostile to Alliance players?",a="Living through the fall of Lordaeron has left the farmers paranoid, bitter, and completely untrusting of anyone outside their immediate circle. Protected by the fanatical Scarlet Crusade, they view all trespassers as potential threats or infected scavengers, attacking Alliance and Horde travelers indiscriminately.",al={"why do farmers attack alliance","are they alliance","why red to alliance"}},{q="Why do the Forsaken want pumpkins from Solliden Farmstead?",a="Apothecaries serving the Royal Apothecary Society require fresh, uncorrupted organic matter to test and refine their New Plague. The plump, untainted pumpkins growing in Solliden's soil serve as ideal living hosts for developing toxic strains.",al={"why steal pumpkins","fields of grief pumpkin quest","royal apothecary society pumpkins"}},{q="Who is Deathguard Simmer, and why does he target the farm?",a="Deathguard Simmer is a Forsaken officer stationed near Deathknell. He views the surviving farmers as a looming security risk, fearing that the Kingdom of Stormwind or neighboring Gilneas might eventually recruit and arm them as an Alliance vanguard against the Undercity.",al={"why kill the farmers","deathguard simmer quest","reaping the reapers"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the newly risen Forsaken, Solliden Farmstead is an immediate lesson in realpolitik: living Lordaeronians who despise what you have become, serving as both raw material for Apothecary toxins and a potential southern beachhead.",["faction:Alliance"]="Seeing living humans tilling Lordaeron's soil brings a glimmer of hope, but the bitter reality is that these isolated survivors view Stormwind's citizens with the same xenophobic hatred they hold for the undead."},kw={"deathguard simmer","deathknell","fields of grief","pumpkins","scarlet palisade","solliden","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:scarlet-palisade","subzone:deathknell","quest:365","npc:deathguard-simmer","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:calston-estate"},src={"Solliden Farmstead"}}
E["subzone:stillwater-pond"] = {t="subzone",n="Stillwater Pond",z="tirisfal",s="Stillwater Pond is a quiet, stagnant body of water resting just west of Brill in Tirisfal Glades. Once a beloved picnic and swimming spot for the living children of Lordaeron, it has decayed into a murky pool inhabited by skeletal fish and prowled by dangerous scavengers.",h="Stillwater Pond is a quiet, stagnant body of water resting just west of Brill in Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Ruined Respite",b="Before the Third War and the ravages of the Plague of Undeath, Stillwater Pond served as a tranquil retreat for the folk of Tirisfal Glades. Families from nearby hamlets gathered on its grassy banks for afternoon picnics, and children too young to brave the treacherous depths of Brightwater Lake learned to swim in its shallows. Today, the idyllic waters have turned lifeless and gray. The living have long vanished, leaving only skeletal fish darting beneath the surface and wandering undead drifting through the surrounding woods.",sp=0},{t="Prowlers in the Mist",b="Though quiet compared to the besieged roads and contested farms of Tirisfal, Stillwater Pond holds its own perils. The murky waters provide water only to the blighted beasts of the glades, most notably a ferocious darkhound named Bayne who stalks the shoreline. Travelers cutting through the western meadows on their way toward Brill must tread carefully, as predatory beasts and aimless zombies frequently linger along the water's edge.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Stillwater Pond like before the Plague?",a="In the days of human Lordaeron, Stillwater Pond was a scenic and popular spot for local picnics. Because it was shallow and calmer than the expansive Brightwater Lake, families frequently brought young children here to swim safely.",al={"stillwater pond history","what was stillwater pond used for","tirisfal swimming spot"}},{q="Is there anything living in the water now?",a="Normal aquatic life did not survive the blighting of Tirisfal. The only things swimming beneath the gray surface are the animated, skeletal remains of fish left behind by the Scourge's corruption.",al={"stillwater pond fish","what lives in stillwater pond","stillwater creatures"}},{q="What dangerous creatures wander near the pond?",a="Apart from mindless undead wandering the glades, the most notorious threat along the shore is Bayne, an unusually powerful and aggressive darkhound who feeds on unwary travelers.",al={"stillwater pond monsters","who is bayne","darkhound near brill"}},{q="Where is Stillwater Pond located?",a="Stillwater Pond sits in central Tirisfal Glades, directly west of the town of Brill and southwest of the larger Brightwater Lake.",al={"where is stillwater pond","stillwater pond location","how to find stillwater pond"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For Forsaken who retain memories of life in Lordaeron, Stillwater Pond stands as a grim reminder of lost childhood days spent picnicking and swimming along its once-clear banks.",["class:Hunter"]="The blighted wildlife around the pond, including feral darkhounds like Bayne, makes the area a hazardous hunting ground for scouts patrolling the outskirts of Brill."},kw={"bayne","brightwater lake","brill","darkhound","skeletal fish","stillwater pond","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:brill","subzone:brightwater-lake","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:forsaken"},src={"Stillwater Pond"}}
E["subzone:tomb-of-tyr"] = {t="subzone",n="Tomb of Tyr",z="tirisfal",s="The Tomb of Tyr, also known as Keeper's Rest, is a sealed subterranean vault buried deep beneath the waters of Tyr's Fall in the Whispering Forest. It was constructed eons ago to entomb the fallen titan-forged Keeper Tyr alongside the monstrous C'Thraxxi horror he died destroying.",h="The Tomb of Tyr, also known as Keeper's Rest, is a sealed subterranean vault buried deep beneath the waters...",sec={{t="A Monument to Sacrifice",b="Following the cataclysmic battle between Keeper Tyr and Zakajz the Corruptor, Tyr's surviving titan-forged companions laid the keeper to rest beneath the earth of Tirisfal. Alongside him, they entombed his sacred warhammer—the Silver Hand—and sealed away the remains of Zakajz. Potent wards were bound directly to the weapon to ensure the crypt remained undisturbed. The vrykul warrior Yrgrim the Truthseeker and his followers remained behind to guard the vault, establishing the secretive order known as Tyr's Guard, which eventually passed its sacred vigil onto early humanity.",sp=0},{t="The Folly of Thoradin",b="Centuries later, High King Thoradin sought out the legends of the buried titan and forced his way past Tyr's Guard into the subterranean complex. Recklessly commanding his imperial magi to unravel the ancient protective seals, Thoradin accidentally revived the dormant monstrosity Zakajz. In the desperate, bloody battle that followed, Thoradin sacrificed his life by driving his greatsword, Strom'kar, directly into the horror's skull. The blade's enchantments forced the beast into an enduring slumber, sealing both the king and the monster within the darkness below.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is buried in the Tomb of Tyr?",a="The vault holds the remains of Keeper Tyr, a great titan-forged guardian of ancient Azeroth, alongside his great silver warhammer. It also entombs the body of Zakajz the Corruptor, a colossal C'Thraxxi abomination, as well as the ancient human High King Thoradin.",al={"who is buried here","who lies in tyr's tomb","what is in the tomb of tyr"}},{q="Where is the entrance to the tomb?",a="The tomb lies deep beneath the Whispering Forest in western Tirisfal Glades. Its hidden entrance rests underwater at the bottom of the lake known as Tyr's Fall.",al={"how to get into tyr's tomb","tomb of tyr location","where is keepers rest"}},{q="What is Tyr's Guard?",a="Tyr's Guard was a secretive brotherhood founded by ancient vrykul who stayed behind after Tyr's death. As the curse of flesh transformed them, they inducted the earliest humans into their order, passing down the duty of guarding the tomb and keeping Zakajz sealed away.",al={"tyrs guard","who guards the tomb","guardians of tyr"}},{q="What happened to King Thoradin in the tomb?",a="Thoradin entered the tomb seeking power and broke the wards holding Zakajz dead, accidentally reawakening the beast. Thoradin gave his life to drive his sword, Strom'kar, into the horror's brain, locking the beast into a deep magical slumber.",al={"thoradin death","how did thoradin die","what happened to thoradin"}}},ang={["race:Human"]="The tomb holds monumental significance for humanity: it is the resting place of High King Thoradin, the founder of Arathor, and the root origin of Tirisfal's name and early human reverence for the Silver Hand.",["class:Paladin"]="The legendary Keeper Tyr gave his life here fighting cosmic evil, leaving behind the archetype of self-sacrifice and the silver hand icon that forms the spiritual foundation of paladin orders."},kw={"keeper's rest","silver hand","thoradin","tomb of tyr","tyr","tyr's fall","tyr's guard","zakajz"},rel={"subzone:tyr-s-fall","subzone:whispering-forest","zone:tirisfal","subzone:vestibule-of-the-silver-hand","subzone:grave-prison-of-zakajz","subzone:darkwalk","topic:titan"},src={"Tomb of Tyr"}}
E["subzone:tyr-s-fall"] = {t="subzone",n="Tyr's Fall",z="tirisfal",s="Tyr's Fall is a craterous lake hidden deep within the Whispering Forest in western Tirisfal Glades. In the ancient tongue of the vrykul, 'Tyr's Fall' translates to 'Tirisfal', providing the entire glade with its namesake. Beneath its tranquil waters lies the ancient, buried tomb of the fallen titan keeper Tyr and the monstrous horror he sacrificed his life to defeat.",h="Tyr's Fall is a craterous lake hidden deep within the Whispering Forest in western Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="The Fall of the Keeper",b="Thousands of years ago, the titan keeper Tyr fled south from the far north alongside Archaedas, Ironaya, and their followers. Pursued by two titanic horrors sent by the corrupted keeper Loken—the C'Thrax generals Zakajz and Kith'ix—Tyr made a desperate stand to buy his comrades time to escape. For six days and nights, arcane fury and shadow magic tore through the peaceful forest. Exhausted, Tyr unleashed all of his remaining life force in a cataclysmic explosion. The blast laid low Zakajz and forced Kith'ix to flee, carving a massive crater into the earth. Ironaya named the hollow 'Tyr's Fall' in honor of their fallen champion.",sp=0},{t="A Silent Vigil",b="Following the battle, Tyr and Zakajz were interred where they fell, with the keeper's great silver hand placed atop the burial site as a monument. While Archaedas and Ironaya journeyed onward to Uldaman, a devoted contingent of vrykul remained behind to guard the resting place, eventually passing their vigil down to humanity through an order known as Tyr's Guard. In the ages since, the crater filled with water, submerging the tomb beneath a secluded lake while the quiet woods swallowed all obvious trace of the ancient clash.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the connection between Tyr's Fall and Tirisfal Glades?",a="The glade takes its name directly from the site. In the ancient vrykul tongue, 'Tyr's Fall' translates directly to 'Tirisfal', commemorating the place where the titan keeper Tyr gave his life to protect his followers.",al={"why is it called tirisfal","meaning of tirisfal","tirisfal name origin"}},{q="What lies beneath the lake?",a="Beneath the crater lake lies the Tomb of Tyr. It houses the remains of the titan keeper Tyr along with the corpse of the ancient monstrosity Zakajz, sealed together in deep stone beneath ancient wards.",al={"whats under the lake","tomb under tyrs fall","tyrs fall tomb"}},{q="Why is the area so secluded?",a="Tyr's Fall sits tucked away in the Whispering Forest, nestled deep in the mountainous northwestern borders of Tirisfal Glades. Ringed by steep ridges and untouched by the roads connecting Lordaeron's old towns, the secluded lake has stayed largely forgotten by common travelers.",al={"where is tyrs fall","how do you get here","whispering forest lake"}},{q="Who guarded the tomb after Tyr died?",a="The vrykul followers who witnessed Tyr's sacrifice resolved to guard his resting place forever, founding the order known as Tyr's Guard. As mortality took its toll, they inducted early human tribes into their ranks, passing down the history and their solemn oath across generations.",al={"who watched the tomb","tyrs guard lore","vrykul at tyrs fall"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The Order of the Silver Hand draws its inspiration and name from the silver hand of Tyr, whose legendary self-sacrifice for others occurred right beneath these waters.",["race:Human"]="Early human ancestors were taught the virtues of justice and sacrifice by the ancient guardians here, laying the spiritual groundwork for Lordaeron's earliest moral traditions."},kw={"keeper tyr","tirisfal","titan","tomb of tyr","tyr's fall","tyr's guard","tyrs fall","whispering forest","zakajz"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:whispering-forest","subzone:tomb-of-tyr","topic:titan","subzone:uldaman","topic:lordaeron","topic:scourge"},src={"Tyr's Fall"}}
E["subzone:undercity"] = {t="subzone",n="Undercity",z="tirisfal",s="Carved beneath the shattered palace of Capital City, the Undercity serves as the sprawling subterranean stronghold of the Forsaken. Originally a tangle of royal crypts, dungeons, and sewers expanded by the Scourge, it was seized by Sylvanas Windrunner and forged into a heavily fortified capital for her free-willed undead.",h="Carved beneath the shattered palace of Capital City, the Undercity serves as the sprawling subterranean...",sec={{t="From Royal Crypts to Scourge Bastion",b="Before the Third War, the subterranean passages beneath Capital City were known as the Undercity—a vast network of sewers, royal catacombs, and dungeons. It was here that the Alliance once imprisoned the captured warchief Orgrim Doomhammer, and where the poorest citizens scraped a living in the dark. During the fall of Lordaeron, Prince Arthas Menethil ordered his Scourge to begin expanding these depths into a subterranean seat of power. When the Lich King summoned Arthas away to Northrend, the death knight left the construction unfinished.",sp=0},{t="The Forsaken Capital",b="Amid the civil war in the Plaguelands, Sylvanas Windrunner rallied those undead whose minds had broken free from the Lich King's grip. After overthrowing the dreadlords and driving out rival forces, the newly christened Forsaken claimed the subterranean complex. They completed the twisted maze of catacombs the Scourge had started, fortifying it into an impenetrable stronghold beneath the silent ruins of their former kingdom. Today, the Dark Lady rules her people from within its poisoned halls.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Was Undercity always here before the undead took over?",a="Yes, though in a much smaller form. Under the Kingdom of Lordaeron, the area beneath the palace held ancient royal crypts, dungeons, and the city's sewer system, where paupers dwelled and high-profile prisoners—including the captured Orc warchief Orgrim Doomhammer—were kept.",al={"undercity origins","was undercity always there","history of undercity"}},{q="Who actually built the modern Undercity?",a="The initial expansion was begun by Prince Arthas Menethil, who intended to make it the Scourge's seat of power in Lordaeron. When Arthas was recalled to Northrend, Sylvanas Windrunner and her Forsaken captured the unfinished tunnels and spent years excavating and fortifying them into the fortress city seen today.",al={"who made undercity","who built the undercity","undercity construction"}},{q="Why live underground instead of rebuilding the city above?",a="The surface ruins of Capital City are exposed to attacks from the Scarlet Crusade, Scourge remnants, and the Alliance. The subterranean catacombs are naturally defensible, hidden from view, and well suited to the needs of the undead, who do not require daylight, warmth, or open air.",al={"why live underground","why not rebuild lordaeron","why undercity"}},{q="Who rules the Undercity?",a="The city is ruled by Lady Sylvanas Windrunner, the Banshee Queen and leader of the Forsaken, from the royal quarters deep inside the complex.",al={"who is the leader of undercity","undercity leader","who rules undercity"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The Undercity is the beating heart of Forsaken civilization—a sanctuary built from the ruins and crypts of your former lives where you are sheltered from the Scourge and the living alike.",["faction:Horde"]="The subterranean city stands as the Horde's primary military bastion in the Eastern Kingdoms, though its dim, apothecary-tainted passages test the comfort of visitors from Kalimdor."},kw={"arthas","capital city","catacombs","crypts","doomhammer","forsaken","lordaeron","sylvanas","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:tirisfal","npc:sylvanas-windrunner","topic:forsaken","topic:arthas-menethil","npc:orgrim-doomhammer","subzone:sewers"},src={"Undercity"}}
E["subzone:venomweb-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Venomweb Vale",z="tirisfal",s="Venomweb Vale is a shadowed valley in eastern Tirisfal Glades, sitting just south of the Scarlet Monastery. Once a lush woodland teeming with game, the vale has devolved into a blighted nest overrun by aggressive, venomous arachnids. Unknown to most who pass through, it also holds an ancient legacy as the sacred meeting place of the Council of Tirisfal.",h="Venomweb Vale is a shadowed valley in eastern Tirisfal Glades, sitting just south of the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="A Blighted Refuge",b="Before the plague consumed Lordaeron, this valley was a peaceful retreat of lush grass and verdant trees, favored by local hunters tracking deer and rabbits. Today, rot and creeping gloom dominate the landscape. Giant, venomous spiders swarm among the trees and hollows, led by the monstrous arachnid Sri'skulk. The vale's northern edge borders the territory of the Scarlet Crusade, where darkhounds prowl near the fortified Scarlet Encampment under Lieutenant Sanders.",sp=0},{t="Legacy of the Council",b="Long before spiders infested the hollows, the vale served as the clandestine gathering ground for the ancient Council of Tirisfal. It was here that the very first Guardian of Tirisfal was empowered to battle demonic incursions. In a desperate and misguided attempt to secure their sanctuary against intruders, one council member bred and unleashed the deadly spiders that plague the basin today. An odd boulder of fool's gold—the result of a centuries-old transmutation mishap by the apprentice Falric—still marks the secluded spot where Guardian Aegwynn once convened with the Council.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there so many spiders in Venomweb Vale?",a="The spiders are not simply wild beasts or products of the Scourge plague. Centuries ago, a member of the secret Council of Tirisfal magically created and unleashed them in a mad attempt to defend their secluded meeting grounds from trespassers. They multiplied and overtook the valley.",al={"venomweb spiders origin","why so many spiders","who made the spiders"}},{q="What is the Council of Tirisfal's connection to this valley?",a="Venomweb Vale served as the traditional secret assembly site for the Council of Tirisfal. Within this quiet valley, elven and human magi gathered to bestow their collective might upon the realm's defenders, including empowering the very first Guardian of Tirisfal.",al={"council of tirisfal vale","guardian meeting place","council history venomweb"}},{q="Who rules the arachnids in the vale?",a="The spider brood is led by a massive, deadly arachnid known as Sri'skulk, who stalks the shadowed hollows beneath the valley's blighted canopy.",al={"spider boss venomweb","sri'skulk","spider leader tirisfal"}},{q="What is the story behind the fool's gold rock in the vale?",a="Centuries ago, an apprentice named Falric accidentally transformed a boulder into fool's gold during his studies. The strange landmark became the exact meeting point where the famed Guardian Aegwynn would gather with the Council of Tirisfal.",al={"fools gold rock","aegwynn meeting rock","falric gold rock"}}},ang={["class:Mage"]="For practitioners of the arcane, the vale is hallowed ground: it was the historic meeting site of the Council of Tirisfal, where Guardians of old—including Aegwynn—were chosen and empowered.",["race:Undead"]="Forsaken travelers traveling toward the Scarlet Monastery must navigate both the lethal toxins of Sri'skulk's brood and the watchful patrols of Lieutenant Sanders's Crusaders to the north."},kw={"aegwynn","council of tirisfal","falric","lieutenant sanders","scarlet encampment","sri'skulk","tirisfal glades","venomweb vale"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Venomweb Vale"}}
E["subzone:vestibule-of-the-silver-hand"] = {t="subzone",n="Vestibule of the Silver Hand",z="tirisfal",s="The Vestibule of the Silver Hand is a sunken, forgotten antechamber hidden beneath the waters of Tirisfal Glades. Positioned just beyond an ancient submerged passage, it serves as the grand entrance to the legendary Tomb of Tyr.",h="The Vestibule of the Silver Hand is a sunken, forgotten antechamber hidden beneath the waters of Tirisfal...",sec={{t="The Threshold to Tyr's Rest",b="Hidden deep beneath Tirisfal, this subterranean vestibule marks the true gateway into the resting place of the titan-forged keeper Tyr. Accessible only by braving deep submerged tunnels, the chamber stands sealed away from the surface world, shrouded in silence and protected by ancient warding mechanisms that have outlasted the rise and fall of mortal kingdoms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Vestibule of the Silver Hand?",a="It is an ancient entrance hall hidden beneath the waters of Tirisfal Glades, constructed directly before the inner chambers of the Tomb of Tyr.",al={"vestibule silver hand","what is this place","vestibule of tyr"}},{q="How do you reach this chamber?",a="Reaching the vestibule requires navigating a flooded underwater passage concealed far beneath the glades of Tirisfal.",al={"how to get here","vestibule entrance","reaching vestibule"}},{q="Why is it named after the Silver Hand?",a="The hall honors Keeper Tyr, the legendary titan-forged guardian known for his sacrificial silver hand, whose mythical battle gave Tirisfal its name.",al={"why silver hand","name origin","tyr silver hand"}},{q="What lies beyond the vestibule?",a="Beyond this antechamber lie the deeper vaults of the Tomb of Tyr, protected by ancient defensive systems.",al={"what is past here","where does it lead","inner tomb"}}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The imagery of the Silver Hand originates in this subterranean vault, honoring the legendary sacrifice of Keeper Tyr long before mortal paladin orders ever took up the symbol.",["race:Human"]="Early human tribes named Tirisfal in awe of Tyr's fall, though few living souls today suspect the titan-forged keeper's tomb rests sealed deep beneath the soil."},kw={"keeper tyr","silver hand","tirisfal glades","tomb of tyr","underwater passage","vestibule of the silver hand"},rel={"subzone:tomb-of-tyr","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Vestibule of the Silver Hand"}}
E["subzone:whispering-forest"] = {t="subzone",n="Whispering Forest",z="tirisfal",s="The Whispering Forest is a secluded, mountainous woodland nestled behind the steep cliffs west of Deathknell. Largely cut off from the rest of Tirisfal Glades, it harbors uncanny wildlife, a mysterious fairy circle, and deep-seated corruption sleeping far beneath the soil.",h="The Whispering Forest is a secluded, mountainous woodland nestled behind the steep cliffs west of Deathknell.",sec={{t="The Hidden Glen",b="Tucked away behind Northface Rock and Bandarion Keep, the Whispering Forest feels entirely alienated from the surrounding plague-touched kingdom. While it contains afflicted deer and roaming predators, it also features a tranquil lake and a strange ring of giant mushrooms. At regular intervals, ethereal Fey-Drunk Darters appear from the mist, gathering around the fairy circle in an eerie ritual of converging beams and song. Spectators from the surrounding wild gather in silence, observing a natural magic that seems to defy the Scourge-ruined land.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow Beneath the Woods",b="Despite its outward wonder, the forest is tainted by an ancient dread. Centuries ago, the high elves briefly attempted to settle in Tirisfal Glades before being driven away when the latent evil sleeping deep underground began driving them mad. Around the local lake, Vile Fin murlocs and the undead threshadon Blightsculler prowl the waters, while the ruined settlement of Shadowvale lies blighted by necromantic remnants. Even mad wanderers across Lordaeron mutter fearful warnings of the consuming darkness resting beneath Tirisfal's roots.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the Whispering Forest located?",a="The forest lies in the mountains of western Tirisfal Glades, positioned just west of Deathknell and south of Tyr's Fall. It is walled off by Northface Rock, the steep ridge upon which Bandarion Keep rests.",al={"whispering forest location","where is whispering forest","how to get to whispering forest"}},{q="What happens at the giant mushroom circle?",a="Several Fey-Drunk Darters manifest around the giant glowing mushrooms, converging over the mist to perform a singing ritual with focused beams of light. Nearby wildlife gathers peacefully to watch before the darters fade back into the ether.",al={"mushroom circle tirisfal","faerie dragon ring","fairy ring ritual"}},{q="Who watches over the forest?",a="The overlooking heights of Bandarion Keep are held by Tyr's Watch, an order of Forsaken paladins. Near the fairy circle itself, the spectral Knight of Mourning is bound by oath to wander the woods.",al={"who guards whispering forest","bandarion keep whispering forest"}},{q="Why did the high elves abandon this region long ago?",a="When the high elves originally landed on Lordaeron's shores, they attempted to build a settlement in Tirisfal. Within a few years, an unsettling presence buried deep underground began eroding their sanity, compelling them to abandon the glades and travel north.",al={"high elves tirisfal","why elves left tirisfal","madness beneath tirisfal"}},{q="What is Shadowvale?",a="Shadowvale is a ruined village situated southwest of the forest's lake. It is occupied by the Tarnished alongside mindless undead afflicted by a necromantic crystal fragment dating back to clashes involving the Undercity.",al={"shadowvale tirisfal","ruined village whispering forest"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The gathering of Fey-Drunk Darters and their ritualistic communion over the faerie ring stands out as one of the few vibrant pulses of natural magic remaining within blighted Lordaeron.",["race:Undead"]="Nestled just past Deathknell and overseen by Tyr's Watch at Bandarion Keep, the secluded woodland hides forgotten dangers that pose a silent threat right on the Undercity's doorstep."},kw={"bandarion keep","blightsculler","deathknell","faerie ring","fey-drunk darter","shadowvale","tirisfal","whispering forest"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:bandarion-keep","subzone:deathknell","subzone:tyr-s-fall","topic:lordaeron","topic:forsaken","npc:nat-pagle","topic:murloc"},src={"Whispering Forest"}}
E["subzone:whispering-shore"] = {t="subzone",n="Whispering Shore",z="tirisfal",s="The Whispering Shore is a somber stretch of coastline in western Tirisfal Glades, resting just north of the Solliden Farmstead. Once a tranquil and bountiful retreat for Lordaeron's fishermen, its cold waters have since been overrun by a violent tribe of murlocs.",h="The Whispering Shore is a somber stretch of coastline in western Tirisfal Glades, resting just north of the...",sec={{t="A Ruined Haven",b="Before the Third War swept across northern Lordaeron, the Whispering Shore was renowned among locals as a favored fishing haven, celebrated for its calm waters and plentiful catches. Today, the chilling spray of the Great Sea crashes against an empty coast stripped of its peaceful past. The waters have grown cold and dark, devoid of their former bounty, and any unfortunate traveler wandering down from the hills risks being ambushed by territorial coastal dwellers.",sp=0},{t="The Murloc Menace",b="The beach is now firmly claimed by a band of hostile murlocs who ruthlessly attack anyone approaching the surf. Led by a fierce chieftain named Muad, these aquatic scavengers guard the shallows and tidal flats aggressively, posing a constant danger to nearby roads and the nearby Solliden Farmstead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Whispering Shore located?",a="The Whispering Shore lies along the western coast of Tirisfal Glades, directly north of the Solliden Farmstead.",al={"whispering shore location","where is whispering shore","whispering shore map"}},{q="What used to be at the Whispering Shore before the Scourge?",a="In the days of the Kingdom of Lordaeron, the shore was a beloved and tranquil spot for local fishermen drawn to its rich coastal waters.",al={"whispering shore history","what was whispering shore used for","whispering shore past"}},{q="Who controls the Whispering Shore now?",a="A tribe of aggressive murlocs has taken over the coastline. They are led by a particularly vicious murloc chieftain named Muad, attacking anyone who strays near the water.",al={"who lives on whispering shore","whispering shore enemies","whispering shore mobs"}},{q="Can you still fish peacefully at the Whispering Shore?",a="The coastline is no longer the peaceful haven it once was. Its waters are cold and dark, having lost much of their former bounty, and hostile murlocs aggressively guard the shoreline.",al={"fishing at whispering shore","whispering shore fish"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken securing western Tirisfal Glades, the murloc infestation at Whispering Shore poses an unruly threat right along the perimeter of their holdings."},kw={"coast","fishing","muad","murloc","solliden farmstead","tirisfal glades","whispering shore"},rel={"zone:tirisfal","subzone:solliden-farmstead","topic:murloc"},src={"Whispering Shore"}}
E["zone:tirisfal"] = {t="zone",n="Tirisfal Glades",z="tirisfal",s="Tirisfal Glades is the haunting northern territory of Lordaeron, now serving as the heartland of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken. Beneath blighted skies and rotting boughs lie fallen manors, dormant crypts, and the vast underground capital of the Undercity. Surrounded by mindless Scourge and zealous Scarlet crusaders, it is a perilous realm where free-willed undead carve out their survival.",h="Tirisfal Glades is the haunting northern territory of Lordaeron, now serving as the heartland of Lady...",sec={{t="A Land in Twilight",b="Once the fertile cradle of humanity, Tirisfal Glades has withered beneath the curse of the Lich King's plague. The sun rarely penetrates the murky gloom, casting an eternal sickly pale over dying woods, neglected pumpkin patches, and cold coastal hills. While remnants of old farmsteads like the Agamand Mills and Balnir Farmstead remain, their former masters have largely been swept into mass graves or risen as restless dead. Despite the devastation, a dark resilience permeates the countryside, anchored by towns like Brill and the cloistered sanctuary of Deathknell, where freshly awakened Forsaken learn to endure their second life.",sp=0},{t="A War on Two Fronts",b="Though Lady Sylvanas claims dominion over the region from the subterranean Ruins of Lordaeron, the Forsaken remain embattled on all sides. Residual Scourge thralls still infest hollows, fields, and dilapidated crypts, entirely subservient to the frozen throne of Northrend. To the east, the fanatical Scarlet Crusade has made northern Tirisfal its primary bastion, operating out of the Scarlet Monastery. Zealously devoted to the extermination of every undead creature, living and unliving alike, their outposts and patrols wage constant guerrilla warfare against Forsaken scouts and civilian travelers.",sp=0},{t="Echoes of the Ancient Past",b="Long before human kingdoms crowned their first monarchs, the Glades bore an ancient legacy. In the ancient tongue of the vrykul, 'Tirisfal' translates to 'Tyr's Fall,' christened after the heroic titan keeper Tyr fought to the death against colossal cosmic horrors. In subsequent eras, high elven exiles briefly tried to settle these woods before shadowy energies deep beneath the earth began driving them mad, prompting their migration north. In later centuries, the secret mortal cabal known as the Council of Tirisfal chose these shadowed groves to empower solitary Guardians, shielding Azeroth from demonic intrusion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the sky green and the land rotting?",a="During the Third War, Prince Arthas and the Scourge unleashed the Plague of Undeath across the Kingdom of Lordaeron. The magical blight poisoned not only the populace, but the soil, trees, and water itself, leaving the glades in an eternal state of eerie, sickly decay.",al={"why is tirisfal blighted","what happened to tirisfal","why is tirisfal dying"}},{q="What is the difference between the Forsaken and the Scourge here?",a="The Forsaken are undead who broke free from the Lich King's telepathic domination after the Battle of Mount Hyjal, choosing to follow Lady Sylvanas Windrunner with their own free will. The Scourge roaming the farmsteads and ruins remain mindless slaves bound to the Lich King's commands.",al={"forsaken vs scourge","why are zombies attacking undead","are all undead evil"}},{q="Who are the red-armored soldiers attacking travelers?",a="They belong to the Scarlet Crusade, an uncompromising splinter order of former Silver Hand paladins and survivors. Convinced all undead are irredeemable abominations that must be purified by sword and fire, they execute both mindless thralls and free-willed Forsaken with fanatical hatred.",al={"scarlet crusade","red humans","monastery humans"}},{q="Where does the name Tirisfal come from?",a="The region is named in honor of the titan keeper Tyr. According to legend, Tyr fell in battle against eldritch horrors in this glade. In the ancient vrykul tongue, 'Tyr's Fall' evolved into the name 'Tirisfal,' and the keeper's silver hand became an emblem woven deeply into early human mythology.",al={"tirisfal meaning","tyrs fall","origin of tirisfal"}},{q="Where do newly awakened Forsaken begin their journey?",a="Newly awakened Forsaken emerge from the crypts of the Shadow Grave inside Deathknell, a cloistered town nestled in southwestern Tirisfal. There, administrators and executors evaluate whether the risen dead possess the sanity and loyalty required to serve the Dark Lady.",al={"undead starting zone","where is deathknell","forsaken starting area"}},{q="How do travelers leave Tirisfal for other continents?",a="A large goblin-operated zeppelin tower sits on the hillside south of Brill, right outside the Ruins of Lordaeron. These airships provide direct, regular transit across the seas to Orgrimmar in Kalimdor and Grom'gol Base Camp in Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"tirisfal zeppelins","how to get to orgrimmar","how to get to stranglethorn"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="This is your ancestral homeland twice over: the kingdom you built in life, and the precarious sanctuary you must defend in undeath under Lady Sylvanas.",["faction:Horde"]="Tirisfal is the Horde's vital bastion in the northern Eastern Kingdoms, anchoring diplomatic ties with the Forsaken while warding off human extremists and the Scourge.",["faction:Alliance"]="For the surviving nations of the Alliance, Tirisfal is a tragic monument to Lordaeron's fall, filled with the desecrated tombs of former brothers and sisters in faith.",["class:Priest"]="Historic holy grounds like Faol's Rest—the tomb of Archbishop Alonsus Faol, founder of the Silver Hand—lie here, warped by death and contested between zealots and Shadow priests."},kw={"agamand","balnir","brill","deathknell","forsaken","glades","lordaeron","scarlet crusade","sylvanas","tirisfal","tyr","undercity"},rel={"zone:undercity","zone:ruinsoflordaeron","zone:scarlet","zone:silverpine","zone:westernplaguelands","subzone:brill","subzone:deathknell","subzone:bulwark"},m={levels="1-10"},src={"Tirisfal Glades (Classic)","Tirisfal Glades"}}
